    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.1">
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.1">These are the mysteries given by Yehovah20 to Yeshua the Messiah, to show his servants what would soon happen. And He sent them by the hand of his messenger to his servant, John.   The Scriptures: Revelation21 of עשוהי Messiah, which Elohim gave Him to show His servants what has to take place with speed. And He signified it by sending His messenger to His servant Yoḥanan, ele, “these,” (3 ms, Yehovah l' yeshu, “to/ for/ ha' mashiach, “the messiah,” (n ms) secrets, mysteries,” appear,” (v. Nif’al, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Yeshua,” (prep, la’avadav, “to/ belonging to/ for she' yihyeh, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it will be,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) becherov, “soon,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms sholeach, “he/it sent,” (v. Pa’al/ Qal, qatal, past, otam, “them,” (DO (prep, n mp, 3mp la' avdo, “to/ for/ belonging to/ his servant,” (prep, n ye’annos, John, al’yadei, “by the hand of,” (idiom) whom, to, for, of, Note: transliterated him/it,” (rel part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.2">The witness is the Word of Yehovah and the testimony24 of Yeshua the Messiah and of what he saw.  The Scriptures: who bore witness to the Word of Elohim, and the witness of עשוהי Messiah – to all he saw.  Aramaic: who bore witness to the word of God, and to the testimony of Jesus the Messiah, as to all that he saw. Yehovah v' ha' eydut, “and/ ha' mashiach, “the messiah,” (n ms) mi' mah, “from/ of what,” (prep, inter testimony,” (n ms) testimony,” (n fs) she' re’eh, “that/ which/ who/ whom Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.3">Holy26 are the reader27 and the hearers of these prophecies and those establishing what is written.  The Scriptures: Blessed is he who reads and those who hear the words of this prophecy, and guard what is written in it, for the time is near.  Aramaic: Blessed is he that readeth, and they who hear the words of this prophecy, and keep the things that are written in it; for the time is near. qadosh, “holy, set apart, sanctified, hu, “he/it,” (pron, ha' qorei, "I/ you (ms)/ he/it crier, v' ha' shomayim, “and/ but/ so/ or zot, “these,” (pron, ha' neviot, "the u' me' kaymim, “and/ but/ so/ or we / you (mp)/ they, those (m) prophecies," (n fp) consecrated,” (adj proclaim, one who hearing,” (n mp, announces," (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, establishing,” (v. Pi'el, act part, mp) she'katuv, “that/ which/ who/ whom written,” (rel part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.4">John and the seven elders in Asia minor, grace, and peace to you from He who is, and was, and will be, and from the seven Spirits30 that are from His throne.  The Scriptures: Yoḥanan, to the seven assemblies31 that are in Asia: Favour to you and peace from Him who is and who was and who is coming, and from the seven Spirits that are before His throne,  Aramaic: John to the seven churches which are in Asia: Grace to you and quietude, from him who is, and who was, and who is to come, from the seven Spirits which are before his throne; ye’hannos, John, v' ha' shiv’a, “and/ zkenim,” elders,” b' asia,” in Asia,” chesed, “grace, v' shalom, “and/ but/ so/ or peace,” yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, kindness, charity,” seven,” (card num) Note: transliterated imachem, “with you (mp),” (prep, ma' ze,” of/ from this,” (prep pron, she' haya, “that/ v' hoveh, “and/ but/ so/ or who I/ you (ms)/ he/it is,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act v' yihyeh, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it u' m' ha’shiv’a, “and/ but/ so/ or ruchot, “spirits,” (n which/ who/ whom part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, seven,” (prep, card she’hemah, “that/ which/ who/ they, m'kiso, “from/ of (prep, n ms, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.5">And from Yeshua the Messiah, the faithful witness and the first One resurrected from the dead and the Messiah and Prince33 commanding on the earth, the One who loves us and washes34 our transgressions35 in His blood.  The Scriptures: and from עשוהי Messiah, the trustworthy witness, the first-born from the dead, and the ruler of the sovereigns of the earth. To Him who loved us and washed us from our sins in His own blood,  Aramaic: and from Jesus the Messiah, the Witness, the Faithful, the First-born of the dead, and the Prince of the kings of the earth; who hath loved us, and released us from our sins by his blood; u' mi’ yeshu, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of ha' mashiach, “the messiah,” (n ms) ne'eman, “faithful, v' rishon, “and/ but/ so/ or first,” she’kam, “that/ witness,” (n ms) loyal, devoted,” which/ who/ whom he/it rose, got up,” Yeshua,” (prep, dead(s),” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v' nagid, “and/ but/ so/ or the leader, prince, ruler,” (n v’metzova, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you ha’ahavatenu, “the I/ you (ms), he/it v’rochtzatenu, “I/ wash(es) us,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, iniquities,” (prep, commands,” (v. Pi’el, act part, ms) Pa'al/Qal, act part, im, “with,” (prep) damo, “his/its blood,” (n ms, 3ms pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.6">For he made us kings and priests38 before Yehovah, His Father. To Him be honor and glory forever and ever, amen.  The Scriptures: and has made us sovereigns and priests to His Elohim and Father, to Him be esteem and rule forever and ever. Amĕn.  Aramaic: and hath made us a kingdom sacerdotal to God and his Father: to whom be glory and power, for ever and ever. Amen. v’a’seh, “and/ but/ otanu, “us,” (DO l' melachim, “to/ for/ belonging to kings,” (prep, n Yehovah v' aviv, “and/ but/ so/ or he/ it did, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to priests,” (prep n before the face of, before me, in front Father,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) Pa'al/Qal, qatal, tihye, “it shall be,” chevod, “honor,” v’tiferet, “and/ but/ so/ or glory,” (n fs) me’olam, “from/ of forever,” (prep, v' ad, “and/ but/ so/ or eternity,” (n olam, “forever,” (n him/it,” (prep, 3ms yiqtol, fut, 3ms) “Amen,” (adv)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.7">See, He will come in a cloud40 and those who pierced him will see Him. And all the clans41 of the earth will weep.42  Yes, Amen!  The Scriptures: See, He is coming with the clouds, and every eye shall see Him, even they who pierced Him. And all the tribes of the earth shall mourn because of Him. Yes, Amĕn.  Aramaic: Behold, he cometh with clouds; and all eyes shall see him, and also they who speared him; and all the tribes of the earth shall mourn on account of him. Yes: Amen. re'e, “(to a man) hu, “he/it,” (3ms yavo,” he/it will b' anan, “in/ with/ by (the) cloud,” v' tir'u, “and/ but/ oto, “him/it,” (DO see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, so/ or you (mp) will see,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2mp, Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, oto, “him/it,” (DO va’yivku, “and/ kol, “all,” (n ms) ha' mishpachot, “the families, clans,” (n fp) ken, “yes, truth,” but/ so/ or they will weep, cry, mourn, those who pierced,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, pssv Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, “Amen” (adv)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.8">I am He who is the First and the Last,45 the beginning and the end, says the Almighty,46 the one who is, and who was, and who will be.  The Scriptures: “I am the ‘Aleph’ and the ‘Taw’, Beginning and End,” says הוהי “who is and who was and who is to come, the Almighty.”  Aramaic: I am Alpha, also Omega,47 saith the Lord God; who is, and was, and is to come, the omnipotent. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) hu, “he/it,” (3ms ha' rishon, “the first,” (n ms) v' ha' acharon, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) last”, (n ms) v' ha' sof, “and/ but/ so/ or the end,” (n amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, “beginning,” (n ms) ha’haya, “the/that v' hoveh, “and/ but/ so/ or who is,” (ms) v' yihyeh, “and/ Master, Lord,” (n great, powerful,” he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or he/it will be,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.9">I, John, was on the island called Patmos for the sake of the Word of Yehovah and the testimony48 of Yeshua the Messiah.  The Scriptures: I, Yoḥanan, both your brother and co-sharer in pressure, and in the reign and endurance of עשוהי Messiah, came to be on the island that is called Patmos for the Word of Elohim and for the witness of עשוהי Messiah.  Aramaic: I John, your brother, and partaker with you in the affliction and suffering that are in Jesus the Messiah, was in the island called Patmos, because of the word of God, and because of the testimony of Jesus the Messiah. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ye’annos, John, hayiti, “I was,” (v. b' i’, “in/ with/ by (the) island,” (prep, ha' nikra, “the I/ you (ms)/ he/it is called,” (v. Nif’al, “Patmos” (name) bishvil, “for, for the Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sake of,” (prep) Note: transliterated ha' dibur, “the speech,” (n ms) Yehovah v' ha' eydut, “and/ mi' yeshu, “of/ from Yeshu(a)” ha' mashiach, “the messiah,” (n ms) testimony,” (n fs) <note type="footnote" n="45">This is a direct quote from Isaiah 44:6, 48:12. See also Isaiah 41:4 and is a unique Hebrew marker. The “Alpha” and “Omega” are modifications in the Greek manuscripts. 46 Literally, “mighty Master.”  47 This verse is a translation from the Greek as Yehovah does not say He is the Alpha and Omega. Yehovah says that He is “the First and the Last,” as in Isaiah 44:6; 48:12 and see also Isaiah 41:4. 48 See Revelation 1:2 for more details on this word.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.10">And the Holy Spirit soaked51 over me, and I heard a great voice from behind me,  The Scriptures: I came to be in the Spirit on the Day of הוהי, and I heard behind me a loud voice, as of a trumpet,  Aramaic: I was in the Spirit on the Lord's day;52 and I heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet, which said: v’shora, “I/ you ali, “upon me, over,” (prep, 1cs ha' koesh, “the holy,” (adj, ms) v' shema'ati, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, m' acharei, “of/ from behind me,” (prep, pron 1cs) qol, “voice, sound,” (ms)/ he/it soaked, Pa'al/Qal, act part, gadol, “great,” (adj <note type="footnote" n="49">This spelling is found in Book of Tobit 7:7. 50 This spelling is found in Letter of Aristeas 266. 51 Jastrow and Klein indicate this word means “soaked” as used in the Talmud. However, it can also simply mean to “rest” or “dwell.” The successors to the high priesthood (Cohanim) were consecrated by profusely pouring oil over the Cohen Gadol’s (High Priest) heads, (see Leviticus 21:10-12; Exodus 29:7; Psalm 133:2). But for the remaining priest’s consecration it was the ritual blood that was applied to the ear, thumb, and big toe — but not oil (Exodus 29:20). However, the leper, on the day of his cleansing has a process to go through for cleansing, and the remaining oil… “he shall put on the head of him who is to be cleansed,” (Leviticus 14:25). Then after the application of the oil upon the ear, thumb, and toe of the restored leper, it was the applied in a more customary way of anointing the head of the restored leper as in the same manner the priests and kings were anointed (Leviticus 14:14-18).  52 The “Lord’s Day” is a translation from Greek and appears to be an addition. This verse is often used to argue that the first day of the week (i.e. Sunday) was changed to the first day of the week (i.e. Sunday). However, Yehovah does not change (Psalms 55:11, Malachi 3:6) and the seventh day of the week remains on the seventh day (i.e. Saturday). See Leviticus 23:3.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.11">then said, “I am the First and the Last53; and all that you see,54 write in a scroll, and send it to the Elders of Asia; and to Ephesus, and to Smyrna, and to Pergamos, and to Thyatira, and to Sardis, and to Philadelphia, and to Laodicea.  The Scriptures: saying, “I am the ‘Aleph’ and the ‘Taw’, the First and the Last,” and, “Write in a book what you see and send it to the seven assemblies of Asia – to Ephesos, and to Smurna, and to Pergamos, and to Thyatira, and to Sardis, and to Philadelphia, and to Laodikeia.”  Aramaic: That which thou seest, write in a book, and send to the seven churches, to Ephesus, and to Smyrna, and to Pergamos, and to Thyatira, and to Sardis, and to Philadelphia, and to Laodicea. v’ahmrah, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ha' rashon, “the v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) she' rayita, “that/ which/ who/ whom you (ms) saw,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, past, 2ms) “and/ but/ so/ or the said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, ktov! (to a man) ba' sefer, “in (the) v' schlach, “and/ but/ so/ or send! oto, “he/it,” (DO l' ha’ zekanim, “to/ for/ belonging to the elders,” (prep, b' ashia, “in Asia,” v’l’ ephesus, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ Pa’al/Qal, imp, document,” (prep, n Ephesus,” (name) v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” (part) le’ smyrnon, “to/ for/ belonging to Smyrna,” (prep, v' l' pergamos, and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” le' tyateyros, “to/ for/ belonging to Thyatira,” (prep, v' le' zardos, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or moreover, Pergomos,” (prep, l' filadelfia, “to/ for/ belonging to v' laoditzeon, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ Laodicea,” (prep, <note type="footnote" n="53">See verse the footnote in 1:8. 54 Literally, “you saw” (past).  55 See Revelation 1:4 for more details. 56 Second Temple Book of Maccabees II 3:3.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.12">And I turned to see the voice that spoke with me. So, when I turned, I saw seven menorahs57 of gold.  The Scriptures: And I turned to see the voice which spoke with me. And having turned, I saw seven golden lampstands,  Aramaic: And I turned myself to look at the voice that talked with me; and when I had turned, I saw seven candlesticks of gold; v’ hafachti, “and/ lir’ot, “to see,” (v. et, (DO marker) ha' kol, “the voice, ha’dovrot, “the I/ imi, “with me,” (prep, 1s pronom) v’kashhafachti,”an Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sheva, “seven,” shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zahav, “gold,” (n “menorahs,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.13">And in the midst of them was One in the likeness of man58 and dressed in white garments and girded upon the chest59 with a sash of gold.  The Scriptures: and in the midst of the seven lampstands One like the Son of Aḏam, dressed in a robe down to the feet and girded about the chest with a golden band.  Aramaic:  and, in the midst of the candlesticks, one like the Son of man, clothed to the feet, and girded about his paps with a girdle of gold. uv’nei’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or midst of, among them,” (prep, mp, 3mp echad,”one,” (card ba' dmut, “in/ with/ by (the) image of,” adam, “man,” (n v' lavush, “and/ b' ’chatonot, “in/ lavan, “white,” you(ms)/ he/it was garments, tunics,” v' chagor, “and/ ha’ chazeh, “the chest, breast,” (n shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zahav, “gold,” (n you(ms)/ he/it was girdle, sash, wrap, binding" (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.14">Indeed, his head and hair were white, as white as wool, and his eyes were as flames of fire.  The Scriptures: And His head and hair were white as white wool, as snow, and His eyes as a flame of fire,  Aramaic: And his head and his hair were white, like white wool, like snow; and his eyes, like a flame of fire: aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay v' se'aro, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its hair,” haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, lavan, “white,” k' zemer, “like/ as (the) wool,” (prep, lavan, “white,” head,” (n ms, 3ms v’einav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its eyes,” k' lahevet, “like/as a flame of,” (prep, eish, “fire,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.15">And his feet were like copper, and his voice was like the noise of mighty rushing waters.  The Scriptures: and His feet like burnished brass, as if refined in a furnace, and His voice as the sound of many waters.  Aramaic: and his feet were like fine brass, flaming in a furnace: and his voice, like the sound of many waters. v' raglav “and/ but/ so/ or his/its legs, feet,” (n mp, 3ms k' nekhoshet, “like/ v' qolo, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its voice, sound,” (n ms, 3ms k' ra'ash, “like/ as mayim, “waters,” gedolim, “mighty, many,” (adj mp) as (the) copper,” rushing, rattling, quaking, shaking,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.16">And seven stars were in his right hand, and from His mouth came a double-edged sword, and His appearance shined like the sun  The Scriptures: And in His right hand He held seven stars, and out of His mouth went a sharp two-edged sword, and His face was just as the sun shining in its strength.61  Aramaic: And he had in his right hand seven stars; and from his mouth issued a sharp twoedged sword; and his visage was like the sun shining in its strength. v' shiv’a, “and/ but/ so/ or seven,” (card kochavim, “stars,” b' yad, “in/ with/ by (the) hand,” (prep, yemino, “his/its right,” (n ms, 3ms u’m’piv “and/ but/ so/ or from his/its mouth,” (n ms, 3ms Idiom: “two-edged Pa'al/Qal, qatal, pipiyot, “edges, spikes,” (n fp) cherev, “sword,” (n umarehu, “and/ but/ k' shemesh, “just as, like/ as (the) sun,” (prep, n ms) so/ or I/ you(ms)/ his/its appear(s),” (v. Hi’fil, act part, Pa'al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.17">And when I saw Him, I fell, as if dead at His feet. And placing His right hand on me, He said, "Fear not. I am the First and the Last."62  The Scriptures: And when I saw Him, I fell at His feet as dead, and He placed His right hand on me, saying, “Do not be afraid, I am the First and the Last, v' k’she' raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or when I saw,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, oto, “him/it,” (DO nafalti, “I fell,” (v. l’raglav,” to/ for/ belonging to his/its feet,” (prep, n ms) v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ Pa'al/Qal, qatal, placed,” (v. Hif’il, (prep,v. Pa'al/Qal, et, (DO marker) yad, “hand,” (n fs) yemino, “his/its right,” (n ms, 3ms v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, al, “not,” (neg part) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) tira, “you (ms) will fear,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ha' rishon, “the first”, (n ms) “and/ but/ so/ or the yiqtol, fut, 2ms) <note type="footnote" n="61">Notice that “in its strength” is not in the Cochin manuscript but only matches the Greek and Aramaic. The Aramaic Revelation closely aligns with the Greek Revelation throughout Revelation. It has an appearance that the Aramaic may be a translation from Greek. 62 See the footnote in Revelation 1:8.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.18">“See I,63 I was dead, and now I live. I am eternal. And I have the keys to death and Gehinnom.”  The Scriptures: and the living One. And I became dead, and see, I am living forever and ever. Amĕn. And I possess the keys of She’ol and of Death  Aramaic: and who liveth and was dead; and behold, I am alive for ever and ever. Amen. And I have the keys of death and of the unseen world. v’re’eh, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a man) see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, ani, “I,” (pron 1cs) ani,hayiti,  “I was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, meit, “I/ you(ms)/ he/it is dead,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, v' achshav, “now,” chay, “I/ you (ms)/ he/ it live(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) m' olam, “from/ of eternity,” (prep, n v' li, “and/ but/ so/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” ha'mot, “the death,” v' ha’gehinnom, there exists,” (part) and/ but/ so/ or the Gehinnom, hell, or belonging to me,” Hinnom,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.19">“Write what you saw, and what follows,”  The Scriptures: “Write therefore what you have seen, both what is now and what shall take place after these:  Aramaic: Therefore, write what thou hast seen, and the things that are; and the things that are to be hereafter: ktov! (to a man) she' raita “that/ u' mah, “and/ but/ she’yihyeh, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it will be,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) Idiom: "after in this way" which/ who/ whom you (ms) saw,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 2 ms) Pa’al/Qal, imp, vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) kakh, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.1.20">“and the mystery of the seven stars that you saw in His right hand, and the seven menorahs of gold. For the seven stars are the seven messengers, and the seven menorahs are the seven elders.” v' hasod, “and/ but/ kochavim, “stars,” she’ raita, “that/ b' yad, “In/ with/ by his/its hand,” (prep, yemino, “his/its v' sheva, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) seven,” so/ or the secret, mystery,” (n ms) which/ who/ whom you saw,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, right,” (adj ms, 3ms seven,” (prep, card shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zahav, “gold,” (n kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this hu, “he/it,” (3ms, kochavim, “stars,” “menorahs,” (n mp) seven,” (card num) ele, “these,” (3ms, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, shiv’a, “seven,” v'ha'shiv’a, “and/ shiv’a, “seven,” “menorahs,” (n mp) messengers,” (n seven,” (card num) zkenim,” elders,”</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.2">
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.1">“Then write to the messenger of the congregation of Ephesus. ‘He who has the seven stars in His right hand and walks among the seven menorahs of gold, says,’”  The Scriptures: “To the messenger of the assembly of Ephesos write, ‘He who is holding the seven stars in His right hand, who is walking in the midst of the seven golden lampstands, says this:  Aramaic: To the angel of the church which is at Ephesus write: These things saith he who holdeth all things, and the seven stars, in his right hand; he that walketh in the midst of the seven candlesticks of gold; v’l’ ha’malach, m’ ha’eda, “from/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” Epheyzos (name) ketov! “(to a man) koh, “so, thus, to such extent,” (adv) amar, “he/it said),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to Pa’al/Qal, imp, assembly,” (prep, n transliteration of messenger,” (prep, ze, ”this,”  (pron, she’yesh, “that/ b’ yad, “in/ into/ y’mino, “in his/its right,” (prep n fs) ha’ shiv’a, “the kokavim, “stars,” ha’holekh, “the I/ which/ who/ whom seven,” (card num) hand,” (prep, n cs) Pa’al/Qal, act part, betokh, “inside, midst” (prep) shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zahav, “gold,” (n seven” (card num) “menorah,” (n fp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.2">“‘I know your works and hopes. You are not able to tolerate the wicked. You are testing those who say they are prophets,67 and finding they are liars.’” ani, “I,” (1cs pron) et, (DO marker) m’ asekha, “your v’ tiqotecha, “and your hopes,” (n fs, v’ et, “and/ but/ so/ or,” (DO marker) lo, “no/ not” (neg (ms) deeds, works,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, tukal, “you (ms) will be able,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, lisbol, “to suffer; to tolerate, to bear,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf et, (DO marker) ha’reshaim, “the v’ tenase,” and/ le’eylu, “to/ for/ ha’amorim, “the those who say,” (n but/ so/ or you (ms) will try,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, 2ms) belonging to these, wicked, villains, wrong,” (n mp) she’he’mah, “that/ which/ who/ they, ve’eynam, “and/ va’timatze, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it will she’he’mah, “that/ which/ who/ they, kozvanim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those lying,” (v. “prophets,” (n mp) but/ so/ or neither,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="67">Compare to Deuteronomy 13:1-5.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.3">“’So, your hopes and your troubles are all for the sake of My Name.’”  The Scriptures: and you have been bearing up and have endurance, and have laboured for My Name’s sake and have not become weary.  Aramaic: And thou hast had patience, and hast borne the burden, on account of my name, and hast not fainted. v’ tikvatecha, “and/ v’ tarakhte’cha, “and/ but/ so/ or ha’ kol, “the all,” (n bishvil, “for, for the but/ so/ or your there exists,” (part) sake of,” (prep) name,” (n ms, 1cs hopes,” (n fs, 2ms your trouble, pain,” <note type="footnote" n="68">The Greek and the Aramaic translations both reference works and labor whereas the Cochin says, “hopes.” See Psalms 131:3. 69  Second Temple spelling, first found in c. 135 CE, Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Amalek 2:42.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.4">“’ So, I am bewildered.  Why would you leave your first love?’”  The Scriptures: “But I hold this against you, that you have left your first love.  Aramaic: Yet I have [a charge] against thee, on account of thy former love, which thou hast left. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but temia, “astonished, bewildered”’ (adj fs Idiom: Because of what? ta’azov, “you (ms) atah, “you,” (2ms) belonging to me,” (prep, pron 1cs) mipnei, “from, of, away from, from contrariwise, nay Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, before, because,” (prep rishona, “first,” (adj</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.5">“‘Remember who you are and repent,74 and do your first works! But if not, your menorah will be quickly pushed from its place if you do not repent.’”75  The Scriptures: “So remember from where you have fallen, and repent and do the first works, or else I shall come to you speedily and remove your lampstand from its place, unless you repent.  Aramaic: Therefore remember whence thou hast fallen; and repent, and do the former works: or if not, I will come to thee quickly, and I will remove thy candlestick from its place, except thou repent. za’kor,” (to a man) atah, “you,” (2ms) Idiom: “and repent!” o’sey, “and/ but/ ma’asekha, “from/ of your (ms) deeds, remember!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, so/ or (to a woman) do!” (v. Pa’all/Qal, ve’o’sey, “and/ but/ so/ or those doing,” works,” (prep, n mp, 2ms pronom) teshuva, “repentance,” (n fs) rishonim, “first,” u’vim, “and/ but/ so/ or by if, when, whether,” (prep, lo, “no/not” (neg yidchof, “he/it will menoratcha, “your (ms) menorah, “(n mp) 2ms pronom) m’mi’qomo, “from/ of his/its location,” (prep, n ms, 3ms “quickly, speedily, be pushed,” (v. Nif’al, yiqtol, fut, ba’im, “by/ with/ in if, when, whether,” she’lo, that/ which/ who/ whom no/not, (rel part, neg part) Idiom: “repent” ta’aseh, “you shall make, do,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, Yiqtol, fut, 2ms) tshuvah, “repentance,” (n fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.6"/>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.7">“’Whoever has ears, hears what the Spirit says to the congregation: Whoever prevails will eat from the Tree of Life,79 which is in the Garden of Eden.’”80  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. To him who overcomes I shall give to eat from the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim.”  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. To him who is victorious, will I give to eat of the tree of life which is in the paradise of my God. she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznayim, “ears,” (n shomea “I/ you she’ha’ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, act the Spirit, wind, exists,” (rel part, breath,” (rel part, n omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l’ha’edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the she’menatzach, yochal, “he/it will eat,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, m’etz ha’hayim, “from/of the Tree of Life.” (prep, n he/it say(s),” (v. “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it prevails,” (rel Pa’al/Qal, act part, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) assembly,” (prep n part, v. Pi'el, act she’yesh, “that/ be’ gam, “in/ with/ “Eden,” (name) which/ who/ whom by the garden,” exists,” (rel part, <note type="footnote" n="77">Nicolaitans are mentioned in Revelation 2:14. 78 The Cochin verse numbers are inserted to demonstrate that the numbering of the verses is different in the Cochin than that of the KJV. 79 This exact phrase in Hebrew is used in Genesis 3:22, where it is commonly translated as "Tree of Life;" however, "life" is plural, so it is literally, "the tree of lives" or "the living tree." This phrase is also found in Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 18:11, The Midrash of Philo 3:22:7. 80 Joel 2: 1-2 describes a people in the day of Yehovah, a future day of great judgement as “a fire has consumed and behind them a fire burns” as they pursue the Garden of Eden. For in that day (the judgement day of Yehovah), a mighty people will arise, a great army of Yehovah, “…a people many and strong, the like of whom has never been, nor shall there ever be again after them, to the years of many generations.” This mighty army appears to be the servants of Yehovah who will do mighty deeds. Yehovah expects highly of His servants to repent and serve Yehovah in the greatest time and place in the history of the children of Israel.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.8">“Then write to the messenger of the congregation of Smyrna, ‘Thus says the First and the Last of the dead and is risen.’”  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Smurna write, ‘This says the First and the Last, who became dead, and came to life:  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church which is at Smyrna, write: These things saith the First and the Last, he who was dead, and liveth. v' ‘l’ malach, and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the ma’ha’eda, “of/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” ktov!, “(to a man) ko, “so, thus, to amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, past, “Smyrna” (name) such extent,” (adv) Pa’al/Qal, imp, angel, messenger,” assembly,” (prep n transliteration of ha' rashon, “the v' ha' acharon, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) last,” (n ms) ha’mat, “the dead,” v' kam, “and/ but/ so/ or I/you (ms)/ he/it is, risen,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part <note type="footnote" n="81">This spelling is found in Tractate Kallah Rabbati 5:1 as early as c.100 BCE. 82 The gershayim (two slash marks above the word) is to indicate that this is an abbreviation of a name. This does not affect the translation.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.9">“I know your works and sorrows, and the blasphemy of those who say they are Jews but are not.  They are the children of Satan.”  The Scriptures: “I know your works, and pressure, and poverty – yet you are rich – and the blasphemy of those who say they are Yehuḏim and are not, but are a congregation of Satan.  Aramaic: I know thy works, and the affliction, and the poverty, (yet thou art rich;) and the railing which is from them who say they are Jews, and they are not, but are of the congregation of Satan. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ma’asecha, “your (ms) deeds, works,” “and/ but/ so/ or your sorrows,” (n mp, 2mp/2ms “and/ but/ so/ or the blasphemy,” (n ms) m’alv, “from/ of ha’om’rim, “the those who say,” (n (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act these,” (prep, pron) she' hem, “that/ ve’einam, “and/ rak, “only, just,” he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, m’ benei, “from/ or which/ who/ whom “Judeans,” (n mp) but/ so/ or they (m) are not,” (pronom, they,” (rel part, sons,” (prep, n mp adversary,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.10">Translation #1: “Do not fear them. See, Satan will possess them in order to test you. And the sorrow will last for ten days. Be faithful until your death is set in motion, so that I may give to you the crown of life.”86  Translation #2: “Do not fear them. See, Satan will take some among the captives87 in order to test you. And the sorrow will last for ten days. May you be faithful until your death, so that I may give to you the crown of life.”  The Scriptures: “Do not be afraid of what you are about to suffer. See, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison, in order to try you, and you shall have pressure ten days. Be trustworthy until death, and I shall give you the crown of life.  Aramaic: Be not terrified at any of the things thou art to suffer. For lo, the Accuser will throw some of you into custody, that ye may be tried; and there will be trouble to you ten days. Be faithful unto death, and I will give thee the crown of life. al, “not,” (neg part) tira, “you (ms) will fear,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, mehem, “of/ from them,” (prep, 3mp) re'e, “(to a man) yikach, “he/it will take,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, some, certain, any,” adversary,” (n ms) yiqtol, fut, 2ms) yiqtol, fut, 3ms) mehem, “of/ from them,” (prep 3mp) k’dei, “be able, le’nasot, “to test, prove,” (v. Pi’el, et’chem, “with/ in you (mp),” (prep, ve’ha’tza’ar, “and/ yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “in/ with/ by (the) captives,” (prep, n according to, as, in but/ so/ or the sorrow,” (n ms) order to,” (conj) lachem, “to/ for/ belonging to you,” asara. “ten” (card yamim, “days,” (n te’hi, “let there be,” ne'eman, “I/ you ad, “until,” (prep) yom, “the day,” (n (v. Pa’al/Qal, jus faithful,” (v. Nif’al, motcha, “of/ from your death,” (prep n ms, 2ms pronom) k’dei, “be able, she’eten, “that/ keter, “the crown,” ma’chayim, “from/ of the life,” (prep n according to, as, in which/ who/ whom belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) order to,” (conj) I will give,” (v Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.11">“Whoever has ears, hears88 what the Spirit is speaking to the congregation:  and whoever that prevails will not have the anguish of another death.”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. He who overcomes shall by no means be harmed by the second death.”’  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. He that is victorious, shall not be harmed by the second death. she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznayim, “ears,” (n shomea, “I/ you she’ha’ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, act the Spirit,” (rel exists,” (rel part, omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l’ha’edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the she’menasteach,  “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s),” al, “not,” (neg adv) thihye, “you (ms) he/it say(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, him/it,” (prep, 3ms assembly,” (prep n (rel part, v. Pi'el, tza’ar, “sadness, sorrow, regret, remorse,” (n ms) me’mot, “from/ of the death,” (prep, n achheret, “other, another, different,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.12">“Write to the messenger of the congregation of Pergamum: ‘Thus, says the One who has the double-edged sword,’”89  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Pergamos write, ‘He who has the sharp two-edged sword, says this:  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church at Pergamos, write: Thus saith he who hath the sharp two-edged sword; 88 “Ears to hear” is first found in Deuteronomy 29:4. 89 The Hebrew idiom “two-edged sword” is first found in Psalms 149:6. Pergamum90 ktov! “(to a man) v‘l’hamalach, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the angel, messenger” me’ha’eda, “of/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” ko, “so, thus, to amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal such extent,” (adv) Pa’al/Qal, imp, ze, “this” (pron, she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom Idiom: “two-edged sword” him/it,” (prep, 3ms kherev, “sword, sabre, saber,” (n fs) exists,” (rel part, piyfot, “a two edged,” (n cp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.13">“’I know your works and your place. You are in the place of the throne of Satan. Believe in My Name,91 and my faithfulness, and my timing. He killed my faithful friend, Antipas, who walked with you in the place where Satan dwells.’”  The Scriptures: “I know your works, and where you dwell, where the throne of Satan is. And you hold fast to My Name, and did not deny the belief in Me, even in the days in which Antipas was My trustworthy witness, who was killed near you, where Satan dwells.  Aramaic: I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, [even] where the throne of Satan is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied the faith of me, in those days when my faithful witness, who was slain among you, was made a spectacle where Satan dwelleth. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) yodea, “I/ you eth, (DO marker) ma’asecha, “your (ms) deeds, works,” u’makom, “and/ shelcha, “to, for, of, belonging to you,” (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act but/ so/ or a place,” there exists,” (part) she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom kise, “throne,” (n ve’ata, “and/ but/ ta’amin, “you (ms) will believe,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut be’she’mi,”‘in/ so you,” (pron 2ms) with/ by my name,” place,” (prep, n ms) adversary,” (n ms) (prep, n ms, 1cs exists,” (rel part, u’beemunati, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by my faith, creed, u’be’iti, “and/ but/ so/ or in my time,” (n fs, 1cs pronom) eth, (DO marker) chaveri, “my ha’ne’eman, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is “Antipas,” (name) friend,” (n ms, 1cs Pa’al/Qal, qatal, transliteration of faithfulness,” (prep, n ms, 1cs promon) Nif’al, act part, ms) etzlechem, “with you,” (prep pron be’makom, “in/ with/ by (the) “that/ which/ who/ whom the satan, adversary,” (rel dar, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it dwell(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, place” (prep, n ms) <note type="footnote" n="90">Pergamum is an older spelling of Pergamos that is a city near the Aegean Sea near the ancient city of Smyrna. 91 Compare to Joel 2:32, Psalms 91:14-16, 99:6 and Exodus 34:6-7 when Yehovah called out His own Name before revealing His glory to Moses. The power of deliverance, healing and the revealing of Yehovah’s glory is through calling out His Name.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.14">“‘And you also hate those among you who are students of the teachings of Balaam, who guided the way of Balak to do evil to the children of Israel, causing them to sin by whoredom.’”94  The Scriptures: “But I hold a few matters against you, because you have there those who adhere to the teaching of Bil‛am, who taught Balaq to put a stumbling-block before the children of Yisra’ĕl, to eat food offered to idols, and to commit whoring.  Aramaic: Yet I have a small [charge] against thee. Thou hast there them who hold the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balak to throw a stumbling-block before the children of Israel, that they might eat the sacrifices of idols, and might commit whoredom. ve’ gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” atah, “you,” (2ms sone, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it hate(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, me’eilu, “from/ of these, those,” (prep she’lomidim, “that/ which/ who/ whom learn, study,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, be’limud, “with/ by shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” learning, studies, teaching,” (prep, n “Balak,” (name) la’asot, “to do, l’benei, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) sons, children of,” “Israel,” (name) al’yadei, “by the hand of,” (idiom) make, create,” (v. wickedness,” (n lachato, “to sin,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) be’z’nut, “in/ with/ fornication,” (prep, <note type="footnote" n="92">See Tractate Kallah Rabbati 3:13. 93 This spelling is in Letter of Aristeas 38. 94 Balaam advised the Moabites how to entice the children of Israel with prostitutes and idolatry. He could not curse Israel directly, so he devised a plan for Israel to bring a curse upon themselves. Balak followed Balaam’s advice, and Israel fell into sin, worshiping Baal of Peor and committing fornication with Midianite women. And in Numbers 31:16, the Midianite women were kept alive when Moses sent one thousand from each tribe to battle with the Midianites and all the Midianite women who had laid with a man was ordered to be killed.  See Numbers chapter 22, 23, and 31:16; Deuteronomy 23:4-5; Joshua 13:22 for more details. Also consider that “stubbornness” is described as “idolatry” and “rebellion” as “witchcraft,” in 1 Samuel 15:23.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.15">“’But also, you hate the teachings of the Nicolaitans, which also I hate of these.’”  The Scriptures: “So you also have those who adhere to the teaching of the Nikolaites, which teaching I hate.  Aramaic: So also thou hast them who hold the doctrine of the Nicolaitans. In like manner, repent thou. ve’ gam, “and/ but/ so again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” (part) atah, “you,” (2ms) me’limud, “from/ of (the) studies, “Nikalatetzian,” ve’af, “and/ but/ so/ or also, yea, though, so much the more,” (conj) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) (ms)/ he/it hate(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act learnings, class,” Note: transliteration me’eilu, “from/ of these, those,” (prep (ms)/ he/it hate(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act <note type="footnote" n="95">Spelling is as early as c. 100 CE in Sefer HaKanna 105:4. 96 See Revelation 2:14 for more details. 97 This word is traditionally transliterated as Nicolaitans…it is probably from (1) the noun νικη (nike), victory, and (2) the noun λαος (laos), [common] people – source Abarim Publications. The work and the doctrine of the Nicolaitans, consisted of hierarchizing the church, destroying the horizontal framework, to raise a pyramidal order. See website for more details: https://alsina-sa.com/sobre-religion/cual-es-la-doctrina-de-la-iglesia-filadelfia.html.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.16">“Repent!99  But if you do not, I will come swiftly to make war with you, by the sword in my mouth.”  The Scriptures: “Repent, or else I shall come to you speedily and fight against them with the sword of My mouth.  Aramaic: Or if not, I will come to thee quickly, and I will war upon them with the sword of my mouth. Idiom: “repent!” v’im, “and/ but/ or if/ whether,” (conj) lo, “no/not,” (neg ava, “I will come,” ani, “I,” (1cs pron) (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) “quickly, speedily, asi, “do!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, 2fs) tshuva, “repentance,” (n fs) la'asot, “to do, to imcha, “with you (ms),” (prep, 2ms mil’cha’ma, “war, she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom be’pi, “in/ with/ by my mouth,” (prep, n ms, 1cs pronom) al’yadei, “by the hand of,” (idiom) dagger, the sword,” exists,” (rel part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.17">“’Whoever has ears, hear whatever the Spirit says to the congregation:  Whoever prevails, I want to give him the hidden manna to eat;102 but also, good testimonies of him  ̶  and in the testimonies, a new name written so that not anyone can read except he who receives it.’”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. To him who overcomes I shall give some of the hidden manna to eat. And I shall give him a white stone, and on the stone a renewed Name written which no one knows except him who receives it.”’  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. To him that is victorious, will I give to eat of the hidden manna; and I will give him a white counter, and upon the counter a new name written, which no one knoweth but he that receiveth it. she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznayim, “ears,” (n shomea, “I/ you she’ha’ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom the spirit/ wind,” (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, act exists,” (rel part, omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l’ha’edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the she’menatzeach, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s), (rel part, v. Pi’el, rotzeh, “I/ you (ms) he/ it want(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) he/it say(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, assembly,” (prep, n le’echol, “to eat,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf) m’ ha’ man, “from/ ha’nistar, “hidden, concealed,” (adj ve’ gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” edut, “testimonies,” pleasant,” (adj fs) him/it,” (prep, 3ms u’va’zeh, “and/ but/ shem, “name,” (n chedash, “new, new katuv, “written,” yuchal, “he/it will testimonies,” (n fs) thing,” (adj ms) which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, sum, “any,” (in a neg sentence) 104 echad, “one,” (card likro, “to read,” (v. rak, “only, just,” ze, “this,” (pron, she’kibel, “that/ oto, “him/it,” (DO which/ who/ whom he/it received,” (rel part, v. Pi'el, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="98">This is a Second Temple word first used in the Book of Jubilees 31:36 dating from c. 460 BCE to 140 CE.  99 Literally, “do repentance.” Also see footnotes on Revelation 2:7 regarding the end of day servants of Yehovah. 100 Notice the added pronoun. This is common in this manuscript where pronouns are added when not necessary. 101 See Revelation 2:5 for more details.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.18">“And to the messenger of the congregation of Thyatira write, ‘Thus says the Son of Yehovah, whose eyes are as flames of fire, his legs, copper,’”  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Thyatira write, ‘This says the Son of Elohim, who has eyes like a flame of fire, and His feet like burnished brass:  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church at Thyatira, write: These things saith the Son of God, who hath his eyes like a flame of fire, and his feet like fine brass: ve’le’malach, “and/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” “Thyatiera” (name) ktov!, “(to a man) ko, “so, thus, to amar, “he/it said,” (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or to/ for such extent,” (adv) transliteration of Pa’al/Qal, imp, messenger,” (prep, assembly,” (prep, n ben, “son,” (n ms) Yehovah she’einav, “that/ he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, lechavat, “flame of…” (n fs constr) eish, “fire, flame,” which/ who/ whom similarly to, such his/its eyes,” (rel part, n fs, pronom 3ms) ve’ raglav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its legs, feet,” (n fp, “copper,” (n fs) <note type="footnote" n="104">In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.19">“’I know your works - your love, your service, your faith, your hope - in all seasons, doing more.’”  The Scriptures: “I know your works, and love, and service, and belief, and your endurance. And as for your works, the last are more than the first.  Aramaic: I know thy works, and love, and faith, and service, and also thy patience; and that these thy latter works are more than the former. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) eth, (DO marker) ma’asecha, “from/ of your (ms) deeds, ve’ahavatcha, “and/ v' shereticha, “and/ ve’emunatecha, “and/ but/ so/ or your faith,” (n ms, 2ms/2mp pronom) (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act but/ so/ or your but/ so/ or your works,” (prep, n mp, 2ms pronom) assistance,” (n ms, ve’tikvatecha, “and/ but/ so/ or your hope,” (n ms, u’vechol, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by (the) all,” (prep, n et, “time,” (n fs) na'ase, “I/ you yoter, “more, more become(s),” (v. NIf'al, act part, ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.20">“But I have a small matter - You must abandon the woman Jezebel who says she is a prophetess but teaches and inflames to cause my servants to commit whoredom.”  The Scriptures: “But I hold against you that you allow that woman Izeḇel, who calls herself a prophetess, to teach and lead My servants astray to commit whoring and to eat food offered to idols.  Aramaic: But I have [a charge] against thee, because thou sufferest thy woman Jezabel, who saith she is a prophetess, and teacheth, and seduceth my servants to whoredom, and to eating of the sacrifices of idols. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay katan, “small,” (adj aleicha, “on, upon, she' ta'azov, “that/ which/ who/ whom you will abandon,” thing, matter,” (n there exists,” (part) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) regarding, on you (ms),” (prep, 2ms Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, ha' ishah, “the woman,” (n fs) yezabel, “Jezebel,” ha' omerot,” I/ you (fs)/ she/it say(s),” (Pa’al/Qal, act part, v' lomdim, “and/ u' mesitim,”and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (ms)/ they incite,” (Hif'il, act part, mp) which/ who/ whom “prophetess,” (n fs) she/it,” (rel part, Pa’al/Qal act part, Note: Spelling is: eth, (DO marker) avdei, “my la’asot, “to cause to do something, to force,” (Pa’al/Qal, servants,” (n mp, “prostitutions, vice, fornication,” (n fs) <note type="footnote" n="105">Compare to Ibn Ezra on Genesis 25:24:1.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.21"/>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.22">“’See I, I bring great sorrow upon her and those who lay106 with her, if they do not repent of their works.’”  The Scriptures: “See, I am throwing her into a sickbed, and those who commit adultery with her into great affliction, unless they repent of their works.  Aramaic: Behold, I will cast her upon a bed, and them who commit adultery with her into great affliction, unless they repent of their deeds. re'e, “(to a man) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) mevi, “I/ you (ms)/ aleha, “upon her,” v'al,”and/ but/ so/ or on, upon,” (prep) ze, “this (pron, ms) she’shokev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it lays,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, (prep pron 3fs) (Pa’al, act part ms) imah, “with her,” (prep, pron 3fs) harbeh, “many, tza'ar, “sadness, regret, remorse, suffering,” (n ms) b'im, “in/ with/ by if, when, whether,” Idiom: “repent” much, a lot,” (adv) which/ who/ whom no/ not,” (rel part, ta'asu, “you (mp) will do,” (Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2mp) tshuvah, “repentance,” (n fs) ma'aseychem, “their deeds, works,” (n mp, 3mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="106">Literally, “lays with her.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.21">‘” For I gave her time to repent.’”107  The Scriptures: “And I gave her time to repent of her whoring, and she did not repent.  Aramaic: And I gave her a season for repentance, and she is not disposed to repent of her whoredom. v' ani, “and/ so, but/ or I,” (1cs natati, “I gave,” (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, “time,” (n fs) Idiom: “repent! (prep, 3fs pronom) asot, “to/ for/ belonging to cause to do,” (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, inf constr) tshuvah,” answer, reply; solution (to a problem), repentance,” (n fs) <note type="footnote" n="107">Literally, “to do repentance.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.23">“’And her children will be put to death: And all the congregation will know it is I who is the tester the innermost parts.108  And everyone will be paid according to his measure.’”  The Scriptures: “And I shall slay her children with death. And all the assemblies shall know that I am the One searching the kidneys and hearts. And I shall give to each one of you according to your works.  Aramaic: And her children will I slay with death: and all the churches shall know, that I am he who searcheth reins and hearts; and I will render to each of you according to your works. v’et, “and/ but/ so/ or,” (DO marker) baneha, “her/its yumtu, “they will be killed, put to death,” (v. Hif’il, pssv, yiqtol, fut, v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) takiru, “you (mp) will know,” (v. Hif'il, yiqtol, fut, sons, children,” (n mp, 3fs pronom) congregation,” (n which/ who/ whom I,” (rel part, 1cs hu, “he/it,” (pron) ha' bochen, “the tester, examiner, prober, examiner,” klay'ot, “kidneys, reins, the mind, innermost parts, seat of affection v' lav, “and/ but/ so or heart, courage, sense, mind,” (n v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card kfi, “according to,” and thought,” (n fp) midotav, “his/its yeshulam, “he/it will be paid,” (v. Pi'el, pssv, fut, him/it,” (prep, 3ms attributes,” (n mp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.24">“’However, to you and others in Thyatira, I say that I will not bring more sorrow upon you because you do not learn the teachings of Satan.’” aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay lachem, “to/ for/ belonging to you (mp),” (prep 2mp) ve’ le’acherim, ha’ he’mah, “the omer, “I/ you (ms)/ ani, “I,” (1cs pron) “and/ but/ so/ or to/ these, those,” (3mp, with/ by Tyatiera,” he/it say(s),” (v for/ belonging to others,” (prep, adj Pa’al/Qal, act part, transliteration of avi, “I will bring,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, aleichem, “on you (mp),” (prep, 2mp tza’ar, “sadness, kivan, “because, as which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, regret, remorse,” (n soon as, since,” which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, kivan, “directly, exactly,” (adv) tilmedu, “you (mp) m’limud, “from/ of teachings,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, adversary,” (n ms) <note type="footnote" n="108">Literally, “the kidneys and the heart,” which is a Hebrew idiom for a person’s (nefesh) meaning, “soul”.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.25">“’However, be strong in what you have, until I come.’”109  The Scriptures: “But hold fast what you have until I come.  Aramaic: but, what ye have, hold fast until I come. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay techezku, “you b’ze, ‘in/ with/ by (the) this,” (prep, she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom lachem, “to/ for/ belonging to you,” which/ who/ whom I will come,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) strong,” (v. Pi’el, exists,” (rel part, “’But to him that prevails, I will give the nations for his inheritance!’”110  The Scriptures: “And he who overcomes, and guards My works until the end, to him I shall give authority over the nations,  Aramaic: And to him that is victorious, and to him that observeth my works unto the end, to him will I give authority, over the nations; u'mi, “and/ but/ so/ she’menateach, etne, “I will give goyim, “nations,” nachalato, “his/its inheritance,” (n fs, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s),” (rel part, v. Pi’el, (of),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “’And He leads them with a rod of iron, as an instrument111 that shatters them into pieces.’”112 v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ yinhag, “he will drive, lead,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) b' shevet, “in/ with/ v' k'kli,”and/ but/ so/ or like/as an instrument, tool, vessel,” (prep, n yotzer, “I/you (ms)/ by (the) rod of, staff, branch, scepter,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, tanafttzem, “you will shatter, them into pieces,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, “‘As I have received from my Father, so I will give to him the dawn.’”114  The Scriptures: as I also have received from My Father.  Aramaic: I also have received of my Father. v'cmo, “and/ but/ she' kibalti, “that/ which/ who/ whom m' avi,” from/ of kakh, “so, thus, therefore, in this eten, “I will give,” ha’ shachar, “the sunrise, dawn,” (n my father,” (prep, n (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) similarly,” (prep) I received,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) ms, 1cs pronom) him/it,” (prep, 3ms <note type="footnote" n="110">Verse 26 is likely a paraphrase of Psalm 2:7-8, because verse 27 alludes to Psalm 2:9. 111 See Psalms 2:9, Jewish Publication Society (JPS). This phrase is also used in Revelation 12:5, and 19:15. 112 See Daniel 2:44, “And in the days of these kings shall the God of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand forever.”</note> <note type="footnote" n="113">See 1 Samuel 17:40b, Jewish Publication Society (JPS). 114 “The dawn” or “the sunrise.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.28"/>
      <verse osisID="Rev.2.29">“’Whoever has ears, hears what the Spirit says to the congregation.’”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies.”’  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. mi,” ‘who?” (inter she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznayim, “ears,” (n shomea, “I/ you she’ha’ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom the spirit/ wind,” (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, act exists,” (rel part, omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l’ha’edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the he/it say(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, assembly,” (prep, n</verse>
