    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.3">
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.1">“Write to the messenger of the congregation of Sardis: ‘Thus says the one who has the Spirits of Yehovah115 and the seven stars: I know your works because you have a name116 that lives, yet you are dead.’”  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Sardis write, ‘He who has the seven Spirits of Elohim and the seven stars, says this, “I know your works, that you have a name that you are alive, but you are dead.  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church which is at Sardis, write: These things saith he who hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars: I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and thou art dead. v’l’ ha’mal’ach, shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zardin, “Sardis” ktov! “write!” (v. ko, “so, thus, to amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ such extent,” (adv) for/ belonging to assembly,” (prep, n messenger” (prep, ze, “this,” (pron, she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom ha' ruchot, “the spirits,” (n cp) Yehovah v' ha' shiv’a, “and/ kochavim, “stars,” him/it,” (prep, 3ms seven,” (card num) exists,” (rel part, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) et, (DO marker) ma'asecha, “from/ shem, “name,” (n (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act there exists, (part) (prep, n mp, 2ms she' atah, “that/ which/ who you,” chay, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it live(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve'atah, “and/ but/ so you,” (pron 2ms) mat, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it die(s),” (v. belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="115">See Revelation 1:4 for more details on the seven Spirits of Yehovah. 116 The word,  םש (shem) means “name” or can mean “reputation.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.2">“’Therefore, do not sleep, but be strong for those who want to die, because I did not find your works before Yehovah completed.’”  The Scriptures: “Wake up, and strengthen what remains and is about to die, for I have not found your works complete before Elohim.  Aramaic: Awake, and preserve the things that remain, which are ready to die; for I have not found thy works complete before my God. lachen, “therefore, al, “not, don’t’ (neg tishan, “you (ms) v' t'che'zek, “and/ but/ so/ or you will she' rotzeh, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it wants,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, lamut, “to die,” (v. will sleep,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, belonging to this,” (prep, pron, ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, lo, “no/not,” (neg matzati,” I found,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, (DO marker) ma'asecha, “from/ of your (ms) deeds, schlma, “I/ you (ms) /he/it is over, before the face of, before me, in front works,” (prep, n mp, 2ms pronom) Pa’al/Qal, act part, Yehovah</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.3">“‘And now remember how you received and heard and establish them. So, repent!117  But if not, I will come upon you unexpectedly,118 and you do not know which hour I come.’” v’achshav,”and/ but/ so/ or now,” zakor,''(to a man) remember!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp, she’ kibalta, “that/ which who/ whom you (ms) received,” v' shumatah, “and/ but/ so/ or you (ms) u' mekayem, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) (rel part, v. Pi'el, qatal, past, 2ms) Pa'al/Qal, qatal, confirm(s),” (v. Pi'el, act part, ms) Idiom: “Repent!” v'im, “and/ but/ so/ lo, “not,” (neg adv), avo, “I will come,” ani, “I,” (1cs pron) aleicha, “to you, on, upon; over; about, regarding you,” (prep, 2ms or if, whether,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) v'asi! “and/ but/ so/ or (to a woman) do!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp, 2ms) Aramaic), Jastrow tshuva, “repentance,” (n fs) v'atah, “and/ but/ so/ or you,” (pron eina, “that/ which/ b' eizeh, “in/ with/ “unexpectedly” season, a set time, appointed time,” (n which/ who/ whom I will come,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) nothing, not, non-existence,” (prep, which, some, any” k' ganav, “as/ like a thief,” (prep, n ms) Pa'al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="117">Literally, “you (feminine singular) make repentance!” Also see footnotes on Revelation 2:7 regarding the end of day servants of Yehovah. 118 “As a thief” is an idiom meaning “unexpectedly,” as in 1 Thessalonians 5:2, 2 Peter 3:10.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.4">“Furthermore, your name is heard in Sardis. For they are worthy because they did not defile their garments121 and will walk with me in white robes.”  The Scriptures: “Nevertheless, you have a few names in Sardis who have not defiled their garments. And they shall walk with Me in white, because they are worthy. v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” shim’cha, “your b' sardin, “in/ with/ by Sardis” (prep, she'lo, “that/ which/ et, (DO marker) polluted, defiled,” (Pi'el, qatal, past, reputation,” (n ms, heard',” (v, Nif'al, no/not,” (rel part, bgedayhem,”in/ with/ by their ve' he’ma, “and/ but/ so/ or they, telku, “you (mp). will go, walk,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, a'imi, “with me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) levinim, “white,” garments,” (prep, n mp, 3mp pronom) these, those,” (3mp clothing,” (prep, n he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, re'uyim, “worthy,” belonging to this,” (prep, pron, ms) <note type="footnote" n="119">See Revelation 1:18 for first occurrence. 120 Second Temple word first used in the Mishnah, Berakhot (“Blessings”). 121 “They did not defile their garments,” meaning, “they did not defile themselves.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.5">“Whoever that prevails will walk in white robes, and I will not blot out his name from the Book of Life and I will declare his name before my Father, and before His messengers.”  The Scriptures: “He who overcomes shall be dressed in white robes, and I shall by no means blot out his name from the Book of Life, but I shall confess his name before My Father and before His messengers.  Aramaic: He that is victorious, shall be so clothed in white robes; and I will not blot out their name from the book of life; and I will confess their name before my Father, and before his angels. u’mi, “and/ but/ so/ she’menatzeach, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s),” taylaych, “you (ms) will go, walk,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, levinim, “white,” v' ani, “and/ but/ lo, “no/not,” (neg so/ or I,” (1cs pron) garments,” (prep, n (rel part, v. Pi'el, Idiom: “from the book of life” emacheh, “I will et, (DO marker) shmo, “his/its v' ani, “and/ so/ but erase, blot out,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, name,” (n ms, 3ms m’ sefer, “in/ with/ by (the) book, scroll, Hif'il act part, ms) document,” (prep, n ms) ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp) et, (DO marker) shmo, “his/its avi, “my father,” (n v’lifnei, “and/ but/ melachav, “his/its messengers,” (n ms, 3mp pronom) name,” (n ms, 3ms before the face of, before me, in front ms, 1cs pronom) so/ or before, in front of, before <note type="footnote" n="122">The scribe uses gershayim (two slash marks) to indicate that this is an abbreviation for a name. This does not affect the translation.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.6">“’Whoever has ears, hears what the Spirit says to the congregation.”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies.”  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. mi, “who?” (inter she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznayim, “ears,” (n she'ha'ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms the spirit/ wind, Pa'al/Qal, act part, breath,” (rel part, n omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l'ha'edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the he/it those who Pa'al/Qal, act part, assembly,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.7">“To the messenger of the congregation of Philadelphia, write: ‘Thus says the Holy and the Faithful. This is he who has the Key of David, the One who opens, and no one can shut; and the One123 who shuts, so no man can open,’”124  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Philadelphia write, ‘He who is set-apart, He who is true, He who has the key of Dawiḏ, He who opens and no one shuts, and shuts and no one opens, says this:  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church which is at Philadelphia, write: These things saith he that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David, who openeth and no man shutteth, and shutteth and no man openeth; v' l' ha’ mal’ach, m’haeda, “of/ from the congregation, assembly,” (prep, n shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” katov!  “(to a man) koh, “so, thus, to such extent,” (adv) amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp messenger,” (prep, ha’kadosh, “the holy,” (adj, ms) v' ha’ nehehman, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it is faithful, devoted,” (v. Nif'al, act part, ze, “this” (pron ms) she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom ha’ mafteach, “the shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” him/it,” (prep, 3ms exists,” (rel part, David, (name) ha' poteach,”I/ you v' sum, “and/ but/ so/ or any,” (in a echad, “one,” (card yuchal, “he/it will l' sagir, “to shut, to close, to deliver,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, inf) ha' masgor, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it close(s), shut(s), lock(s) the Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa'al/Qal, act part, Pa'al/Qal, act part, v'sum, “and/ but/ so/ any,” (in a neg echad, “one,” (adj yuchal, “he/it will liftoach, “to unlock Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, (v. Pa'al/Qal inf <note type="footnote" n="123">The word דחא (echad), “one” can be translated as meaning, a person. 124 See Isaiah 22:22. 125 In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.8">“’I know your works. See, I have given you an open doorway,126 that no one can shut. But you have little power, but you kept my Words and did not deny My Name.’”  The Scriptures: “I know your works – see, I have set before you an open door, and no one is able to shut it – that you have little power, yet have guarded My Word, and have not denied My Name.  Aramaic: I know thy works. And lo, I have set before thee an open door, which no man can shut: because thou hast a little strength; and thou hast kept my word, and hast not denied my name. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) et, (DO marker) ma'asecha, “from/ of your (ms) deeds, re'e, “(to a man) natati, “I gave,” (v. lefanecha, “before you, before your face,” (prep, 2ms (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, works,” (prep, n mp, 2ms pronom) patuach, “open,” sum, “any,” (in a echad, “one,” (adj yuchal, “he/it will lisgor, “to close, otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, (v. Pa'al/Qal, inf entrance,” (n ms) m'at, “a little, little few, less, lesser, meager,” (adv) coach, “power,” v' shamarta, “and/ et, (DO marker) there exists, (part) belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, v' ainecha, “and/ but/ so/ or you are not,” (pron, neg kofer, “I/ you (ms)/ be' she'mi,”in/ with/ he/it deny(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act (n ms,1cs pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.9">“See, I will give those of the fellowship of Satan128 who say they are Jews,129 but are not  ̶  they are only liars. See, I will make them come to pray130 at your feet, for you to know that I love you.’”131   The Scriptures: “See, I am giving up those of the congregation of Satan, who say they are Yehuḏim and are not, but lie. See, I am making them come and worship before your feet, and to know that I have loved you.  Aramaic: Behold, I will give them of the congregation of Satan, who say they are Jews, and are not, but lie, behold I will make them to come and do obeisance before thy feet; and to know that I have loved thee. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) eten, “I will give,” she’hemah, “that/ which/ who/ they, m' chavrotat, “from/ of (the) fellowship of,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) belonging to these, those,” (prep, 3mp adversary,” (n ms) (prep, pron 3mp) ha' omrin, “the I/ you (ms)/ he/it she’he’mah, “that/ which/ who/ they, yehudim, “Jews, Judeans,” (n mp) ve'einam, “they are not, neither,” (3mp rak, “only, just,” kozvim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those re'e, “(to a man) see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, Pa'al/Qal, act part deceivers,” (n mp) rotza, “I/ you (ms) he/ it want(s), one asot, “to do, to make, to create,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, inf) she’he’mah, “that/ which/ who/ they, tavou, “he/it will litpalel, “to pray, to judge, to execute l'ragleycha, “to/ for/ belonging to your feet,” (prep, n which/ who/ whom I,” (rel part, 1cs Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, (v. Pi’el, inf constr) fs, 2ms pronom) Pa'al/Qal, act part, v’l'ehakir, “and/ she' havati,” which/ that/ who/ whom 'I marker) “you,” (2ms pronom) know,” (v. Hif’il Pa'al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.10">“Because you kept132 the Word, as I hoped, I will keep you from the time of the coming trial upon the earth, to test those dwelling upon the earth.”   The Scriptures: “Because you have guarded My Word of endurance, I also shall guard you from the hour of trial which shall come upon all the world, to try those who dwell on the earth.  Aramaic: Because thou hast kept the word of my patience, I also will keep thee from the hour of temptation, that is to come on all the inhabited world, to try them who dwell on the earth. kevan, “because,” she'shamarta, “that/ which/ who/ whom you (ms) guarded, kept, maintained,” m'tikvoti, “from/ of kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this ani, “I,” (1cs pron) eshmor, “I will word(s) of,” (n ms) according to my hope,” (prep n fs,1cs pronom) guard, I will keep, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, m'haeyt, “from/ of the time,” (prep, n shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” ha’nisayion, “the marker), “you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) linsot, “to prove,” (v. Pi’el, inf constr) hadarim, “the we/ you (mp)/ they, al, “upon, in, on, over, by, for, both, beyond, through,” belonging to these, those dwelling,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part following” (prep, <note type="footnote" n="132">Literally, “guarded.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.11">“See, I will come quickly. Guard what you have, so that no one will take your crown.”  The Scriptures: “See, I am coming speedily! Hold what you have that no one take your crown.  Aramaic: I come quickly: hold fast what thou hast, so that no one take thy crown. re'e, “(to a man) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) avo, “that I will shamor, “guard, she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, “quickly, speedily, Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa'al/Qal, imp 2ms) exists,” (rel part, k’dei, “be able, she'lo, “that/ which/ yikach, “he/it will take,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, sum, “any,” (in a et, (DO marker) belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) according to, as, in order to,” (conj) no/not,” (rel part, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) katarecha, “your crown,” (n mp, 2mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="133">See Revelation 2:5 for more details on this Second Temple word. 134 In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.12">“Whoever prevails, I will write on him the name of my Eloah,135 and the name of the new Jerusalem, which is the city of my Eloah, which will come from the heavens to the earth, and also My new Name.’”  The Scriptures: “He who overcomes, I shall make him a supporting post in the Dwelling Place of My Elohim, and he shall by no means go out. And I shall write on him the Name of My Elohim and the name of the city of My Elohim, the renewed Yerushalayim, which comes down out of the heaven from My Elohim, and My renewed Name.  Aramaic: Him that is victorious, will I make a pillar in the temple of my God; and he shall not again go out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and of the new Jerusalem which descendeth from heaven from my God, and my own new name. mi, “who?” (inter she'menatzeach,   “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s),” (rel part, v. Pi’el, alav, “on him, upon m'elohay, “from/ of my God(s),” (prep, n mp, 1cs pronom) v'ha’shem, “and/ concerning him,” (prep, 3ms pronom) mi’yerushalayim ''from/ of/ out of Jerusalem,” (prep, ha’chadash, “the new,” (adj ms) ha'ir, “the city,” (n she' yavo, “that/ m'hashamayim, “from/ of, the heavens, skies,” l'ha’eretz, “to/ for/ belonging to the earth,” (prep, n fs) God(s),” (n mp, 1cs which/ who/ whom he/it will come,” Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, m'elohay, “from/ of my God(s),” (prep, n mp, 1cs pronom) v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” she'mi, “my name,” (n ms, 1cs pronom) ha'chadash, “the new,” (adj ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.13">“’Whoever who has ears, hears what the Spirit says to the congregation.’”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies.”  Aramaic: He that hath ears, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. mi, “who?” (inter she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznim, “ears,” (n she' omea, “I/you (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” she'ha'ruach, “that /which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa'al/Qal, act the Spirit, wind, exists,” (rel part, breath,” (rel part, n omer, “I/ you (ms)/ l'ha'edah, “to/ for/ belonging to the he/it say(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, assembly,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.14">“And to the messenger of the congregation of Laodicea said, “Write, ‘Amen!137 The faithful witness from the beginning of creation.’”  The Scriptures: “And to the messenger of the assembly in Laodikeia write, ‘The Amĕn, the Trustworthy and True Witness, the Beginning of the creation of Elohim, says this:  Aramaic: And to the angel of the church which is at Laodicea, write: These things saith the Amen, the witness, the faithful, the true, the Chief of the creation of God: v’l'mal’ach, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the ma’eda, “of/ from the congregation, assembly,” (prep, n Laoditzea (name) ktov! “(to a man) ko, “so, thus, to amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, such extent,” (adv) angel, messenger,” ne'eman, loyal, faithful, devoted m'ha' briot, “from/ witness,” (n ms) “the beginning, started,” (n fs) of the creation, universe, creation,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.15">“’I know your works, that you are neither cold nor hot. I would rather that you be either cold or hot!’”  The Scriptures: “I know your works, that you are neither cold nor hot. I would that you were cold or hot.  Aramaic: I know thy works, that thou art neither hot, nor cold; I would that thou wert cold or hot. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) et, (DO marker) ma'asecha, “your she' atah, “that/ lo, “no/not,” (neg kar, “cold,” (adj, (ms)/ he know(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act (ms) deeds, works,” which/ who/ whom you,” (rel part, 2ms ve' lo, “and/ but/ cham, “hot,” (adj she' tiyeh, “that/ kar, “cold,” (adj, o, “or,” (conj) cham, “hot,” (adj perhaps, it may be which/ who/ whom you will be,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.16">“However, since you are neither cold nor hot, for this reason I will spit you out of my mouth.”  The Scriptures: “So, because you are lukewarm, and neither cold nor hot, I am going to vomit you out of My mouth.  Aramaic: So, because thou art lukewarm, neither hot nor cold, I am about to vomit thee from my mouth. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay kiven (h3559) “to lo, “no/not,” (neg kar, “cold” (adj, v' “and/ but/ so/ or, cham, “hot,” (adj which/ who/ whom you,” (rel part, 2ms fashion, fasten,” (v. bishvil, “for, for the ze, 'this (pron, ms) yarak,”he/it spat” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) m'pi “from/ of my mouth,” (prep, n ms, 1cs pronom) sake of, for this reason,” (prep) marker), “you,” (2ms pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.17">“And you will say, ‘I am wealthy, and I have enough and have no need of anything.’ However, you do not know that you are poor and destitute!’”  The Scriptures: “Because you say, ‘Rich I am, and I am made rich, and need none at all,’ and do not know that you are wretched, and pitiable, and poor, and blind, and naked.  Aramaic: Because thou sayest, I am rich and affluent, and have no want of any thing; and thou knowest not, that thou art impotent, and miserable, and needy, and blind, and naked; v'atah, “and/ but/ so/ or you,” (2ms tomar, “you will say,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ashir, “wealthy,” v' yesh, “and/ but/ so/ or there is, there dei, “enough of, belonging to me,” (prep, pron 1cs) yiqtol, fut, 2ms) necessary supply,” v'eina, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it is not,” tzorech, “need, dvar, “thing, word, aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay ainecha, “you not,” belonging to any,” matter,” (n ms) (pron, neg adv) requirement,” (n Pa'al/Qal, act part, oni, “poor,” (adj, v' evyon, “and/ but/ which/ who/ whom you,” (rel part, 2ms so/ or, destitute,” <note type="footnote" n="138">The word ןוכ with this spelling is found in the Mishnah Berakhot dating from c. 190CE to 230CE. 139 In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.18">“’I give my counsel to you: Acquire wealth140 from Me. And you will dress in white garments, and I will anoint your eyes with oil, so that you will be able to see.’”  The Scriptures: “I advise you to buy from Me gold refined in the fire, so that you become rich; and white garments, so that you become dressed, so that the shame of your nakedness might not be shown; and anoint your eyes with ointment, so that you see.  Aramaic: I counsel thee to buy of me gold tried in the fire, that thou mayest become rich; and white raiment, to be clothed, and that the shame of thy nakedness may not be seen; and put eye-salve on thine eyes, that thou mayest see. v' ani, “and/ so/ but/ or I,” (1cs noten, “I/ you (ms)/ shtikneh, “that/ zahav, “gold,” (n mimeni, “from/ of me,” (prep, 1 cs belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) which/ who/ whom (v. Pa'al/Qal, act (n fs, 1cs pronom) Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, v’t'lavush, “and/ m'lavushim, “from/ of (the) garments,” l'vanim, “white,” (purity) (adj mp) u’mashchat, “and/ et, (DO marker) aynehcha, “your eyes,” (n fp, 2mp bashemen, “with/ by/ in (the) oil, in oil,” (prep, n ms) but/ so/ or you will Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, anoint(s),” (v. Pi'el, k’dei, “be able, she'tuchal, “that/ lara'ot, “to see,” (v. according to, as, in which/ who/ whom/ you will be able,” order to,” (conj) yiqtol, fut, 2ms) <note type="footnote" n="140">Literally, “gold.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.19">“’I send a message to those whom I loved. So now, repent!’”142  The Scriptures: “As many as I love, I reprove and discipline. So be ardent and repent.  Aramaic: As many as I love, I rebuke and chasten. Be emulous therefore, and repent. v' ani, “and/ so/ but, or I,” (1cs she' havati, “that/ which/ who/ whom v'achshav,”and/ but/ so/ or now,” Idiom: “Repent!” (ms)/ he/it send(s),” belonging to these, those,” (prep, 3mp (v. Pa'al/Qal, act aseh, “make, do,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, 2ms) Pa'al/Qal, qatal, tshuvah,” repentance,” (n fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.20">“See!  I am standing before the door knocking.  If one hears my voice and opens the door, I will walk in.”144  The Scriptures: “See, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I shall come in to him and dine with him, and he with Me.  Aramaic: Behold, I have been standing at the door, and I will knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me. re'e, “(to a man) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) omed, “I/ you (ms)/ po'teach, “I/ you v'dofek, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms) / he/it knock(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part ba, “in/ with/ on/ see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, he/it Stand(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act before the face of, before me, in front (prep, 3fs pronom) Pa'al/Qal, act part, u’vim, “and/ but/ so/ or by if, when, whether,” (prep, she'echad, “that/ yishma,” he will et, (DO marker) koli, “my voice,” (n v' yipatach, “and/ but/ so/ or he will ha’po'teach, “I/ you which/ who/ whom one,” (rel part, card hear,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, ms, 1cs pronom) yiqtol, fut, 3ms) Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa'al/Qal, act part, aylach, “I will go,” belonging to this,” (prep, pron ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.21">“Whomever prevails, I will permit him to sit with Me upon My throne, in the same way as I have overcome and sit with my Father upon His throne.”  The Scriptures: “To him who overcomes I shall give to sit with Me on My throne, as I also overcame and sat down with My Father on His throne.  Aramaic: And to him that is victorious, to him will I give to sit with me on my throne, even as I was victorious, and sat down with my Father on his throne. mi, “who?” (inter she’menateach, eten, “I will give,” layashev, “to sit, dwell, inhabit,” 'imi, “with me,” (prep, 1s pronom) “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it overcome(s),” (v. Pi'el, act part, belonging to this,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) (prep pron, ms) (v. Pi'el inf constr) kisi, “my throne,” (n ms, 1cs pronom) she' nitzachti, “that/ which/ who/ whom I won,” (rel part, v. v'yashavti, “and/ but /so/ or I will dwell, abide,” im, “with,” (prep)  avi, “my father,” (n ms, 1 cs pronom) similarly to, such Pi'el, qatal, past, (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, throne,” (n ms, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.3.22">“Whoever who has ears, hears what the Spirit says.”  The Scriptures: “He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies.”’  Aramaic: He that hath ears to hear, let him hear what the Spirit saith to the churches. mi, “who?” (inter she'yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom oznim, “ears,” (n shomea “I/ you she'ha'ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom (ms)/ he/it hear(s),” him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa'al/Qal, act the Spirit/ wind, breath,” (n cs) exists,” (rel part, omer, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it say(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part,</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.4">
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.1">Then then I saw an open door in the heavens, and the first voice I heard speaking to me was like the voice of a shofar.145  It said, “Come here, I want to show you what comes after this!”  The Scriptures: After this I looked and saw a door having been opened in the heaven. And the first voice which I heard was like a trumpet speaking with me, saying, “Come up here and I shall show you what has to take place after this.”  Aramaic: After these things, I looked and lo, a door [was] open in heaven. And the first voice which I heard, was as of a trumpet talking with me. It said, Come up hither; and I will show thee the things that must occur hereafter. Idiom: "after this way" ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, po’teach, “door, echad, “one” (card b’shamayim, “in/ “that/ which I/you entrance,” (n ms) heavens,” (prep, n vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) opened,” (rel part, v. Nif'al, act part, kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” v’ ha’ kol, “and/ ha’rashon, “the first,” (ord num) ha’medaberet, “the I/ you (fs)/ she/it a'imi, “with me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) ke’kol, “like/ as (the) voice of,” shofar, “shofar, trumpet,” (n ms) “that/ which/ who/ whom I heard,” speak(s),” (v. Pi’el, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, amar,” he/ it said,” (v Pa’al/Qal,qatal, lechan, “to/ for/ belonging to here, v’ani, “and/ but/ so/ or I,” (pron, belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) show, explain, to cause to see,” (v. Hif’il, inf constr) Pa’al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, act part, Idiom: "after this way" belonging to you,” “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it will be,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” <note type="footnote" n="145">The voice of a shofar implies the shofar blast of war (see Nehemiah 4:20). For after the shofar blast, the Spirit soaks over John and he is shown various images in the heavenlies that demonstrates Yehovah and His Seven Spirits are about to bring judgement. And, in Revelation 4:8, Yehovah is called, “Yehovah of Armies.” Then, in Revelation 5, the seals are opened and Yehovah brings a great judgement upon the earth. It is also important to note that in Nehemiah 4:20, at the sound of the shofar blast, Yehovah fights on behalf of the children of Israel.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.2">And immediately, the Holy Spirit soaked over me, and I saw a throne sitting in the heavens, and upon the throne was One sitting upon it.  The Scriptures: And immediately I came to be in the Spirit and saw a throne set in the heaven, and One sat on the throne.  Aramaic: Instantly, I was in the Spirit: and lo, a throne was placed in heaven; and there was [one] seated on the throne. v’techef, “and/ but/ so/ or in a moment, very soon, at once, u’miyad, “and/ shoreh, “I/you (fs)/ ayii, “upon/ in/ over/ by/ through ruach, “Spirit, wind, breath” (n h'kodesh, “the holy,” (adj, ms) v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, immediately, lit. “from the hand,” soak(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act kise, “throne,” (n echad, “one” (card yoshev, “he/it sat, b’shamayim, “in/ v'al, “and/ but/ so/ ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) yoshev, “I/you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), Pa’al/Qal, qatal, heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, echad, “one” (card</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.3">Then He who sat upon it, His countenance was like the appearance of a sapphire stone and jasper, and around the throne was a rainbow as an emerald.  The Scriptures: And He who sat there was like a jasper and a ruby stone in appearance. And there was a rainbow around the throne, like an emerald in appearance.  Aramaic: And he who sat, was like the appearance of a jasper-stone, and of a sardine [sard], and of a rainbow of the clouds, round about the throne, in form as the appearance of emeralds. v’ha’yoshev, “and/ alayv, “on, upon, haya, “it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, mareho, “his/its even, “stone,” (n saffire, “saffire,” but/ so/ or the I/you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), dwell(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act him,” (prep, 3ms appearance,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) appearance,” (prep v’yashfe, “and/ ve’saviv, “and/ le’ha’kise, “to/ for/ haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, echad, “one” (card keshet, “bow, rainbow,” (n fs) but/ so/ or Jasper,” belonging to the throne,” (prep n similarly to, such nofekh, “emerald,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.4">And around the throne were twenty-four seats.  Upon them were sitting twenty-four elders, clothed in white garments, and upon their heads, a crown of gold.  The Scriptures: And around the throne were twenty-four thrones, and on the thrones I saw twenty-four elders sitting, dressed in white robes. And they had crowns of gold on their heads. ve’saviv, “and/ le’kise, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) haya, “it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, arba, “four,” (card ve’esrim, “and/ kisevim, “thrones,” ve’ale’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or upon but/ so/ or twenty,” throne,” (n ms) them,” (prep, 3mp yosevim, “we/ you (mp)/ they sit(s), arba, “four,” (card ve’esrim, “and/ zkenim,” elders,” lavush, “clothed,” b’melevushim, “in/ levanim, “white,” but/ so/ or twenty,” Pa’al/Qal, act, mp) clothing,” (prep, n v' al, ”and/ but/ so/ rasheihem, “their ketehr, “crown,” (n zahav, “gold,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.5">Then from the throne came sounds - thunders and lightnings - and seven lamps were before the throne for those are the seven Spirits of Yehovah.146  The Scriptures: And out of the throne came lightnings, and thunders, and voices. And seven lamps of fire were burning before the throne, which are the seven Spirits of Elohim.  Aramaic: And from the throne proceeded lightnings, and the sound of thunders; and seven lamps of fire were burning before his throne, which are the seven Spirits of God. u’me’hakiseh, “and/ so/ but/ or yotzei, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it goes out,” (Pa’al/Qal, kolot, “voices, sounds,” (n mp) ve’reamim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) thunders,” (n mp) u’vrakim, “and/ ve’shiv’a, “and/ so/ but/ or seven,” lightnings,” (n mp) throne,” (prep, n ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) v' eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, shiv’a, “seven,” ruchot, “spirits,” (n before the face of, before me, in front the following,” (3mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="146">See Revelation 1:4 for more details on the seven Spirits of Yehovah.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.6">And before the throne was a sea of glass147 like an amethyst; and in the midst and around the throne were four living creatures148 full of eyes in front and back.  The Scriptures: And before the throne there was a sea of glass, like crystal. And in the midst of the throne, and around the throne, were four living creatures, covered with eyes in front and in back.  Aramaic: And before the throne, as it were a sea of glass like crystal; and in the midst of the throne, and around it, and before the throne, were four Animals, full of eyes in their front and in their rear. v’lifnei, “and/ but/ ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, yam, “sea,” (n ms) echad, “one” (card shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” tzlochit, “flask, bottle, saucer” (n so/ or before, in front of, before kidmut, “as, like, u’ve’toch, “and/ but/ so/ or inside, ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) ve’saviv, “and/ le’ha’kise, “to/ for/ arba, “four,” (card “amethyst,” (n fs) belonging to the throne,” (prep, n haiyot, “beasts, male, “he/it filled,” einayim, “eyes,” (n me’lifneihem, “from/ of before ve’m’acharei’hem, living creatures” (n “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of behind qatal, past, 3ms) face(s),” (prep, 3mp pronom) them,” (prep, 3mp <note type="footnote" n="147">Or “sea of glass or reflecting pool.” 148 The word היח can mean “beast” or “living creature.” But when referring to the beast of Satan, “beast” is used and “living creature” when referring to the creatures before the throne of Yehovah.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.7">And the first living creature was like the image of a lion; the second like an ox; the third like a man; and the fourth, like an eagle.   The Scriptures: And the first living creature was like a lion, and the second living creature like a calf, and the third living creature had a face like a man, and the fourth living creature was like a flying eagle.  Aramaic: And the first Animal resembled a lion; and the second Animal resembled a calf; and the third Animal had a face like a man; and the fourth Animal resembled an eagle when flying. ve’haiyot, “and/ but/ so/ or the beast, living harishon, “the first”, (ord num) haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kid’mutt, “like/ as aryeh, “a lion,” (n keshor, “just as, like/ as an ox,” “and/ but/ so/ or the second,” (n fs) creature,” (n fs) v’ha’shlishi, “and/ ke’ adam, “like/ as v’ha’revi’i, “and/ ke’nesher, “like/ as (the) eagle,” (prep, but/ so/ or the third,” (adj ms) fourth,” (adj ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.8">Every one of them had six wings150 and filled with eyes within.151 And there was no rest for them day or night, as they continually declare, “Holy, Holy, Holy152 is Yehovah of Armies, the Almighty One, who was, is, and will be!”153  The Scriptures: And the four living creatures, each having six wings, were covered with eyes around and within. And they do not cease, day or night, saying, “Set-apart, set-apart, set-apart, הוהי Ěl Shaddai, who was, and who is, and who is coming!”  Aramaic: And these four Animals had, each of them, six wings around it: and within they were full of eyes: and they have no cessation, day or night, from saying: Holy, Holy, Holy, the Lord God, the Omnipotent, who was, and is, and is to come. v’le’kol “and/ but/ echad, “one” (card shesh, “six,” (card u’me’ b' nefim, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of within,” me’lelu’im, “filled, im, “with,” (prep) “wings,” (n fp) setting,” (n mp) belonging to (the) all,” (prep, n ms) einayim, “eyes,” (n ve’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not,” lahem, “to /for/ menucha, “rest,” yom, “day,” (n ms) ve’ laylah, “and/ but/ so/ or night,” there exists,” (part) them,” (prep, 3mp ve’ omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those Yehovah tzvaot, “hosts, armies,” (n mp) consecrated,” (adj consecrated,” (adj consecrated,” (adj Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’haya, “the/that ve’hoveh, “and/ but/ so/ or I/you (ms)/he/it to be” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act ve’yihye, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it mighty, great,” he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, <note type="footnote" n="149">The crossed-out word appears to have been struck through by the original scribe and does not affect translation and therefore was not included.</note> <note type="footnote" n="150">See Isaiah 6:3. 151 See Ezekiel 1:18. 152 See Isaiah 6:1-13. 153 See Exodus 3:14.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.9">At that time, the living creatures praised and gave thanks to this One sitting upon the throne and lives forever and ever.  The Scriptures: And when the living creatures give esteem and respect and thanks to Him who sits on the throne, who lives forever and ever,  Aramaic:  And when these Animals give glory and honor and praise to him that sitteth on the throne, to him who liveth for ever and ever, u’ve’sha’ah “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ notanim “we/ you (mp)/ they, those shevach, “praise,” ve’hodah, “and/ she’yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), dwell(s),” “that/ which/ who/ whom the beasts, living creatures” belonging to this” (prep, pron, ms) by (the) hour, at that time,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, confession,” (n fs) Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) v’k'chay, "and/ meo’lam, “from/ of (the) forever,” v’ad, “and, but/ so/ olam, “forever,” (n but/ so/ or as/ like or until, up to,” "and my strength,"</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.10">There were twenty-four elders prostrate before Him praying154 the One who lives forever and ever, casting their crowns before Him, saying, The scriptures: the twenty-four elders fall down before Him who sits on the throne and bow before Him who lives forever and ever, and they cast their crowns before the throne, saying,  Aramaic: the twenty and four Elders fall down before him who sitteth on the throne, and they worship him who liveth for ever and ever; and they cast their coronets before the throne, saying, hayu, “they were,” noflim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those arba, “the four,” ve’esrim, “and/ zkenim,” elders,” lefanav, “before him/it,” (prep, 3ms pronom) u’mitpalelim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those but/ so/ or twenty,” qatal, past, 3mp) Pa’al/Qal, act part, worshiping,” (v. Hit’pael, act part, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it live(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, molam, “from/ of ve’ ad, “and/ but/ so/ or until, up to,” olam, “forever,” (n ve’zorkim, “and/ kitreihem, “their crowns,” (n mp, 3mp pronom) belonging to this,” (prep, pron, ms) but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ those lefanav, “before ve’ omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.4.11">“Lord, You are worthy to receive honor and glory. For You created all things, and by the hand of Your will, everything was made."  The Scriptures: “You are worthy, O הוהי, to receive esteem and respect and power, for You have created all, and because of Your desire they are, and were created.”  Aramaic: Worthy art thou, O Lord our God, the Holy, to receive glory and honor and power; for thou hast created all things, and by thee they exist; and because of thy pleasure they had being and were created. atah, “you,” (pron re'uya, “worthy,” liqach, “take,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf abs) chevod, “honor,” ve’ tif'eret, “and/ but/ so/ or glory, splendor, beauty, magnificence,” (n atah, “you,” (pron ha’ kol, “the all, everything,” (n retzoncha, “your desire, your will,” ha’ kol, “the all, everything,” (n al’yadei, “by the hand of,” (idiom) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, become(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, <note type="footnote" n="155">The added yod (י) mater lectionis is a unique late Second Temple Hebrew linguistic shift due to the pressure of the neighboring Aramaic language. The linguistic shift is called Hebrew “Aramaism” and would have been spoken by John.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.5">
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.1">And the One who sat upon the throne: I saw in His right hand a scroll sealed from within and on the outside with seven seals.  The Scriptures: And I saw in the right hand of Him who sat on the throne a scroll written inside and on the back, having been sealed with seven seals.  Aramaic: And I saw, at the right hand of him who sat on the throne, a book, which was written within and on the back side, and which was sealed with seven seals. ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, she’yashav “that/ which/ who/ whom ha’ kise, “the throne,” (n ms) ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, be' yad, “in/ with/ yemino, “his/its right,” (n ms, 3ms by (the) hand,” he/it sat, dwelt,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, sefer, “book, scroll, document” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card v' chatum, “and/ but / so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it is sealed up,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, b' chatimot, “in/ with/ by (the) m' b' penim,” “from/ of (the) interior, within,” um’behotz,” and/ but/ so/ or from/ of in/ with/ by (the) outside, exterior,” signatures, seals,” seven,” (prep, card “signatures, seals,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.2">And I saw a messenger cry out with a great voice, “Who is worthy to open the scroll and break its seals?”  The Scriptures: And I saw a strong messenger proclaiming with a loud voice, “Who is worthy to open the scroll and to loosen its seals?”  Aramaic: And I saw a strong angel, who proclaimed with a loud voice, Who is competent to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof? v’rai’ti “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, echad, “one,” (card tzoek, “I/you (ms)/ b' qol, “in/ with/ by (the) voice, sound,” gadol, “great,” (adj mi, “who?” (inter Pa’al/Qal, act part, re'uyah, “worthy,” liftoach, “to open, et, (DO marker) ha' sefer, “the book, scroll, document,” v’l’shaver, “and/ “his/its signatures, seals,” (n fp, 3 ms smash,” (v. Pi’el,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.3">But no one in the heavens or on the earth was able to open the scroll and see it.  The Scriptures: And no one in the heaven or on the earth or under the earth was able to open the scroll, or to look at it.  Aramaic: And no one either in heaven above, or on the earth, or beneath the earth, was able to open the book, or to look thereon. v'sum, “and/ but/ so/ any,” (in a neg echad, “one,” (card lo, “no/ not” (part) b’shamayim, “in/ v' b’eretz, “and/ yuchal, “he/it will liftoach, “to open, but/ so/ or with/ in/ by/ with/ in (the) earth,” (prep, n fs) heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha' sefer, “the book, scroll, document,” (ulirot,) “and/ but/ so/ or to see,” (v. bo, “in/ with/ by him/it” (prep   3ms <note type="footnote" n="156">In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.4">And I wept much because not one was found worthy to do this thing.  The Scriptures: And I wept much, because no one was found worthy to open and read the scroll, or to look at it.  Aramaic: And I wept much, because no one was found, who was competent to open the book, or to look on it. ve ‘bocha, “and/ but/ for/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it cry(s) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) kevan, “because,” nimtza, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is echad, “one,” (card which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) found,” (v. Nif’al, Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha' dbar, “the word, thing, matter,” (n “worthy,” (adj fs) belonging to this, this one,” (pron ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.5">Then one of the elders said to me, “Do not weep!  See, the eternal Lion from the family of Judah, the root of David, has prevailed to open the scroll and its seals!”  The Scriptures: And one of the elders said to me, “Do not weep. See, the Lion of the tribe of Yehuḏah, the Root of Dawiḏ, overcame to open the scroll and to loosen its seven seals.”  Aramaic: And one of the Elders said to me, Weep not; behold, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, hath been victorious: He will open the book, and its seven seals. v' echad, “and/ but/ so/ or one,” (card me’ha’zkanim, “from/ of the amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, al, “not,” (neg adv) tivke, “you will re'ei, “see!” (v. belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) Pa'al/Qal, imp, ms) elders,” (prep, adj Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, she’nitzeach, “that/ which/ who/ whom arye, “the lion,” (n ha'yesh, “the, that/ m' meshpachti, “from/ of my yuda, “Judah,” “from/ of the root,” (the) eternal,” (n family, tribe, clan,” Should be spelled: liftoach, “to open, unlock, to unseal,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf ha' sefer, “the book, scroll, document,” v’le’shaver, “and/ seven,” (card num) “signatures, seals,” smash,” (v. Pi’el,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.6">I saw in the midst of the throne, the living creatures and the twenty-four elders, standing as a Lamb that was killed.  And He had seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of Yehovah157 sent into all the earth.  The Scriptures: And I looked and saw in the midst of the throne and of the four living creatures, and in the midst of the elders a Lamb standing, as having been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of Elohim sent out into all the earth.  Aramaic: And I looked, and in the midst of the Elders stood a lamb, as if slain; and it had seven horns, and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God that are sent into all the earth. ve’ ra'iti, “and/ but/ She’ betoch, “that/ which/ who/ whom inside, midst,” (rel ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) ve’ha’arba, “and/ v’esrim, “and/ but/ zkenim,” elders,” so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, “and/ but/ so/ or the four,” (card num) creatures,” (n fp) amad, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it stand(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, seh, “lamb,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card k’mo, “like, as, similarly to, such she’ne’herag, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it was killed,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms shiv’a, “seven,” karnayim, “horns,” v' sheva, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) seven,” einayim, “eyes,” (n v' eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, ruchot, “spirits,” (n seven,” (card num) the following,” (3mp pronom) nishlach, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is sent,” (v. Nif'al, act part, be'chol, “in/ with/ by (the) all,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.7">And He came and took the scroll from the right hand of He who sat upon the throne.  The Scriptures: And He came and took the scroll out of the right hand of Him sitting on the throne.  Aramaic: And he came, and took the book from the right hand of him who sat on the throne. uvah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it came,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’lakach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it took,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, m' yod, “from/ of (the) hand,” (prep, v' yemino, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its m’ze, “from/ of this,” (prep, pron she’yashav, “that/ which/ who sat,” document,” (n ms) right (arm),” (n ms, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.8">And when He took the scroll, the four living creatures158 and twenty-four elders fell before the Lamb.  And in their hands were a lyre and censors full of incense, which are the prayers of the holy ones.  The Scriptures: And when He took the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb, each holding a harp, and golden bowls filled with incense, which are the prayers of the set-apart ones.  Aramaic: And when he took the book, the four Animals and the twenty and four Elders fell down before the Lamb, each of them having a harp, and cups of gold full of odors, which are the supplications of the saints. u'vsha'a, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by (the) hour,” (prep, she’lakach, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it took” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha' sefer, “the book, scroll, document,” hayu, “they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, noflim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those chaiyot, “beasts, four,” (card num) living creatures” (n Pa’al/Qal, act part, v' arav'a, “and/ but/ so/ or four,” (card v' ashrim, and/ but/ zkenim,” elders,” ha’se, “the lamb,” v' b' yidihem, “and/ but/ so/ or in their hands,” (n fp, 2ms kinor, “stringed before the face of, before me, in front musical instrument, harp, lyre,” (n s) umachtot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) utensils, censers, fire pans,” (n fp) mele'im, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those ketoret, “incense sacrifices,” (n fs) v' zot, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, hi, “she/ it,” (3fs tefilat, “prayer of,” ha' kadoshim, “the holy ones, the set-apart ones,” (adj Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.9">And they sang159 a renewed song and said, “You are worthy to take the scroll and open its seals, for You were slain, and You redeemed us by Your own blood.” v' zimru,”and/ but/ so/ or they sing(s),” shir, “song, poem,” v' amaru, “and/ but/ atah, “you,” (pron re'uya, “worthy,” liqach, “take,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf abs) so/ or they said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve’liftoach, “and/ but/ so/ or to open, unlock, unseal,” (v. et, (DO marker) chatimotaiv, atah, “you,” (pron neherag, “I/ you “his/its signatures, seals,” (n fp, 3ms document,” (n ms) killed,” (v. Nif'al, v' kanita, “and/ but/ so/ or you otanu, “us,” (prep, b' damecha, “with/ blood(s),” (prep, n ms, 2 mp pronom) purchased,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.10">“You made us to be priests and kings162 so we become kings upon the earth.”  The Scriptures: and made us sovereigns and priests to our Elohim, and we shall reign upon the earth.”  Aramaic: and thou hast made them kings and priests to our God; and they reign on the earth. v' ashita, “and/ but/ otanu, “us,” (prep, l' kohanim, “to/ for/ v' anachnu, “and/ but/ so/ or we/us,” melachim, “kings,” so/ or you made “and/ but/ so/ or to/ became,” (Nif'al, qatal, past, 3mp) priests,” (prep n for/ belonging to Pa’a/Qal, qatal, (the) kings,” (n mp) Note: should be, “we <note type="footnote" n="160">The song is either new (adjective masculine singular) or renewed (active participle) from old. See Ecclesiastes 1:9. 161 The added yod (י) mater lectionis is a unique Second Temple Hebrew linguistic shift due to the pressure of the neighboring Aramaic language. The linguistic shift is called Hebrew “Aramaism” and would have been spoken by John. Tractate Avadim 2:3 uses this exact spelling and is traced from as early as c. 100 BCE to 900 CE. 162 Also see Exodus 19:6, Isa 61:6; 66:21; 1 Peter 2:5,9; Revelation 1:6, 5:10; 20:6.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.11">Then I saw and heard many voices of messengers surrounding the throne.  Their number was thousands of thousands.  The Scriptures: And I looked, and I heard the voice of many messengers around the throne, and the living creatures, and the elders. And the number of them was myriads of myriads, and thousands of thousands,  Aramaic: And I looked, and I heard, as it were the voice of many angels, around the throne, and the Animals and the Elders; and the number of them was a myriad of myriads, and thousand of thousands, ra'iti, “and/ but/ so/ v' shama'iti, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) ha’ rabeh, “great, vast, numerous,” m’ha’mal’achim, saviv, “around, l’ha’kise, “to/ for/ belonging to the throne,” (prep, n Pa'al/Qal, qatal, surrounding,” (adv) messengers,” (prep, u’misparam, “and/ haya, “it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, riv'vot, “myriad, a great many, tens of thousands,” (n fp) but/ so/ or their number,” (n ms, “thousands,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.12">Then they say with a loud voice, “The Lamb that was killed is worthy of power, honor, glory, and prayers!”  The Scriptures: saying with a loud voice, “Worthy is the Lamb having been slain to receive power and riches and wisdom, and strength and respect and esteem and blessing!”  Aramaic:  who said, with a loud voice; Competent is the Lamb that was slain, to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honor, and glory, and blessing; v' omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (mp)/ they say(s)”, (v. Pa’al/Qal, act b' qol, “in/ with/ by (the) voice, sound,” gadol, “great,” (adj ha’se, “the lamb,” ha' neh'erag, “the slain, the (one) killed, slain,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, re'uya, “worthy,” l' koach,” to/ for/ belonging to (the) strength, power, force,” (prep n ms) v’l’chevod, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the) honor,” (prep, n v'l’tif'eret, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) glory,” (prep, n fs) v'lit'hilat, “and/ but/ belonging to (the) prayers,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.13">All the living creatures in the heavens and upon the earth, beneath the earth and in the sea:  I heard them say, “To the One sitting upon the throne and to the Lamb, are given glory, adoration, and praise forever and ever!”  The Scriptures: And every creature which is in the heaven and on the earth and under the earth and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, I heard saying, “To Him sitting on the throne, and to the Lamb, be the blessing and the respect and the esteem and the might, forever and ever!” v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) ha' briot, “from/ of ha'yesh, “the, that/ b’shamayim, “in/ ve’ al, “and/ but/ so/ or upon, on,” umitachat, “and/ but/ so/ or beneath, universe, creation,” heavens,” (prep, n underneath,” (prep) u’b' yom, “and/ she' omrim, “that/ which/ who/ whom we/ you (mp)/ they, those saying,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, ha' yoshev, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), but/ so/ or in/ with/ by (the) sea,” (prep, which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it belonging to this,” (prep, pron ms) heard),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) v’l’hase, “and/ but/ chevod, “honor, glory,” (n ms) v' tehilot, "and/ but/ v' shevach, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) praise,” (n ms) m' olam, “from/ of v' ad, “and/ but/ belonging to (the) lamb,” (prep, n ms) adoration, glories," forever,“ (prep, n eternity,” (n ms) m' olam, “from/ of (the) eternity, forever,“ (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.5.14">Then the four living creatures answer, “Amen!” And the twenty-four elders fell, praying to the One who lives forever and ever.  The Scriptures: And the four living creatures said, “Amĕn!” And the twenty-four elders fell down and bowed before Him who lives forever and ever.  Aramaic: And the four Animals said: Amen. And the Elders fell down, and adored. ve’ arba, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) four,” ha’ chayot, “and/ onim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those answering,” (v. ve’ arba, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) four,” ve’esrim, “and/ but/ zkenim,” elders,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, noflim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those u’mitpallim, “and/ but/ so /or (the) we/ she’ chai, “that/ which who I/ you (ms)/ he/it live(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act m' olam, “from/ of v’ad, “and/ but/ so/ m' olam, “from/ of belonging to this,” or until, up to,” Pa'al/Qal, act part, duration, forever, everlasting,” (prep, duration, forever, everlasting,” (prep, Hit’pael, act part, <note type="footnote" n="164">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.6">
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.1">And I saw the Lamb open one of the seals and I heard the four living creatures say as one voice, “Come and see!”  The Scriptures: And I saw when the Lamb opened one of the seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures saying, like a sound of thunder, “Come and see.”  Aramaic: And, when the Lamb had opened one of the seven seals, I looked, and I heard one of the four Animals say, as with a voice of thunder, Come, and see. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, she'ha’se, “that/ poteach, “I/ you echad, “one,” (card v' shamati, “and/ she’ha’arba, “that, which/ who/ whom, the four,” (rel part, which/ who/ whom the lamb,” (rel part, “signatures, seals,” but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, chayot, “beasts, omrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those who say(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act k'qol, "as/like (the) voice", (prep, n ms) bo, “(to a man) v’re’eh, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a man) see,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, living creatures” (n Pa’al/Qal, imp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.2">Then I saw a white horse, and he who sat upon him had a bow in his hand, and a crown given to him. And he proceeded to prevail and be victorious.  The Scriptures: And I looked and saw a white horse, and he who sat on it holding a bow. And a crown was given to him, and he went out overcoming and to overcome.  Aramaic: And I looked, and there was a white horse: and he who sat on it, had a bow; and a coronet was given to him, and he went forth conquering, that he might conquer. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sus, “horse,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card lavan, “white,” (adj ve’ha’yoshev, “and/ but/ so/ or I/you (ms)/ he/it haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, concerning him/it,” (prep, 3ms pronom) Pa’al/Qal, act part, beyado, “in/ with/ by his/its hand,” (prep, n fs, 3ms keshet, “bow, rainbow,” (n fs) echad, “one,” (card v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ noten, “I/ you (ms)/ keter, “crown,” (n echad, “one,” (card belonging to him,” (prep, 3ms pronom) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms le’natseach, “to “victory,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, overcome,” (v. Pi'el, inf constr)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.3">And when the second seal was opened. I heard the second living creature say, “Come and see!”  The Scriptures: And when He opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature saying, “Come and see.”  Aramaic: And when he had opened the second seal, I heard the second Animal say, Come. l' kevan, “and/ but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” she’niftach, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you/ (ms)/ he/it is opened,” (v. Nif’al, she’haya,“that/ ha’ sheniyah, “the “signatures, seals,” second,” (adj ms) which/ who/ whom Pa'al/Qal, qatal, the beast, living creature,” (rel part, amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, v’re’eh, “and/ but/ Pa’al/Qal, imp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.4">Then another went out; a red horse.  Sitting on it was authorized to take peace from the earth, and he was given a great sword.165  The Scriptures: And another horse, fiery red, went out. And it was given to the one who sat on it to take peace from the earth, and that they should slay one another. And a great sword was given to him.  Aramaic: And there went forth another, a red horse; and to him who sat thereon, it was given, to take tranquillity from the earth; and that they should kill one another; and there was given to him a great sword. ve’halach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it la’chutz,“to/ for/ sus, “horse,” (n ms) acher, “other, adom, “red,” (adj, ve’ha’yoshev, “and/ but/ so/ or I/you (ms)/ he/it alav, “on, upon/ by concerning him/it,” (prep, 3ms pronom) another, different,” outside, out,” (prep, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, notan, “I/ you (ms)/ liqach, “take,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf abs) ha’shalom, “the peace,” (n ms) me’ha’eretz, “from/ of the earth,” (prep, v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ noten, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it give(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, (v. Pa’al/Qal, act destroy(s),” (v. him/it,” (prep, pron Pa’al/Qal, act part, cherev, “sword,” (n gadol, “great,” (adj</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.5">Then when the third seal was opened, the third living creature said, “Come and see!” And I saw a black horse and one sitting on it had a set of scales in his hand.  The Scriptures: And when He opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature say, “Come and see.” And I looked and saw a black horse, and he who sat on it holding a pair of scales in his hand.  Aramaic: And when he had opened the third seal, I heard the third Animal say, Come, and see. And I looked, and lo, a black horse; and he that sat thereon, had a balance in his hand. u’ba’' sha'a, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by (the) moment, while, hour,” (prep, she’poteach, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it open(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act ha’shlishi, “the amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’shlishi, “and/ “signatures, seal,” third,” (card num) but/ so/ or the third,” (adj ms) creature” (n fs) bo, “(to a man) ve’ re’eh, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sus, “horse,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card shachor, “black,” “and/ but/ so/ or I/ Pa’al/Qal, imp, man) see, behold,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, act part, alav, “on him/it,” (prep, pron 3ms) haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, be’yadu, “in/ with/ by his/its hand,” (prep, n ms, 3ms echad, “one,” (card “scales, balances” <note type="footnote" n="165">This phrase can be translated as, “he was granted to do great destruction.” 166 The added yod (י) mater lectionis is a unique Second Temple Hebrew linguistic shift due to the pressure of the neighboring Aramaic language. The linguistic shift is called Hebrew “Aramaism” and would have been spoken by John.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.6">Then I heard a voice in the midst of the four living creatures say, “A measure of wheat for two faces,167 three measures of barley for two faces; but the oil and the wine do not injure.  The Scriptures: And I heard a voice in the midst of the four living creatures saying, “A measure of wheat for a denarius, and three measures of barley for a denarius. And do not harm the oil and the wine.”  Aramaic: And I heard a voice in the midst of the four Animals, saying: A choenix of wheat for a denarius, and three choenices of barley for a denarius; and hurt not the oil and the wine. v' shama'iti, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, qol, “voice,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card betoch, “inside, chayot “beasts, amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, which, the four,” living creatures” (n middle, among” midah, “measure,” echat, “one,” (card chitim, “wheat(s),” v’shlosha, “and/ but/ so/ or three,” midot, “measures,” second,” (adj ms) be’sheni, “in/ with/ v’le’ha’shemen, “and/ but/ so/ for/ to the oil,” (n ms) ve’ha’yayin, “and/ al, “not,” (neg adv) ta’aseh, “you shall “barley(s),” (n fp) by (the) two, second,” (prep, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, wickedness,” (n <note type="footnote" n="167">Possible Hebrew idiom meaning, “faces of coins” or “coins.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.7">And when the fourth seal opened, I heard the fourth living creature say, “Come and see!”  The Scriptures: And when He opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature saying, “Come and see.”  Aramaic: And when he had opened the fourth seal, I heard the fourth Animal say, Come, and see. v' kevan, “and/ but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” she’petach, “that which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it open,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’ revi’i, “and/ but/ so/ or the ha’ revi’i, “and/ but/ so/ or the “signatures, seal,” fourth,” (ord num) Pa'al/Qal, qatal, creature” (n fs) fourth,” (ord num) omer, “I/ you (ms)/ bo, “(to a man) ve’ re’eh, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a he/it say(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, imp, man) see, behold,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.8">Then I saw a strong mottled168 horse and the one who sat on him was named the Messenger of Death, and Gehinnom169  went after him.  He was given authority to cause death to a fourth upon the earth with sword, hunger, and death by the living creatures of the earth.  The Scriptures: And I looked and saw a green horse. And he who sat on it had the name Death, and She’ol followed with him. And authority was given to them over a fourth of the earth, to kill with sword, and with hunger, and with death, and by the beasts of the earth.  Aramaic: And I looked, and lo, a pale horse; and the name of him who sat thereon was Death; and Hades followed after him. And there was given him authority over the fourth part of the earth, to slay with the sword, and by famine, and by death, and by the ravenous beast of the earth. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sus, “horse,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card ba’rad, “hail,” (as if ve’ometz, “and/ but/ or strong, ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron) she' yeshav, "that/ which/ who/ whom he/it sat,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, hail), mottled” (n courageous, brave, valor,” (adj ms) alav, “on, upon, by, concerning him/it,” (prep, 3ms pronom) haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ha'mot, “death,” (n v' ha’gehinnom, halach, “he/it went, name,” (n ms, 3ms and/ but/ so/ or the Gehinnom, hell, or Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Hinnom,” (n ms) v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ or to him/it,” (prep, noten, “I/ you (ms)/ rashut, “authority, lehamit, “to cause to die,” (v. Hif'il, chelek, “portion, ha’ revi’i, “fourth,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act permission,” (n fs) u’va’ra’av, “and/ u’be’mot, “and/ chaiyot, “beasts, “by/ with/ in (the) sword,” (prep, n but/ so/ or with/ by/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ Idiom: v' al’yadei, “by the hand of,” living creature,” (n for (the) famine, hunger,” (prep, n by (the) death,” <note type="footnote" n="168">Can also mean, “speckled.” See Genesis 30:10, Exodus 9:18, 28:17, 30:30. This appears to have a direct correlation with the horses of Zechariah 6. 169 Gehinnom is a valley outside of Jerusalem where Solomon built a statue of Moloch.  170 The Gehennom or Gehenna, is not a word formed in the Tanakh, but it begins appearing in texts from c. 500 BCE to 1100 CE (See Perek Shirah, Matthew 5:22).</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.9">And when He opened the fifth, I saw beneath171 the holy place,172 the souls that were killed for the Holy Name, and for the sake of their testimony.  The Scriptures: And when He opened the fifth seal, I saw under the slaughter-place the beings of those having been slain for the Word of Elohim and for the witness which they held,  Aramaic: And when he had opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of them who were slain on account of the word of God, and on account of the testimony to the Lamb which was with them. v' kevan, “and/ but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” she’petach, “that which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it open(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ha’hekal, “the holy ha’neshamot, “the “fifth,” (adj ms) below, bottom, or at the foot,” (prep) k’doshat, “sain, ha’ shem, “the name,” (n ms) (rabbinical term u’bishvil, “and/ but/ so/ or for, for the sake of,” (prep) she'haya, “that/ “that/ which/ who/ whom they were testimony,” (n fs) which/ who/ whom he/it was,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, hallowed,” (adj, fs) killed,” (rel part, v. Nif'al, qatal, past, la’ hem, “to them,” (prep, pron 3mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.10">Then they shout with a great voice saying, “The Lord is holy and faithful!  Until when will You judge, and avenge our blood from those dwelling upon the earth?”  The Scriptures: and they cried with a loud voice, saying, “How long, O Master, set-apart and true, until You judge and avenge our blood on those who dwell on the earth?”  Aramaic: And they cried with a loud voice, saying: How long, O Lord, thou holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth? v’tzo’akim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those b' qol, “in/ with/ by (the) voice, sound,” ve’omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those adon, “Lord,” (n ha’kadosh, “holy, sacred, hallowed,” v’ha’ne’e’man, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is faithful,” (v. Nif'al, gadol, “great,” (adj Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, al, “until, up to,” me’tay, “when, until when” (adv) tishpot, “you will v’inah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) cause,” tinkom, “you will me’eilu, “from/ of these, those, the following,” (prep, blood(s),” (n mp, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, ha’darim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those who dwell,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part <note type="footnote" n="173">Literally, "They were killed." 174 This word,  םשה (ha’shem) is a rabbinic phrase meaning, “The Name” is used instead of the name of Yehovah. The usage of this word is according to rabbinic customs because it is believed that the name of Yehovah is too holy to be spoken.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.11">And every one of them was given white garments, and it was said to them, “Relax still, a little while.”   The Scriptures: And there was given to each one a white robe, and they were told that they should rest a little while longer, until both the number of their fellow servants and their brothers, who would be killed as they were, was completed.  Aramaic: And to each one of them was given a white robe; and it was told them, that they must be quiet yet a little while, until the consummation of their fellow-servants and brethren, who were to be killed as they had been. v' le’ kol, “and/ but/ echad, “one,” (card mehem, “from/ of them,” (prep, 3mp noten, “I/ you (ms)/ lavan, “white,” (adj v’ne’e’mar, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it is said,” (v. Nif'al, act part, belonging to (the) all,” (prep, n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act garments,” (n mp) lahem, “to/ for/ she’ tishketu, “that/ which/ who/ whom mu’at,” few, few in belonging to them,” season, a set time, appointed time,” (n numbers, little,” you (mp) will be yiqtol, fut, 2mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.12">Then I saw that He opened the sixth then there were tremblings of the earth, and the sun became dark, and the moon was red as blood.177  The Scriptures: And I looked when He opened the sixth seal and saw a great earthquake came to be. And the sun became black as sackcloth of hair, and the moon became as blood.  Aramaic: And I looked, when he had opened the sixth seal, and there was a great earthquake; and the sun became black, like sackcloth of hair; and the whole moon became like blood. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, she’poteach, “that which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it open(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, act v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was,” re’adot, “rattlings, sixth,” (card num) “and/ but/ so/ or the (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, tremblings,” (n fp) haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, shachor, “black, dark,” (adj ms) ve hayareach, “and/ haya,” he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, edom, “red,” (adj kedem, “like/ as but/ so/ or (the) moon,” (n ms) (the) blood,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.13">All their armies drop as a withering leaf from the vine, so like a withering fig tree.181  The Scriptures: And the stars of the heaven fell to the earth, as a fig tree drops its unripe figs, being shaken by a strong wind. ve' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) tzva’am, “their (m) yibol, “he/it will wither, to drop kin’vol, “like/ as (the) withering, ele, “leaf,” (n ms) me’gefen, “from/ ve’ka’novelet, “and/ but/ so/ or army, hosts,” (n mp, 3mp pronom) falling off,” (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, inf like/ as I/ you (ms)/ Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, me’teynah “from/ of (the) fig, fig tree,” (prep, n fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.14">Then all the mountains and hills he moved to and fro, and they were shaken183 from their places.184  The Scriptures: And heaven departed like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved out of its place.  Aramaic: And the heavens separated, as a book is rolled up: and all mountains and islands were removed out of their places. ve' chol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) ha’ harim, “the ug’vaot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) hills,” possible meaning: mountains,” (n mp) locations, places” (prep, n mp, 3mp</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.15">And the kings of the earth, the rulers, the wealthy, the officers, the servants, and the freemen hid themselves in rocks, in caves, and in the burrows of the earth186  The Scriptures: And the sovereigns of the earth, and the great ones, and the rich ones, and the commanders, and the mighty, and every slave and every free one, hid themselves in the caves and in the rocks of the mountains,  Aramaic: And the kings of the earth, and the nobles, and the captains of thousands, and the rich men, and the men of valor, and every servant and free man, hid themselves in caves, and in the clefts of the mountains; u’malchei, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) kings of,” (n mp aretz, “earth, land,” ve’roznim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ve’ashirim, “and/ but/ so/ or rich, ve’ha’evrim, “and/ v’ha’chofashim, “and/ but/ so/ or bondservants,” (n “and/ but/ so/ or the rulers, princes,” (n wealthy,” (adj mp) official, officer, secretary,” (n mp) servants,” (n mp) sotrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they hide,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act be' me’arot, “in/ afar, “dust, ashes, earth, dirt,” (n ms) with/ by (the) caves,” (prep, n “and/ but/ so/ or in/ burrows of, clefts of,” (prep, n fp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.16">saying to the mountains and to the rocks, “Fall on us,188 and hide us from before the sight of Him sitting upon the throne189 who sits upon the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.”  The Scriptures: and said to the mountains and rocks, “Fall on us and hide us from the face of Him sitting on the throne and from the wrath of the Lamb,  Aramaic: and they said to the mountains and to the clefts, Fall over us, and hide us from the face of him who sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb: ve’ omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those l'ha’harim, “to/ for/ v’ l' sla'im, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the rocks,” (prep, n nefol! (to a man) aleinu, “on us,” vsetor, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a man) hide, conceal us!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, belonging to the mountains,” (prep, (prep, 1cp pronom) (DO marker, 1cp Pa’al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, act part, m' panei, “from/ of shel, “of, belonging ze, “this,” (pron, ha’yoshev, “the I/ ha' kise, “the throne,” (n ms) sits,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, u'mipanay, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of charon, “anger, ha’se, “the lamb,” indignation,” (n presence of, before, in front of,” (prep)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.6.17">“For the day of His wrath of anger has come, and who will be able to stand before Him?” ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) ha’yom, “the day,” m' charon, “from/ apo, “his/its nose, anger,” (n ms, 3ms ba, “he/it came,” u'mi, “and/ but/ so/ or who,” (interog yuchal, “he/it will (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, anger, indignation,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, la’amod, “to stand, to stop, stand still,” lefanav, “to his/its (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf him/it,” (prep, 3ms <note type="footnote" n="188">Hosea 10:8. 189 Compare to Luke 23:30.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.7">
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.1">Then after this, I saw four messengers standing upon the four corners of the earth, gripping the four winds190 of the earth in their hands, so that the wind would not be upon the earth nor upon the waters, nor on any tree.  The Scriptures: And after this I saw four messengers standing at the four corners of the earth, holding the four winds of the earth, that the wind should not blow on the earth, nor on the sea, nor on any tree.  Aramaic: And after these things I saw four angels, who stood on the four corners of the earth; and they held the four winds of the earth, so that the wind blew not on the earth, nor on the sea, nor on the trees. Idiom: "after this way" ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, arba, “four,” (card omdim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those messengers,” (n vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) Pa’al/Qal, act part, kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” arba, “four,” (card pinot, “corners, v'ochazim,”and/ byadam,” in/ with/ ha’arba, “the four of,” (card num) ruchot, “spirits,” (n corners of,” (n cp) but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those holding, gripping,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act by their hands,” (prep, n fs, 3mp k’dei, “be able, ti’h’yeh, “you (ms) shall be, become,’’ according to, as, in which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) breath, spirit,” (n order to,” (conj) yiqtol, fut, 2ms) ve’al, “and/ but/ so/ or upon, on,” (prep) ha’mayim,” the water,”’ (n mp) ve'al, “and/ but/ so/ or upon, on,” (prep) sum, “any,” (in a etz, “tree, wood (material), tree,” (n <note type="footnote" n="190">See Jeremiah 49:36 describing the “four winds.” 191 See Revelation 1:19 for first occurrence.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.2">And I saw another messenger who came from the east of the sun.  With him was the seal of the living and existing El.  He cried out with a great voice to the four messengers who were permitted to damage the earth and the sea.  The Scriptures: And I saw another messenger coming up from the rising of the sun, holding the seal of the living Elohim. And he cried with a loud voice to the four messengers to whom it was given to harm the earth and the sea,  Aramaic: And I saw another angel, and he came up from the rising of the sun; and he had the seal of the living God; and he called out, with a loud voice, to the four angels to whom it was given to hurt the earth and the sea, saying: v' ra'iti, “and/ but/ sheba, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you mi’miizrah, “from/ ha’shemesh, “the v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ so/ or I looked, another, different,” of (the) place of sunrise, east,” (n saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) him/it,” (prep, 3ms, Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’ya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ha’hachotem, “the meha’el, “from/ of chai, “live, alive, living,” (adj ms) v’kayam, “and/ but/ ve’tsaak, “he/it be’kol, “in/ with/ the El,” (prep, n so/ or existing,” shouted, cried,” (v. by (the) voice, sound,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, gadol, “big, large, great,” (adj ms) l’ha’arba, “to/ for/ belonging to the four,” (prep, card ha’noten, “I/ you (ms) / he/it (that) la’hem, “to/ for/ belonging to them,” damage, injure,” (v. messengers,” (n Hif’il, inf constr) Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’hayam, “and/ but/ so/ or the sea,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.3">He said, “Don’t damage the earth, nor the sea, nor even a tree, until I give a mark (tav)192 upon the foreheads193 of the servants194 of Yehovah.”  The Scriptures: saying, “Do not harm the earth, nor the sea, nor the trees until we have sealed the servants of our Elohim upon their foreheads.”  Aramaic: Hurt ye not the earth, nor the sea, nor the trees, until we shall have sealed the servants of our God upon their foreheads. va’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, al, “don’t,” (part) taziku, “you (mp) will damage,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, l’ha’eretz, “to/ for/ v’l’ha’yam, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) sea,” (prep, n ms) o, “or” (conj) l’etz, “to/ for/ belonging to the earth,” (prep, n fs) belonging to (the) tree,” (prep, n ms) ad, “until up to,” she’eteyn, “that/ tav, “musical note, avdei, “servants of,” (n mp, plural which/ who/ whom I (will) give,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) “foreheads,” (n mp) brand, mark, sign, judgment,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.4">Then I heard the number that was sealed. One hundred forty-four thousand were sealed of the clans196 of the children of Israel:197  The Scriptures: And I heard the number of those who were sealed, one hundred and forty-four thousand, sealed out of all the tribes of the children of Yisra’ĕl:  Aramaic: And I heard the number of them that were sealed, a hundred and forty and four thousand, sealed from every tribe of Israelites. ve’shamati, “and/ so/ but/ or that/ ha’mispar, “the number,” (n ms) me’eilu, “from/ of these, those, the following,” (prep, she’nech’temu, ha’ya,” he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, me’a, “hundred,” (n v’arba, “and/ but/ so/ or four,” (n fs) “that, which, who, which/ who/ whom I heard,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, whom he/it was signed, sealed, stamped” (rel part, v. Nif’al, qatal, v’arba’im, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) forty,” (n mp) mi’mishpachot, “from/ of (the) families, clans,” Israel (name) “thousands,” (n children of,” (n mp who/whom they were signed,” (rel part, v. Ni’fal, qatal, past, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.5">From the tribe of Judah were twelve thousand; from the tribe of Reuben were twelve thousand; from the tribe of Gad were twelve thousand. m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, Yehudah, “Judah,” shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, Reuven, “Reuben,” shenayim, “two” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n u’m’shevet, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, “Gad” (name) shenayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n <note type="footnote" n="196">Literally, “families or clans.” And the word for “tribe” is, (טבש) but in this case, I chose to use the word, “clans.” 197  It is important to note this is not “Jews only” as some Christian doctrines claim. The children of Israel include all the lost tribes of Israel and the foreigner who joins himself to Yehovah and becomes part of Israel. Consider numerous examples of foreigners who became part of Israel, including the new covenant: Genesis 14, 24, Exodus 2:16-21; 12:38; 30:33, 38, 31:14; Leviticus 7:20, 21, 25, 27; Numbers 32:12; Joshua 2:1-2; Ruth 4:13-16; 2 Samuel 11:3; 1 Chronicles 18:17; 22:2; 2 Chronicles 32:25; Isaiah e5e6:6-7; Jeremiah 31:31-33; 35; Ester 8:17; 9:27; Matthew 26:28; Mark 11:17 14;24; Luke 22:20; John 20:20; Acts 2:9-11; 13:16, 26, 16:14, 17:17; 1 Corinthians 11:25, 2 Corinthians 3:6, Hebrews 8:6-13, 9:15, 10:16, 29, 12:24.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.6">From the tribe of Asher were twelve thousand. From the tribe of Naphtali were twelve thousand. From the tribe of Manasseh were twelve thousand.  The Scriptures: of the tribe of Ashĕr twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Naphtali twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Menashsheh twelve thousand were sealed,  Aramaic: of the tribe of Ashur, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Naphtali, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Manasseh, twelve thousand: mi’shavet, “from/ “Asher,” (name) she’nayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n “m’shevet, “‘from/ “Naphtali,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.7">From the tribe of Simeon were twelve thousand. From the tribe of Levi were twelve thousand.  From the tribe of Issachar were twelve thousand.  The Scriptures: of the tribe of Shim‛on twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Lĕwi twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Yissasḵar twelve thousand were sealed,  Aramaic: of the tribe of Simeon, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Levi, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Issachar, twelve thousand: m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep n “Simeon,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, “Levi,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n m’shevet, “and/ “Issachar,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card but/ so/ or from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, elef, “thousand,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.8">From the tribe of Zebulun were twelve thousand.  From the tribe of Joseph were twelve thousand.  From the tribe of Benjamin were twelve thousand.198  The Scriptures: of the tribe of Zeḇulun twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Yosĕph twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Binyamin twelve thousand were sealed.  Aramaic: of the tribe of Zebulon, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Joseph, twelve thousand: of the tribe of Benjamin, twelve thousand. m’shevet, “from/ of (the) tribe,” (prep, “Zebulun,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n u’m'shevet, “from/ “Joseph,” (name) shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n u’m'shevet, “from/ shanayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.9">Then after this, I saw a great multitude that no one199 could number, from all the nations standing before the throne and before the Lamb, wearing white garments, with branches in their hands.  The Scriptures: After this I looked and saw a great crowd which no one was able to count, out of all nations and tribes and peoples and tongues, standing before the throne and before the Lamb, dressed in white robes, and palm branches in their hands, ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, gdula, “greatness, importance,” (adj yuchal, “he/it will Idiom: "after this way" “company, circle of which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) association,” (n ms) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” lispor, “to count, m’chol, “from/ of (the) all,” (prep, n omdim, “we/ you (mp / they, those v’lifnei, “and/ but/ peoples, nations,” before the face of, before me, in front throne,” (n ms) so/ or before, in front of, before (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf (v. Pa’al/Qal act ha’se, “the lamb,” ve’lovshim, “and/ so/ but/ or to/ for/ belonging to we/ you (mp) / they, those wearing,” be'me'levushim, “in/ with/ by (the) garments,” (prep, n levinim, “white,” u’ye’de’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ anafim, “branches,” by their hands,”  (prep n fp, 3mp (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, <note type="footnote" n="198">The tribe of Dan is not mentioned. See Genesis 49:17 and Judges 18:303-31 for more details. 199 Literally, “he/it will not be able to count.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.10">They cried out with a great voice, saying, “Salvation belongs to Yehovah, and to the Lamb!”  The Scriptures: and crying out with a loud voice, saying, “Deliverance belongs to our Elohim who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!”  Aramaic: and they cried, with a loud voice, saying: Salvation to our God, to him who sitteth on the throne, and to the Lamb. ve'tzo’akim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those be'kol, “in/ with/ by (the) sound, voice,” gadol, “big, large, great,” (adj ms) v’omrim, “and/ but/ la’Yehovah,” to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, ha'yeshua, “the salvation,” (n fs) v’l’ha’se, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) lamb,” (prep, n ms) (mp)/ they, those (v. Pa’al/Qal, act (v. Pa’al/Qal, act <note type="footnote" n="200">See Revelation 1:19 for first occurrence.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.11">And all standing before the throne, the messengers, the elders, and the living creatures, fallen on their faces before the throne, praying to Yehovah,  The Scriptures: And all the messengers stood around the throne and the elders and the four living creatures, and fell on their faces before the throne and worshipped Elohim,  Aramaic: And all the angels stood around the throne and the Elders and the four Animals; and they fell upon their faces before his throne, and worshipped God, ve' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) ha’mal’achim, “the omdim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those saviv, “around,” le'kise, “to/ for/ belonging to the throne,” (prep, n ve'he'zkanim, “and/ but/ so/ or the elders,” “and/ but/ so/ or messengers,” (n (v. Pa’al/ act part, ve'noflim, “and/ so/ pneihem, “their face(s),” (n mp, 3mp pronom) ha'kise, “the throne,” (n ms) u’mitpalelim, “and/ but/ so /or (the) we/ you (mp)/ they those laYehovah, “to/ for/ belonging to but/ or we/ you (mp) they, those before the face of, before me, in front (v. Pa’al/Qal, act Hit’pael, act part, mp) <note type="footnote" n="201">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.12">saying, “Praise and thanksgiving, adoration, honor, glory, power, and strength be to our Elohim forever to ever. Amen!”   The Scriptures: saying, “Amĕn! The blessing, and the esteem, and the wisdom, and the thanksgiving, and the respect, and the power, and the might, to our Elohim forever and ever. Amĕn.”  Aramaic: saying: Amen. Blessing, and glory, and wisdom, and thanksgiving, and honor, and power, and might, [be] to our God, for ever and ever: Amen. ve'omrim, “and/ sha’beach, “(to a man) Praise!” (v. Pi’el, imp, 2ms) ve’hoda’a, ‘and/ ve'tehilot, “and/ ve’cavod, “and/ ve'tif’eret, “and/ but/ so/ or glory,” ve’koach, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those but/ so/ or praises’ but/ so/ or honor,” but/ so/ or power,” thanksgiving,” (n (v. Pa’al/Qal, act ve’gvura,”and/ but/ so/ or (the) valor, strength,” (n fs) tihye, “you will le’eloheinu, “to/ for/ belonging to me’olam, “from/ of everlasting,” (prep, be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2ms) but/so/or until, up “everlasting,” (n (prep, n mp, 1cp</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.13">Then one of the elders answered and said to me, “Who are these dressed in white garments?  From what place do they come?”  The Scriptures: And one of the elders responded, saying to me, “Who are these dressed in white robes, and where did they come from?”  Aramaic: And one of the Elders turned, and said to me: These who are clothed in white robes, who are they, and whence came they? va’ya’an, “and/ but/ mi, “who?” (inter eilu, “these, those, so/ or he/it will belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) the following,” (3mp pronom) elders,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) ha’lovshim, “the ba’m’levushim, levanim, “white,” uma’eize, “and/ makom, “place,” (n ba’im, “we/ you (mp)/ they/ those who come,” (v. he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, we/ you (mp) /they, “in/ with/ by from/ of (the) garments,” but/ so/ or from/ of those wearing,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act which, what?”  (prep, pron ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.14">I said to Him, “Master, You know.” And He said to me, “These are those coming out of the midst of much sorrow. They have washed and purified their garments by the blood of the Lamb.”  The Scriptures: And I said to him, “Master, you know.” And he said to me, “These are those coming out of the great distress, having washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.  Aramaic: And I said to him: My lord, thou knowest. And he said to me: These are they who came from great affliction; and they have washed their robes, and made them white in the blood of the Lamb v’amarti, “and/ but/ ata, “you (ms),” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, act eilu, “these, those, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, ha’ba’im, “next, coming,” (adj mp) mi’tokh, “from/ of har’beh, “many, tza’ar, “sadness,” belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) the following,” (3mp pronom) va’rachatzu, “and/ b'gdeihem, “in/ v' zqaqu, “and/ but/ so/ or they distilled, purified,” (v. Pi'el, qatal, past, 3mp) b'gdeihem, “in/ badam, “in/ with/ ha’se, “the lamb,” but/ so/ or they with/ by their piece with/ by their piece (of),” (prep, n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.15">For this reason, they are before the throne of Yehovah and shall serve Him day and night. And this One sitting upon the throne will dwell among them.  The Scriptures: “Because of this they are before the throne of Elohim, and serve Him day and night in His Dwelling Place. And He who sits on the throne shall spread his Tent over them.  Aramaic: Therefore are they before the throne of God; and they serve him day and night, in his temple; and he who sitteth on the throne, will protect them: ve’bishvil, “and/ but/ so/ or for, for the sake of,” (prep) ze, “this,” (pron, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, ha’ kise, “the throne,” (n ms) Yehovah veshertu, “and/ but/ so/ or they served,” before the face of, before me, in front oto, “him/it,” (DO yom, “day,” (n ms) v’layla, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) night,” ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, she’yashav, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it sat, dwelled, ha’ kise, “the throne,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, tadur, “you (ms) aleihem, “upon them,” (prep, 3 mp yiqtol, fut, 2ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.16">She204 will not hunger, nor thirst, nor be afflicted by the scorching heat and sun!205  The Scriptures: “They shall hunger no more, neither thirst any more, neither shall the sun strike them, nor any heat,  Aramaic: they will not hunger, nor thirst any more; nor will the sun fall on them, nor any heat. v'hi, “and/ but/ so/ lo, “no, not,” (neg yir’avu, “they (m) will be hungry,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not,” (neg part) yitzme’u, “they (m) will have lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not,” (neg part) yakem, “he/it shall (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut yiqtol, fut, 3mp) sha’rav, “heat, scorch,” (n ms) v’she’mesh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.7.17">For the Lamb shall lead them to a well of waters, and Yehovah Elohim will wipe the tear from all faces.  The Scriptures: because the Lamb who is in the midst of the throne shall shepherd them and lead them to fountains of waters of life. And Elohim shall wipe away every tear from their eyes.”  Aramaic: Because the Lamb, which is in the midst of the throne, will feed them; and will lead them to fountains of living water; and God will wipe every tear from their eyes. ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) ha’se, “the lamb,” ye’na’hagen, “he/ it otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) la’be’er,”to/ for/ belonging to (the) well, pit, spring,” ma’yim, “waters,” u’ma’chah, “and/ but/ so/ or shall shall lead them,” (v. Pi'el, yiqtol, fut, wipe out, blot out,” 3ms, 3mp, obj) (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf dim’ah, “tear,” (n me’al, “from/ of upon, on” (prep) kol, “all,” (n ms) panim, “face, faces,” (n fp) Elohim, “God,” (n <note type="footnote" n="204">Isaiah 39:10 has been translated to be, "They will not hunger nor thirst.” 205 Isiah 49:10.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.8">
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.1">And when he opened the seventh, all were silent in the heavens for a while.  The Scriptures: And when He opened the seventh seal, there came to be silence in the heaven for about half an hour.  Aramaic: And when he had opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven, for about half an hour. v' kevan, “and/ but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” she'patach, “that/ which/ who/ whom b’shamayim, “in/ with/ by (the) heavens,” Idiom: “for a while” seventh,” (adj ms) which/ who/ whom we/ you (mp)/ they them,” (n mp, 3mp k' sha'a, “just as, like/ as an hour,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, part, v. Pa’al/Qal, chad, “one, or single, sharp,” (adj ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.2">I saw seven messengers coming before Yehovah and they were given seven shofars.  The Scriptures: And I saw the seven messengers who stand before Elohim, and to them were given seven trumpets.  Aramaic: And I saw the seven angels, who stood before God; and to them were given, seven trumpets. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, shiv’a, “seven,” mal’achim, “messengers, angels,” (n mp) ba’im, “we/ you (mp)/ they (m)/ v’le’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to them,” before the face of, before me, in front those who come,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act noten, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is given,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part shiv’a, “seven,” shofarot, “shofars,” <note type="footnote" n="207">Daniel 4:16 Jewish Publication Society (JPS) translates this idiom as,” for a while.” This form of דח "one" is found in the First Century Targum Onkelos Genesis 1:15.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.3">Another messenger came walking near to the holy place and in his hand was a censer of gold. He was given much incense to deliver prayers for the holy ones before the holy place and before the throne.  The Scriptures: And another messenger came and stood at the slaughter-place, holding a golden censer, and much incense was given to him, that he should offer it with the prayers of all the set-apart ones upon the golden slaughter-place which was before the throne.  Aramaic: And another angel came and stood by the altar; and he held a golden censer: and much incense was given him, so that he might offer, with the prayers of all the saints, upon the golden altar before the throne. acher, “another,” ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),”  (v. Pa’al/Qal, act v’ darach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/ it etzel, “at, in the possession of, near,” (prep) ha’hekal, “the holy u’v’’yado, “and/ “and/ but/ so/ or but/ so/ or in/ with/ by his/its hand,” messenger,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mach’tot, “censors, shel, “of, belonging ‘zahav, “gold,” (n ve’lo, “and/ but/ so/ noten, “I/ you (ms)/ 'ha' rabah, “greatly, ke’toret, “incense,” firepans,” (n fp) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act him/it,” (prep, 3ms le’tfilat, “to/for (the) prayer of,” (prep n fs constr) ha’hechal, “the v’lifnei, “and/ but/ ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) “saints, holy ones,” before the face of, before me, in front holy place,” (n ms) so/or before, in front of, before <note type="footnote" n="208">The scribe uses nikkudot (vowel points) for emphasis and clarity.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.4">The smoke from the incense of the holy ones went up from the hand of the messenger before Yehovah.  The Scriptures: And the smoke of the incense, with the prayers of the set-apart ones, went up before Elohim from the hand of the messenger.  Aramaic: And the smoke of the incense of the prayers of the saints went up before God from the hand of the angel. v’ha’ashan, “and/ m’ ha’ke’toret, “from/ of the hakdoshim, “saint, mi’yad, “from/ of ha’mal’ach, “the angel, messenger,” lifnei, “before, in front of, before but/ so/ or the smoke,” (n ms) incense,” (prep, n hallowed,” (adj Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Yehovah</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.5">The messenger took the censer and filled it with fire and poured it out upon the earth and then came the sounds of thunders and lightnings! v’ha’mal’ach, “and/ v’mile, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it filled,” oto, “him/it,” (DO b’esh, “in/ with/ by (the) fire,” (prep, n v’yitzak “and/ but/ so/ or he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “censor,” (n fs) angel, messenger,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, 3ms) u’bo, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it came,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) uverokim, “and/ “and/ but/ so/ or (the) thunders,” (n lightnings,” (n mp) <note type="footnote" n="209">This is a unique spelling, see Revelation 2:17 for more details.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.6">Then the seven messengers with the seven shofars prepared to blow.  The Scriptures: And the seven messengers who held the seven trumpets prepared themselves to sound.  Aramaic: And the seven angels, who had the seven trumpets, prepared themselves to sound. v’ha’shiv’a, “and/ ‘im, “with,” (prep) ha’shiv’a, “the seven,” (card shofarot, “shofars,” hayu, “they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, muchanim, “we/ you (mp)/ they are prepared,” (v. Hif’il messengers,” (n pssv part, 3mp) litkoa, “to blow,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.7">The first messenger blew, and there was hail and fire mixed with blood. Then it fell upon the earth, and a third of the trees burned, and all the greenery of the field burned.   The Scriptures: And the first messenger sounded, and there came to be hail and fire mixed with blood, and they were thrown to the earth. And a third of the trees were burned up, and all green grass was burned up.  Aramaic: And the first sounded; and there was hail, and fire, which were mingled with water: and these were thrown upon the earth; and a third part of the earth was burned up, and a third part of the trees were burned, and all green grass was burned. v’ha’mal’ach, “and/ tokea, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it blow(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve’ha’yah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it barad, “hail,” (n v’eysh, “and/ but/ so/ or fire,” (n fs) angel, messenger,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, b’dam, “in/ with/ by (the) blood,” v’nafal, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it fell,” (v. v’shlish, “and/ but/ mha’etzim, “from/ of the trees,” (prep, nisraf, “he/it was burnt,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms) so/ or (the) third Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’kol, “and/ but/ so/ yerok, “green,” (n nisraf, “he/it was burnt,” (v Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.8">The second blew, and something like a great mountain, burned with fire, then went into the sea, and a third of the sea was blood.   The Scriptures: And the second messenger sounded, and what looked like a great mountain burning with fire was thrown into the sea, and a third of the sea became blood, v’ha’sheyni, “and/ ve’ha’yah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it c' har, "as/ like (the) mountain" gadol, “big, large, great,” (adj ms) saraf, “he/it was ba’eysh, “in/ with/ second,” (adj ms) was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (v. Pa’al/Qal, act qatal, past, 3ms) v ’halach, “and/ ba’yam, “in (the) v’shlish, “and/ but/ ha’yam, “the sea,” haya, “he/it was,” dam, “blood,” (n but/ so he/it went,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, so/ or (the) third qatal, past, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.9">And a third of the creatures of the sea were put to death, and a third of the ships were sunk.  The Scriptures: and a third of the living creatures in the sea died, and a third of the ships were destroyed.  Aramaic: And a third part of all the creatures in the sea, that had life, died; and a third part of the ships were destroyed. v’shlish, “and/ but/ m’berot “of/ from (the) creatures,” ha’yam, “the sea,” v’shlish,”and/ but so/ or (the) third ma’sfinot, “ships,” nishfarim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those swamped,” (v. Nif’al, act part, so/ or (the) third them to death,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, 3ms, 3mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="210">The word,  עבש (shafa) means “to be full,” or “swamped.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.10">Then the third blew, and a star burned and fell from the heavens upon a third of the springs of water,  The Scriptures: And the third messenger sounded, and a great star fell from the heaven, burning like a torch, and it fell on a third of the rivers and on the fountains of water,  Aramaic: And the third angel sounded, and there fell from heaven a star, burning like a lamp; and it fell upon a third part of the rivers, and upon the fountains of water. v’ha’’shlishi, “and/ tokea “I/ you (ms)/ he/it blow(s)” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’nafal, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it fell,” (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kokhav, “a star,” (n echad, “one,” (card mi’shamayim, “of/ ve’saraf, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it burned,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or the third,” (adj ms) heavens,” (n mp) v’nafal, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it fell,” (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, shlish, “third part,” ha’be'erot, “the mayim, “water,” (n wells, the springs,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.11">and the name of the star was Scarlet.  A third of the waters became bitter. And because of its bitterness, many of the children of man died.   The Scriptures: and the name of the star is called Wormwood. And a third of the waters became wormwood, and many men died from the waters, because they were made bitter.  Aramaic: And the name of the star was called Wormwood; and a third part of the waters became wormwood; and many persons died from the waters, because they were bitter. v’’shem, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) name,” ha’kochav, “the haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’shlish, “and/ but/ haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, “scarlet, worm,” (n so/ or (the) third mar, “bitter,” (adj harbe, “and/ but/ so/ or very many,” metim, “we/ you (mp) /they, those ha’mayim, “the water(s),” (n mp) children of,” (n mp, Idiom: al’yadei, “by the hand of.” Pa’al/Qal, act part, mipnei’, “from/ of, away from,” (prep) mroreihem, “their bitternesses,” (n mp, 3mp pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.12">The fourth blew, and a third part of the sun, moon, and the stars eclipsed, and a third of the day did not shine, nor the night.  The Scriptures: And the fourth messenger sounded, and a third of the sun was struck, and a third of the moon, and a third of the stars, so that a third of them were darkened. And a third of the day did not shine, and likewise the night.  Aramaic: And the fourth angel sounded, and a third part of the sun was smitten, and the third part of the moon, and the third part of the stars; so that the third part of them were dark, and they became dark; and the day did not give light for the third part of it, and the night in like manner. ve’ha’revi’i, “and/ tokaya’a, “I/ you v’nilke, “he/it was struck, eclipsed, hashlish, “the third,” (adj ms) m’ha’semesh, “of/ ha’yarech, “and/ v’kochavim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) stars,” (n mp) fourth,” (adj ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part, (v. Nif’al, qatal, v’shlish, “and/ but/ m’ha’yom, “of/ from the day,” (prep, n ms) lo, “no/not,” (part) v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” so/ or (the) third (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.8.13">Then I saw and heard a messenger hovering in the heavens, and he shouted with a great voice, “Woe! Woe! Woe to those dwelling upon the earth, because the voice of the shofars - which are required - are yet to be blown from the three messengers!”  The Scriptures: And I looked, and I heard an eagle flying in mid-heaven, crying with a loud voice, “Woe, woe, woe to those dwelling upon the earth, because of the remaining blasts of the trumpet of the three messengers who are about to sound!”  Aramaic: And I saw and heard an eagle, which flew in the midst, and it had a tail of blood, while it said, with a loud voice: Woe, woe, to them who dwell on the earth, because of the remaining sounds of the trumpets of the three angels, who are to sound. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ve’shamati, “and/ so/ but/ or that/ echad, “one,” (card b’shamayim, “in/ v’tza’ak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it cried, hovered, floated,” which/ who/ whom heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ba’kol, “in/ with/ by (the) sound, gadol, “big, large,” oyi, “woe!” (interj oyi, “woe!” (interj oyi, “woe!” (interj belonging to these, voice,” (prep, n ms) dwelling,” (adj ms) following,” (prep, mipnei, “of/ from, away from, from before,” (prep) ha’kol, “the voice, the sound, clarion ha’shofarot, “the shofars,” (n mp) she’tzrichim, “that/ which/ who/ whom required,” (adj mp) litkoa, “to blow,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf ha’shlosha, “the malachim, “angels/ three,” (card numb) messengers,” (n</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.9">
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.1">The fifth messenger blew, and I saw a star fall upon the earth from the heavens.  And he was given the key to the deep.  The Scriptures: And the fifth messenger sounded, and I saw a star from the heaven which had fallen to the earth. And the key to the pit of the deep was given to him.  Aramaic: And the fifth angel sounded; and I saw a star, which fell from heaven upon the earth. And there was given to him the key of the pit of the abyss. v’ha’mal’ach,” and/ ha’ḥamishi, “the fifth,” (ord num) ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kokhav, “a star,” nafal, “he/it fell,” angel, messenger,” qatal, past, 3ms) ve’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or belonging to him/it,” (prep, 3ms noten, “I/ you (ms)/ ha’mafteach, “the m’tehom, “from/ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act deep,” (prep, n fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.2">He opened the deep, and smoke went out from the deep like smoke from a large furnace, the sun and the air darkened from the smoke of the deep.   The Scriptures: And he opened the pit of the deep, and smoke went up out of the pit like the smoke of a great furnace. And the sun was darkened, also the air, because of the smoke of the pit.  Aramaic: And he opened the pit of the abyss; and smoke issued from the pit, like the smoke of a furnace that is in blast; and the sun and the air were darkened by the smoke of the pit. v’patach, “then, and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it, v’yatsa, “and/ but so/ or he/it went ashan, “smoke,” m’tehom, “from/ k’mo, “like, as, ashan, “smoke,” out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, deep,” (prep, n fs) qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal m’tanur. “furnace, gadol, “big, large, v’ha’choshech, “and/ but/ so/ or the darkness,” v’ha’avir, “and/ “the sun,” (n ms) but/ so/ or the air,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.3">From the smoke came frogs213 upon the earth, and they were given authority to annihilate to destroy.  The Scriptures: And out of the smoke locusts came upon the earth, and authority was given to them as the scorpions of the earth possess authority.  Aramaic: And out of the smoke, came locusts upon the earth: and power was given them, like that which scorpions have on the earth. (lak’avat) means, "consumption of, to exhaust, to end, to annihilate."  And there is no associated marginal note. Pageview Image MS Oo.1.16.2 bo’im, “we / you (ms) / they come, coming, came,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act tzafradi'im, frogs,” v’lahem, “and/ but/ noten “I/ you (ms)/ “and/ but/ so/ or he/it give(s)” (v Pa’al/Qal, act part smoke,” (prep, n them,” (prep, 3mp l' klay'at, to the “authority,” (n fs) annihilation of, to the extinction (n fs</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.4">They were told, “Do not damage the plants or the green grass of the field, nor any tree.  Injure only the children of mankind who do not have the seal of Yehovah in their foreheads.” ne’emar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it le’yerek , “to/ for/ belonging to (the) ule’esev, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) “to/ for/ pertaining which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) “you will damage, was said, was told” injure, corrupt, hurt, trouble” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, (v. Nif’al, qatal, vegetation,” (prep added mater lectionis o’, ‘or’ (conj)  la’ayts, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) tree,” (prep n ms) rak, “only, just,” levad, “alone, by itself, this only, except,” (adv) l’ benei, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) children, sons of,” (prep, n mp constr) which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) la’hem, “to/ for/ b' mitzcheihem,  “in/ with/ by their there exists, (part) “the signature of, Yehovah,” (prep, added mater lectionis added mater lectionis</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.5">They (the frogs/locusts) were not given authority to kill them, but only to grieve them for five months.  And their grief was like the pain when scorpions bite.  The Scriptures: And it was given to them that they should not kill them, but to torture them for five months. And their torture was like the torture of a scorpion when it stings a man  Aramaic: And it was given them, that they should not kill them, but should torment them five months: and their torment was like the torment of a scorpion, when it striketh a person. noten, “I/ you (ms)/ lo, “no/not,” (neg lehamit, “to kill, to cause to die,” (v. Hif’il, inf constr) otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) rak, “only, just,” l’tza'er, “to sadden, disappoint, bring grief,” (v. Pi’el, inf but/ so/ or to/ for/ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act them,” (prep, 3mp otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) chamisha, “five,” k’ tza'ar, “like/ as (the) grief, pain, “months,” (n mp) “and/ but/ so/ or their grief, pain, sorrow,” (n mp) “scorpions,” (n pa’al/Qal, qatal, b'im, “if, when, whether,” (prep, she' nosheke, "I/ you/ he/it bites (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.6">In those days, you would be wiser to die, but not find it!  The Scriptures: And in those days men shall seek death and shall not find it. And they shall long to die, but death shall flee from them.  Aramaic: And in those days, men will desire death, and will not find it; and they will long to die, and death will fly from them. uva’yamim“and/ but/ so/ or in/ with /by the days,” (n ha’he’ma, “the tachakmu, "you lamut, “to die,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf v’ lo, “not, no” they, these, those,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, yiqtol, fut, 2ms),</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.7">The locusts220 are like the horses poised for battle.221  Upon their heads were crowns as of gold, their appearance like the appearance of mankind.  The Scriptures: And the locusts looked like horses prepared for battle, and on their heads were crowns like gold, and their faces were like the faces of men.  Aramaic: And the appearance of the locusts [was this]; they were like the appearance of horses prepared for battle; and on their heads, was, as it were a coronet, resembling gold; and their faces were like the faces of men. v' arav'im, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they liers-in-wait, ambushers,” (v. Pi'el, act part, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, k’mo, “like, as, ha’susim,” the horses,” (n mp) v’al, “and/ but/ so/ “ready, prepared,” “to/ for/ belonging “locusts,” (n mp) roshhem, “their heads,” (n mp, 3 cadmut, “like/ as,” kitrei, “crowns of” um’reihem, “and/ but/ so/ or their appearance,” (n (prep, n pl constr)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.8">Their hair like the hair of women, and their teeth, like the teeth of a lion,227  The Scriptures: And they had hair like women’s hair, and their teeth were like lions’ teeth.  Aramaic: And they had hair, like the hair of women: and their teeth were like those of lions. ha’nashim, “the v’shinav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its k’ shenai “just as, as/ like (the) teeth of,” (prep, n mp arye, “lion,” (n “just as, like/ as (the) hairs of,” (n mp, 3mp pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.9"/>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.10">and their rears were like the tails of a swarm. They were given authority to grieve the children of mankind for five months.  The Scriptures: And they have tails like scorpions, and stings. And in their tails is their authority to harm men five months.  Aramaic: And they had tails like those of scorpions, and stings; and with their tails they had the power of hurting men five months. arbeh, “swarm, locust, multitude devastation,” (n lahem, “to /for/ by/ “and/ but/ so/ or their tails, rear” (n mp, 3mp pronom) “as/ like (the) tails (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) (prep, n mp constr) (prep, pron 3mp) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act Note: should be: chamisha, “five,” sadden, disappoint, sons, children,” (n “months,” (n mp) afflict,” (v. Pi’el,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.11">Their king was a messenger from the deep.  His name in the Hebrew language, Abaddon, and in the Greek language, Apollyon.234  The Scriptures: And they have over them a sovereign, the messenger of the pit of the deep, whose name in Hebrew is Abaddon, but in Greek he has the name Apolluon.  Aramaic: And they had a king over them, the angel of the abyss; and his name, in Hebrew, is Abaddon; and in Greek, his name is Apollyon. umelek, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) king, sovereign,” (n ms) she’l’ahem, “that/ which/ who/ whom to them, belonging haya, “he/it was,” m’tehom, “from/ u’shmo, “and/ but/ (v.  Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) deep,” (prep, n fs) name,” (n ms, 3ms to them,” (pron ba’la’shon, “in/ with/ by (the) ivri, “Hebrew,” (n u’valashon, "and/ but/ so/ or in the tongue, and by (the) tongue,” (n ya’van, “Greece,” language, tongue,” messenger of the bottomless pit,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.12">Something like a cloud236 passed,237 and behold, the second is coming as clouds!  The Scriptures: The first woe is past. See, two woes are still coming after this. ehad, “one,” (card re'e! “(to a man) k’avim,” like/ as (the) cloud, a dark Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp baim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="234">John, having been in the regions of modern-day Turkey and Greece, would have known some Greek.  Josephus did the same kind of writing style.  See The War of the Jews 5:4:2 - "This new-built part of the city was called "Bezetha," in our language, which, if interpreted in the Grecian language, may be called "the New City." – William Whiston, translator.  However, the added vowel markers (nikkud) would indicate this was added later. 235 Transliteration from the Greek Apollyon.  The scribes chose to include nikkudot (vowel markings) for correct pronunciation. 236 See Ezekiel 1:4 describing a wind coming from the north, a “great cloud” before Yehovah revealed Himself brilliantly like a rainbow and cloud (Ezekiel 1:27-28) before pronouncing judgment upon the children of Israel. 237 The Hebrew words used are “like/as dark storm clouds,” a simile for “more trouble is coming.” The use of a metaphor like "dark cloud" for "woe" shows the writer has familiarity with Hebrew.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.13">And the sixth messenger blew.  I heard a voice coming from the four corners of the holy place that is before Yehovah,  The Scriptures: And the sixth messenger sounded, and I heard a voice from the four horns of the golden slaughter-place which is before Elohim,  Aramaic: And the sixth angel sounded; and I heard a voice from the horns of the golden altar which was before God, v’ha’mal’ach, “and/ but/ so/ or ha’shishi, “the sixth,” (ord num) taka “he/it blew,” kol, “voice, noise, sound, thunder,” (n m’arba, “from/ of “and/ but/ so/ or I qatal, past, 3ms) (prep, ord num) messenger,” (n ms) pinot, “corners,” (n “the holy place,” before the face of, before me, in front</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.14">saying to the sixth messenger who blew, “Go, and search for the four bound messengers in the great sea241 called, 'Euphrates.'”  The Scriptures: saying to the sixth messenger who had the trumpet, “Release the four messengers, those having been bound at the great river Euphrates.”  Aramaic: that said to the sixth angel having a trumpet: Loose the four angels that are bound at the great river Euphrates. v’omeret, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (fs) / she/it say(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act le’ha’mal'ach, “to/ for/ belonging to she’taqa, “that/ lech! “(to a man) Go!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, v’chapes! “and/ but/ so/ or (to a man) Search!” (v. Pi’el, imp, le’ha’arba, “to/ for/ sixth,” (ord numb) which/ who/ whom belonging to the fourth,” (prep, ord Pa’al/Qal, qatal, etsel,”by, beside, ha’yam, “the sea,” ha’gadol, “the great,” (adj ms) ha’nikra, “the I/ you (ms)/ he/it is named,” (v. Nif’al, “the they, those messengers,” (n imprisoned,” (n transliteration of</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.15">The four messengers were prepared to kill a third part244 of the children of mankind in an hour, in a day, in a month, and in one year.  The Scriptures: And the four messengers, those having been prepared for the hour and day and month and year, were released to kill a third of mankind.  Aramaic: And the four angels were loosed; who are prepared, for an hour, and a day, and a month, and a year, to slay the third part of men. ve’ha’arba, “and/ hayu, “they were,” mukanim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those prepared,” (v. Hof’al pssv lehamit, “to kill, to cause to die,” (v. Hif'il, inf constr) ha’shlish, “the third part,” (ord m’ benei, “from/ or (the) children, sons,” (prep, n mp four,” (card num) messengers,” (n qatal, past, 3mp) b’ sha’a, “in/ with/ by (the) hour, in the time,” (prep, n u' b’yom, “and/ “and/ but/ so/ or/ in (the) month,” “and/ but/ so/ or in (the) year,” (n fs) “one,” (card numb) day,” (prep, n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.16">And their riders were numbered a great many245 thousands. And I heard their number.  The Scriptures: And the number of the armies of the horsemen was two hundred million, and I heard the number of them.  Aramaic: And the number of the warrior horsemen was two myriads of myriads: and I heard their number. v’rochveihem “and/ but/ so/ or their riders, their haya, “he/it was,” misparam, “from/ of their numbers,” (prep,n mp 3mp mis’pa’ram, “their “and/ but/ so/ or I qatal, past, 3ms) numerous,” (adj (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) <note type="footnote" n="244">See Ezekiel 5:12. 245 This word could also be translated as "myriad" or "ten thousand," but the context seems to indicate a great many (a thousand upon thousand). Therefore, it was translated as "great many" to indicate this large number. See Psalm 68:18.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.17">After this, I saw the horses in formation and those sitting upon them wearing garments of pitch, brimstone, and fire. The heads of the horses were like the heads of a lion, and from the horses' mouths went fire, smoke, and brimstone.  The Scriptures: And this is how I saw the horses in the vision and those who sat on them, having breastplates of fiery red, and hyacinth blue, and sulphur yellow. And the heads of the horses were like the heads of lions, and out of their mouths came fire, and smoke, and sulphur.  Aramaic: And while I looked on the horses in the vision, and on them who sat on them [I saw] that the breastplates were of fire, and of jacinth, and of sulphur. And the heads of the horses were like the heads of lions; and from their mouths issued fire, and smoke, and sulphur. Idiom: "after this way" ha’ susim, “the horses,” (n mp) v’ha’yoshvim, “and/ but/ so/ or those sitting, the sitters,” (n mp) “in/ with/ by (the) form of, design of, them,” (prep, 3mp vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) (prep, n fs constr) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” she’hehye, “that/ which/ who/ whom l’hem, “to/ for/ belonging to “of,” (prep) zefet, “tar, pitch” v’gofrit, “and/ but/ “and/ but/ so/ or (the) fire,” (n ms) them,” (prep, 3mp (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) v’roshei’, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ha’susim, “the horses,” (n mp) u’m’pi’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of eysh, “fire,” (n fs) “as/ like (the) heads,” (prep, n heads of…,” (n mp Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (prep n mp, 3ms v’ashan, “and/ but/ so/ or smoke,” (n “and/ but/ so/ or <note type="footnote" n="246">See Revelation 1:19 for first use.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.18">And by these three (fire, smoke, brimstone) a third part of the children of mankind were killed,   The Scriptures: A third of mankind was killed by these three plagues, by the fire and the smoke and the sulphur which came out of their mouths.  Aramaic: And by these three plagues, a third part of the men were slain; [namely,] by the fire, and by the smoke, and by the sulphur, which issued from their mouths. um’eylo,”and/ but/ ha’shlosha, “the ha'shlish “the third m’benei, “from/ or adam, “man,” (n so/ or from/ of these, those, the following,” (prep “I/ you (ms)/ he/it part,” (ord num) sons,” (prep, n mp (v. Nif’al, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.19">for their power was in their mouths, and their tails had heads like serpents, with which they kill.  The Scriptures: For the authority of the horses is in their mouth and in their tails, for their tails are like serpents, having heads. And with them they do harm.  Aramaic: For the power of the horses was in; their mouth, and in their tails; for their tails were like serpents, having heads to strike with. ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) kocham, “their strength, power, haya, “he/it was,” v’pihem, “in/ by/ with their mouth,” (prep, n ms, 3mp uzenavihem, “and/ haya, “he/it was,” rashim, “heads, (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) but/ so/ or their (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) chiefs, leaders,” (n force,” (n ms, 3mp c’na’khashim, “as/ v’roshim, “and/ haya, “he/it was,” u’ve’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by these,” (prep, pron, ha’oragim, “the, that we/ you (mp)/ otam, “them,” (DO like snakes, like serpents” (prep, n but/ so/ or heads,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) them,” (prep, 3mp they, those who kill,” (v. Pa’al/Qal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.20">However, there were many children of mankind who will not be put to death by these plagues,251 because they repented252 of their evil works. They did not pray to Satan nor to idols of clay, stone, wood, silver, or gold - which are not able to walk or speak or hear.  The Scriptures: And the rest of mankind, who were not killed by these plagues, did not repent of the works of their hands, that they should not worship the demons, and idols of gold, and of silver, and of brass, and of stone, and of wood, which are neither able to see, nor to hear, nor to walk.  Aramaic: And the residue of men who were not slain by these plagues, repented not of the works of their hands, so as not to worship demons, and idols of gold, and of silver, and brass, and stone, and wood, which cannot see, nor hear. haya,” he/it was,” harbeh,” many, children of,” (n mp which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) qatal, past, 3ms) however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay yumtu, “they will not be killed, put to death,” (Hif'il, pssv, yiqtol, fut, eilu, “these, those, ha’nega’im, “the strokes, plagues, diseases, marks, bishvil, “for the Idiom: “they repented” Idiom: v' al’yadei, “by the hand of,” the following,” (3mp pronom) sake of, according she’asu “that/ which/ who/ whom they did, made,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, marks of leprosy,” tshuva, “repentance,” (n fs) ha’ra’im, “bad, evil,” (adj, mp) u’mitpallim, “and/ l’hasatan, “to/ for/ belonging to the satan, adversary,” v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ but/ so /or (the) we/ you (mp)/ they Hit’pael, act part, u’m’ehven, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of (the) stone,” (prep, o, “or” (conj) me’etz\,” from/ of (the) wood,” (prep v’kesef, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) silver,” abbreviation for “the I/ you (ms)/ he/it become(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, clay, earthenware” to idolatry or idols.” (prep, n v’zahav, “and/ but/ ba’hem, “with/ by/ yecholet, “ability, capability,” (n fs) which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) there exists,” (part) in them,” (prep, 3mp pronom) ledaber, “to speak, talk,” (v. Pi’el, inf o, “or,” (conj) lishmoa, “to hear,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.9.21">And there were those who did not repent for their fornications, nor for their thefts.  The Scriptures: And they did not repent of their murders, nor of their drug sorceries, nor of their whoring, nor of their thefts.  Aramaic: And they repented not of their murders, nor of their sorceries, nor of their whoredom, nor of their thefts. v’she’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or that/ which/ Idiom: “they repented” al, “upon, in, on, over, by, for, both, beyond, through,” “just as, as/ like/ “their prostitution’ vice, fornication,” (n fp constr, 3mp ahsu, “they did, made,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, no/not,” (rel part, qatal, past, 3mp) them,” (prep, 3mp tshuva, “repentance,” (n fs) o, “or” (conj) al, “on, upon,” gnevot’hem- “their . (n fp constr, 3mp <note type="footnote" n="256">First Century word first used in the Midrash of Philo 3:8:8.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.10">
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.1">Then, I saw another messenger descending from the heavens, clothed in a cloud, with a rainbow over his head.  His appearance was like the sun, his feet, like a flame of fire,   The Scriptures: And I saw another strong messenger coming down from the heaven, robed in a cloud, and a rainbow on his head, and his face was like the sun, and his feet like columns of fire,  Aramaic: And I saw another mighty angel, that descended from heaven, clothed with a cloud; and a cloud-bow was over his head, and his face was like the sun, and his feet like pillars of fire. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so /or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, v' lavush, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it was v’a’nanan, “in/ with/ by (the) cloud, cloud,” (prep, n ms) another, different,” descended,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, heavens,” (prep, n clothed, dressed,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, pssv v’keset, “and/ but/ u’m’r’ihu, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its rag’lav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its feet, legs,” (n fs, 3ms head,” (n ms, 3ms “just as, like/ as rainbow,” (n fs) (the) sun,” (prep, n k’lahevet“as/ like a flame, a weapon”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.2">and in his hand was an open scroll.  He stepped with his right foot upon the sea and with his left upon the dry land. u’v’yado, “and/ echad, “one,” (card patuach, “open,” v’ darach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/ it treaded, walked, im, “with,” (prep) raygel, “foot, leg,” but/ so/ or in/ with/ scroll, document,” hand,” (prep, n cs, (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, y’mi’no, “his/its right side” (n fs, ha’yam, “the sea,” v' im, “and/ but/ smolo, “his/its left, left side,” (n ms, ha’yabasha', “the dry land,” (n fs) so/ or with,” (prep)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.3">Then he cried with a great voice, like the cry of a lion.  And within the hour that he shouted, the seven voices spoke with their voices.  The Scriptures: and cried with a loud voice, as when a lion roars. And when he cried out, seven thunders spoke their sounds.  Aramaic: and he cried with a loud voice, as a lion roareth: and when he had cried, the seven thunders uttered their voices. b’kol, “with/ in/ by (the) voice,” (prep, k’ tza’ak, “like/ as u’ve’sha’a, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ she' tza'ak, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it shouted,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) “and/ but/ so/ or he/it cried out,” he/it cried out,” (v. (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, ms) m’dabrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those speaking,” (v. Pi’el, act part, shiv’a, “seven,” kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) b’kolehem, “in/ with/ by their voices,” (prep n ms, 3mp pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.4">After they spoke with their voices, I wanted to write them. But I heard a small voice262  from the heavens say to me, "Shut them up and do not write them!"  The Scriptures: And when the seven thunders spoke their sounds, I was about to write, but I heard a voice from the heaven saying to me, “Seal up what the seven thunders spoke, and do not write them.”  Aramaic: And when the seven thunders had spoken, I was about to write. And I heard a voice from heaven, saying: Seal up the things which the seven thunders have uttered, and write them not. v’acḥar, “and/ but/ she’dab’ro, “that/ which/ who/ whom b’kol’hem, “in/ with/ by/ their voices,” (prep, n mp, 3mp pronom) ra’tsi’ti, “I desired, lichtov, “to write,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) sham’a’ti, “that/ which/ who/ whom Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, added mater lectionis Idiom: “small voice” mi’sha’may’im, “from/ of (the) ha’ o’mer’et, “we/ s’gor, “(to a man) otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) shut! seal!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, bat kol, “voice of God,’ or “small voice,” heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’al, “and/ but/ so/ tik’tov, “you will Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.5">And the messenger which I saw standing on the sea and on the dry land lifted his right and left hands toward the heavens.265  The Scriptures: And the messenger whom I saw standing on the sea and on the land lifted up his right hand to the heaven,  Aramaic: And the angel whom I saw standing upon the sea and the land, raised his right hand to heaven, v’ha’mal’ach, “and/ but/ so/ or ha’yam, “the sea,” v’al, “and/ but/ so/ ha’ya’ba’sha, “the she’raiti, “that/ “I/ you (ms)/ he/it which/ who/ whom (v. Pa’al/Qal, act (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) yarum, “he/it shall yi’mi’no, “his/its right hand,” (n fs 3ms, 3ms pronom) v’smolo, “and/ but/ ha’may’im, “the heavens,” (n mp) so/ or his/its left hand,” (n ms, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.6">And he swore266 by the Eternal Living One, who created the heavens and all that exists - the earth, the sea, and all that is in them – “There is no more time!"267  The Scriptures: and swore by Him who lives forever and ever, who created the heaven and what is in it, the earth and what is in it, and the sea and what is in it, that there shall be no further delay,  Aramaic: and swore, by him who liveth for ever and ever, who created heaven and the things in it, and the earth and the things in it, and the sea and the things in it, that the time should be no longer; v’yi’sheva, “and/ but/ or/ let or may him/it swear,” (v. Nif’al, yiqtol, fut, b’chei’, “with/ by/ u’mah, “and/ but/ she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom there is,” (rel part, in I/ you (ms)/ he/it live(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it create(s),” (rel ever, everlasting, part, v. Pa’al/Qal, bah, “in/ with/ by/ her/it,” (prep, 3fs v’ha’eretz, “and/ v’ha’yam, “and/ v’kol, “and/ but/ she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom there is,” (part) b’hem, “in/ with/ by them,” (prep, but/ so/ or the sea,” od, “again, more, et, “time, season,” which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) there exists,” (part) longer, else, yet still, besides,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.7">“Just as the seven messengers came, they blew the shofars, completing all the mysteries of Yehovah, announcing to His servants and to His prophets!"268  The Scriptures: but in the days of the sounding of the seventh messenger, when he is about to sound, the secret of Elohim shall also be ended, as He declared to His servants the prophets. rak, “only, just, surely” (part) ba’im, “we/ you (mp)/ they/ those tok’im, “we /you b' shofarot, “in/ with/ by/ (the) tiklna, “they will “that/ which/ who/ whom the seven,” accomplish,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3fp) messengers,” (n shofars,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, kol, “all,” (n ms) eyleh, “these,” k’mo, “like, as, she’modia, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it l’adav, “to/ for/ secrets, mysteries,” belonging to his/its (prep, n mp, 3ms Hif’il, act part, ms) v’l’na’vi’av, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to his/its prophets,” (prep, n mp, 3ms pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.8">I heard again the small voice say to me, “Go and take the open scroll out of the hand of the messenger standing on the sea and on the dry land!”  The Scriptures: And the voice which I heard out of the heaven spoke to me again and said, “Go, take the little book which is opened in the hand of the messenger standing on the sea and on the earth.”  Aramaic: And the voice which I heard from heaven, spoke to me again, and said: Go, take the little open book in the hand of the angel that standeth on the sea and on the land. v’shamati, “and/ but/ or/ so I heard, Idiom: “small voice” amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) od, “yet, still,” (adv) bat kol, “voice of God or small voice, divine voice,” (n ms) pa’am, “time, once,” (adv) qol, “voice, sound,” (n ms) lech! “(to a man) Go!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, v’kach, “and/ but/ or/ so (to a man) m' yad, “from/ of (the) hand,” (prep, ha’malach, “the book, document,” “open, opened,” angel, messenger,” “I/ you (ms)/ he/it Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’yam “the sea,” v’al, “and/ but/ so/ ha’yabashah, “the land, dry land,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.9">So, I went to the messenger and said, “Give me the scroll.”  Then he said, “Take, and swallow, for it will be like honey in your mouth, but in your inward parts it will give you grief.”275  The Scriptures: And I went to the messenger and said to him, “Give me the little book.” And he said to me, “Take and eat it, and it shall make your stomach bitter, but it shall be as sweet as honey in your mouth.”  Aramaic: And I went to the angel, telling him to give me the little book. And he said to me, Take, and eat it: and it will make thy bowels bitter, but in thy mouth it will be sweet as honey. v’halachti, “and/ but/ or/ so I went, ‘l’ha’mal’ach, “to/ for/ belonging to the angel” (prep, n v’ amarti, “and/ but/ so/ or I said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal qatal, tnu! “(to men) you belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) him/it,” (prep, 3ms (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, document,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms amar, “he/it said,” kakh!, “(to a man) u' bol'a, "and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it swallow(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act yihye, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it will belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) (DO marker, pron qatal, past, 3ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) be’pi’’cha, “in/ with/ by your b’mayayich “in/ with/ by your (ms) ya’aseh, “he/it will belonging to you,” “as/ like honey,” belonging to you,” (prep, n ms, 2ms however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay (prep, n mp, 2ms yiqtol, fut, 3ms) sorrow, sadness, regret, remorse, sad, inflict pain,” <note type="footnote" n="271">See The War of the Jews 1:6:5 and The War of the Jews 2:21:8. 272 See Revelation 10:4 for more details on this Hebrew idiom. 273 The scribe added nikkudot (vowel markings) to this verb, perhaps, to emphasize the imperative form. Otherwise, it would mean, "to you." 274 See verse Revelation 9:14 of this manuscript for use of the word, םיה (ha'yam) for the river Euphrates.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.10">I took the scroll from the hand of the messenger and then ate. It became like honey in my mouth. But after I swallowed, it was grief to my inward parts.   The Scriptures: And I took the little book out of the messenger’s hand and ate it, and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth, but when I had eaten it, my stomach was made bitter.  Aramaic: And I took the little book from the hand of the angel, and ate it: and it was in my mouth sweet like honey: and when I had eaten it, my bowels were bitter. mi’yad, “from/ of ha’mal’ach, “the angel, messenger,” u’vula’ti, “and/ oto, “him/it,” (DO v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was” “and/ but/ so/ or I but/ so/ or I swallowed,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) document,” (n cs) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, 3ms) kid’vash, “as/ like b’pee,”in/ with/ by vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) she’achlti, “that/ asa, “he/it made,” which/ who/ whom belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) sorrow, sadness, regret, pain, ache, remorse sad,” (n qatal, past, 3ms) v’me’eye’, “in/ with/ by my inward parts,” (prep, n mp, 1cs <note type="footnote" n="275">Compare to Ezekiel 3:3. 276 Compare to Ezekiel 3:3.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.10.11">Then he said to me, “You must prophesy again, to the nations, peoples, and to kings!”  The Scriptures: And he said to me, “You have to prophesy again concerning many peoples and nations and tongues and sovereigns.”  Aramaic: And be said to me, Thou must again prophesy upon many nations, and peoples, and princes, and kings. v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms amar, “he/it said,” belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) should, must,” (adj prophesy,” (v. Pi’el, inf constr) qatal, past, 3ms) “time, once,” (n fs) l’oh’mim, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) nations,” (prep n ule’a’mim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ v’l’melachim, “and/ but /so /or to/ for/ belonging peoples,” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="277">The (ךי) yod-kaf suffix is a result of Second Temple Hebrew influenced by the Aramaic language. This linguistic phenomenon is called “Aramaism” and is a unique Hebrew marker.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.11">
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.1">Then he gave me a reed, like a rod, and he said, “Get up to measure the holy place of Yehovah and His altar, for there are intercessors in it.”   The Scriptures: And a reed like a measuring rod was given to me, and the messenger stood, saying, “Rise and measure the Dwelling Place of Elohim, and the slaughter-place, and those worshipping in it.  Aramaic: And a reed was given to me, like a rod; and the angel stood, saying, Arise, and measure the temple of God, and the altar, and them that worship therein. v’noten, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it give(s),” (v. Pa'al/Qal, act part echad, “one,” (card kid’mut, “like/ as, ma’teh, “a rod,” (n v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) qatal, past, 3ms) kum, “(to a man) v’ mizbecho, “of/ from his/its altar, sacrifice,” (prep, n ms, 3ms pronom) v' eilu, “and/ but/ u’mitpallim, “and/ but/ so /or the we/ you (mp) they/those (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf following,” (3mp who prayers,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, b’o, “in/ with/ by him/it,” (prep, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.2">Rather measure the inner holy place, but do not include281 the outer court: for it is given to the nations to walk the holy city for forty-two months.”  The Scriptures: “But cast out the court which is outside the Dwelling Place, and do not measure it, for it has been given to the nations, and they shall trample the set-apart city under foot for forty-two months.  Aramaic: But the court which is without the temple, leave out, and measure it not; because it is given to the Gentiles; and they will tread down the holy city forty and two months. ha’hekal, “the holy hap’ni’mi, “inner,” zrok! “(to a man) throw, remove!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp lachuts, “outside” v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ timod, “you (ms) will measure,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, or no, not, don’t however,’’ (adv) le’ha’amim, “to/ belonging to the v’darchu, “they will walk, tread” ha’ir, “the city,” ha’kodesh, “the holiness, sanctity,” (v. Pa’alQal, act yiqtol, fut, 3mp) arbaim, “forty,” v’shni’yim “and/ so/ but/ so two,” “months,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.3">“For I give to my two witnesses to prophesy one thousand two hundred sixty days, dressed in sackcloth.”  The Scriptures: “And I shall give unto my two witnesses, and they shall prophesy one thousand two hundred and sixty days, clad in sackcloth.”  Aramaic: And I will give my two witnesses; and they will prophesy a thousand and two hundred and sixty days, clothed in sackcloth. v’ani, “and/ but/ et, (DO marker) shanei, “two,” v’hem, “and/ but/ (ms)/ he/ it give(s), “witnesses,” (n which/ who/ whom to/ for/ belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs Pa’al/Qal, act part, me’na’b’im“we/ you (mp)/ they, elef, “thousand,” v’ shenei, “and/ but/ so/ or two,” meot, “hundred,” yom, “day,” (n ms) ulavush, “and/ but/ “sixty,” (card num) dressed, clothed,” (v. Pi’el, act part, ba’ sa’ kim, “in/ sackcloth,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.4">For these are the two olive trees and the two torches standing before Elohei (God) of the earth.283  The Scriptures: These are the two olive trees and the two lampstands that are standing before the Elohim of the earth.  Aramaic: These are the two olive-trees, and the two candlesticks which stand before the Lord of the earth. v’eyleh, “and/ but/ so/ or these,” (pron he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, ze’tim, “olives, v’shenei “and/ but/ so/ or two,” (card avokot, “torches,” ohm’dim, “we/ you (mp) /they, those standing,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act olive, trees,” (n cp) Elohei, “God(s) of,” (n mp constr) before the face of, before me, in front <note type="footnote" n="283">See also Zechariah 4:11-14 for the prophecy of the two messiahs (anointed ones).</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.5">If anyone wants to harm these, then fire will come284 and consume them.  The Scriptures: And if anyone wishes to harm them, fire comes out from their mouth and consumes their enemies. And if anyone wishes to harm them, he has to be killed in that way.  Aramaic: And if any person will harm them, fire cometh out of their mouth, and consumeth their adversary; and if any one will harm them, thus must he be slain. v’im, “and/ but/ or if/ whether,” (conj) she’echad, “that/ which/ who/ whom one,” (card num) la’a’sot, “to do, la’hem, “to/ for/ tavo, “she/it will (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf them,” (prep, 3mp (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3fs) Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’yasraf, “he/it otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) qatal, past, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="284">The yiqtol can be a simple future tense, the language of the Law, or an iterative action - past (Numbers 11:4-6) or future. See legend and definitions for more details.  285 This could be a gender and number mismatch. However, this could also be referring to Yehovah: “He consumed them with fire.” This would fit better with the Tanakh since Yehovah sends fire to destroy His enemies. See Genesis 19:24, Numbers 16:35 and Ezekiel 5:4 as examples.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.6">During the time they are prophets, they have the authority to shut the heavens so that no rain comes on the earth, and over the waters to turn them into blood,286 and to strike the earth with plagues, whenever they please.  The Scriptures: These possess authority to shut the heaven, so that no rain falls in the days of their prophecy. And they possess authority over waters to turn them to blood, and to smite the earth with all plagues, as often as they wish.  Aramaic: They have power to shut up heaven, so that the rain shall not fall in those days: and they have power over the waters, to turn them into blood; and to smite the earth with all plagues, as often as they please. v’lahem “and/ but/ “yesh, “there is, rashut “authority, permission,” (n fs) lisgor “to shut,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf ha’sha’may’im, “the heavens,” Ya’vo, “he/it shall there exists,” (part) which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) them,” (prep, 3mp yiqtol, fut, 3ms) ge’shem, “rain,” (n bi’may “in/ with/ by (the) days of,” (prep, n mp constr) navi’hem, “their prophets,” (n mp, al, “and/ but/ or/ so ha’mayim, “the waters,” (n mp) la’ha’foch, “to turn into,” (v. Pa’al/Qal ba’dam, “in/ with/ by (the) blood,” v’le’ha’cot, “and/ but/ so/ or to smite, ha’nega’im, “in/ be’chol, “in/ with/ by (the) all,” (prep, ‘season(s),” (n cs) strike, slay, kill” strokes, plagues, diseases, marks, marks of leprosy,” shay’yir’tsu, “that/ which/ who/ whom they will want,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, <note type="footnote" n="286">See Exodus 7:20.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.7">After their testimony was finished, He287 brought forth the beast from the deep. The beast battled,288 prevailed and killed them.  The Scriptures: And when they have ended their witness, the beast coming up out of the pit of the deep shall fight against them, and overcome them, and kill them,  Aramaic: And when they shall have completed their testimony, the beast of prey that came up from the abyss, will make war upon them, and will overcome them. v’aḥar, “and/ but/ so/ or after, and she’ kala, “that/ edu’tam, “their yaaseh, “he/it will she’halach, “that/ which/ who/ whom m’tehom, “from/ which/ who/ whom he/it was finished,” creature,” (n fs) deep,” (prep, n fs) (v. Pu’al, qatal, pssv past, 3ms) yiqtol, fut, 3ms) qatal, past, 3ms) milchama, “war,” imam, “with them” v’yenatseach, he/it will, overcome,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, otam, “them” (DO marker, 3ms pron) v’ya’ha’rog, “he/it otam, “them” (DO marker, 3mp pron) yiqtol, fut, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.8">Then their corpses were thrown292 into the streets of the Holy City, called Sodom and Egypt, and is also the exact place293 where our Master was crucified.  The Scriptures: And their dead bodies lie in the street of the great city which spiritually is called Seḏom and Mitsrayim, where also our Master was impaled,  Aramaic: And their dead bodies [will be] in the open street of that great city, which is spiritually called Sodom and Egypt, where also their Lord was crucified. unvelat’hem’ “and/ tizk’arku, “they will be thrown,” ha’ rechovot, “the m’ha’ ir, “from/ of the city,” (prep, n ha’ kdosha, “the holy,” (adj, fs) ha nokre, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it call(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, but/ or/ so their streets,” (n mp) (v. Nif’al, pssv fut, “Sodom,” (name) v’mitsrayim, “and/ but/ so/ or Egypt,” kivan, “because, as v’gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” ha’makum, “the place,” (n ms) she’sham, “that/ nitzlav, “he/it was soon as, since,” which/ who/ whom Nif’al, qatal, past, kivan, “directly, exactly,” (adv) adoneinu, “our master,” (n ms, 1cp pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.9">Translation #1: And they of the nations and tribes, see their corpses for three and one-half days, but you295 do not bury them.  Translation #2: And they of the nations and tribes will see their corpses for three and one-half days, and they will not be buried.296  The Scriptures: and some of the peoples and tribes and tongues and nations see their dead bodies for three and a half days, and not allow their dead bodies to be placed into tombs,  Aramaic: And [they] of the nations and tribes and peoples and tongues, will look upon their dead bodies, three days and a half; and will not suffer their dead bodies to be laid in the grave. v’ eize, “and what, u' m’ ha' shvatim, “and/ but/ so/ or yiru, “they will et, (DO marker) nvelot’ ihem “and/ shlosha, “three,” and some, any,” see,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, but/ so/ or their corpses,” (n mp, peoples, nations,” yiqtol, fut, 3mp) tribes,” (prep, n yamim, “days,” (n v’chetzi, “and/ but/ v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not,” (neg tikberu, “you (mp) otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp pron) so/ or a half,” (n Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Possible error: Consider the Nif’al</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.10">Those dwelling upon the earth rejoiced over them and sent gifts to one another since the prophets brought a lot of grief to the inhabitants of the earth. v' eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, ha’ darim “the, yisamchu, “they will be happy, rejoice,” (v. v' yishlachu, “and/ that we/ you (mp)/ upon, over, about, regarding, them,” (prep, pron 3mp) but/ so/ or they will send,” (v. the following,” (3mp pronom) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, act part, matanot, “gifts,” (n ish, “a man,” (n ha’ nevi’im, “the prophets,” (n mp) ha' lelu, “the these/ another,” (prep, n ms, 3ms pronom) made, created,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, tza’ar, “sadness, regret, remorse,” v’eilu, “and/ but/ much, a lot,” (adv) certain,” (pron, inhabitants,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.11">And after three and a half days, they rose and stomped to their feet, and great fear and terror fell upon those seeing them.  The Scriptures: And after the three and a half days a spirit of life from Elohim entered into them, and they stood upon their feet, and great fear fell on those who saw them. v’achar, “and/ but/ shlosha, “three,” yamim, “days,” yakumu, “they shall rise up” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, v’ dorchim’ “we/ you (mp)/ they, those stomping, but/ so/ or half,” (n afterwards,” (adv) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act rag’lay’hem, “their legs, feet,” (n mp, u'pachad, "and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’eima, “and/ but/ so/ or terror, fear,” g’dola, “great,” nafal, “he/it fell Pa’al/Qal, qatal, eilu, "those, these, ro’im, “we/ you (mp) / they, those the following," (3mp pronom) (DO marker, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.12">Translation #1:  And they heard a voice saying, “Rise up!” Then they ascended to the heavens in a cloud, and they saw their enemies.    Translation #2: And they heard a voice saying, “Rise up!” Then they ascended to the heavens in a cloud, and their enemies saw them.301   The Scriptures: And they heard a loud voice from the heaven saying to them, “Come up here.” And they went up into the heaven in a cloud, and their enemies saw them.  Aramaic: And they heard a great voice from heaven, which said to them: Come up hither. And they ascended to heaven in a cloud; and their enemies saw them. v’shom’im, “we, you (mp)/ they, amar, “he/it said,” lahem, “to/ for/ va’a’yalu, “and/ but/ so/ they will (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) those hearing,” (v. Pa’alQal, act part, them,” (prep, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, b’shamayim, “in/ b’anon, “in/ with/ by (the) cloud,” v’rau, “and/ but/ so/ or they saw,” (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, sho’n’hem, “we/ you (mp)/ they, above, upwards,” (DO marker, part, heavens,” (prep, n those who hate(s), ”  (v. Pa’al/Qal, act qatal, past 3mp) <note type="footnote" n="301">It is unclear whether the "they" refers to the witnesses or the enemies, so both translations are included.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.13">At that time,302 there were tremblings of the earth; a tenth part of the city fell, and seven thousand died among the children of mankind. Others were terrified but we gave praise to Elohei (God) of the heavens.  The Scriptures: And in that hour there came to be a great earthquake, and a tenth of the city fell. And in the earthquake seven thousand men were killed, and the rest became afraid and gave esteem to the Elohim of the heaven.  Aramaic: And in the same hour there was a great earthquake, and the tenth part of the city fell: and the persons killed in the earthquake, were seven thousand names: and they who remained were afraid, and gave glory to God. uva’sha’a, “and/ haya, “he/it was,” re’adot, “tremors, earthquakes,” (n v’chelek, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) but/ so/ or in/ with/ qatal, past, 3ms) portion, share,” (n m’ha’ir, “of/ from the city,” (prep, n nafal, “he/it fell va’ya’mot, “and/ but/ so/ or will shiv’a, “seven,” m’ benei, “from/ or adam, “man,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, sons,” (prep, n mp (v. Pa’al/ Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp) ve’acherim, “and/ but/ so/ or other, another, different, following,” (adj v’nat’nu, “and/ but/ so/ or we shevach, “praise, le’elohei, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) Elohim of,” (prep, “the heavens,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, value),” (n ms) Nif’al, qatal, past <note type="footnote" n="302">Can also mean, “And in the hour.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.14">See!  The second sorrow has come, and the third sorrow comes!  The Scriptures: The second woe is past, and see, the third woe is coming speedily.  Aramaic: The second woe is passed: behold, the third woe cometh quickly. re’eh, (to a man) v’ ha’ shli’shi, “and/ but/ so/ or ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it comes,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp sadness,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, the third,” (adj ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.15">Then the seventh messenger blew and there were many voices in heaven declaring the songs of creation.304 All things are subject to our Lord Yeshua, and he shall reign forever and ever.  The Scriptures: And the seventh messenger sounded, and there came to be loud voices in the heaven, saying, “The reign of this world has become the reign of our Master, and of His Messiah, and He shall reign forever and ever!” v' ha’mal'ach, “and/ but/ so/ or taka, “he/it blew,” v’ hayu, “and/ but/ so/ or they were,’’ kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) harbeh, “many, much, alot,” (adj b’shamayim, “in/ qatal, past, 3ms) heavens,” (prep, n messenger,” (n ms) qatal, past, 3ms) haom’rim,“we/ you (mp)/ they, those saying, m’ haolam, “from/ holchim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those kulam, “all those,” of everlasting, eternity, world, creation,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, (v. Pa’alQal, act yeshu, “Yeshua,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms m’olam, “from/ of (the) forever, of old,” (prep, n ms) v’ad, “and/ but/ so/ olam, “forever, everlasting,” (n shall rule, govern,” or even, until,” yiqtol, fut, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="303">Chapter 11 continues with verse 15. However, the Cochin manuscript begins chapter 12 with this verse.   304 Can also mean, “world.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.16">And the twenty-four elders sitting on their thrones before Yehovah fell upon their faces, praying to Yehovah,  The Scriptures: And the twenty-four elders sitting before Elohim on their thrones fell on their faces and worshipped Elohim,  Aramaic: And the twenty and four Elders, who are before the throne of God, [and] who sit upon their seats, fell upon their faces, and worshipped God, v’arba, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) four,” v’esrim, “and/ but/ zekeinim, “elders,” ha’yoshvim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those sitting,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, kise’hem, “their thrones,” (n mp, before the face of, before me, in front noflim, “we / you (mp)/ they, those pneihem, “their face(s),” (n mp, 3mp pronom) u’mitpallim, “and/ la’ Yehovah, “to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, but/ so /or (the) we/ you (mp)/ they Pa’al/Qal, act part, Hit’pael, act part, <note type="footnote" n="305">See Revelation 1:1.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.17">saying, “We praise You, Lord of Armies - who was, and is, and will be!”  The Scriptures: saying, “We give You thanks, O  הוהי Ěl Shaddai, the One who is and who was and who is coming, because You have taken Your great power and reigned.  Aramaic: saying: We praise thee, O Lord God, Omnipotent, who art, and wast; because thou hast assumed thy great power, and hast reigned. v’omrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those notnim, “we/ you (mp/ they, those giving, allowing,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act shevach, “praise,” adon,” Lord,” (n tseva’ot “hosts, armies,” (n mp) belonging to you,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’haya, “the/that v’hoveh, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it is,” v’yihye, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (v. Pa’al/Qal, act <note type="footnote" n="306">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem. 307 See Against Apion 2:7:1 by Josephus (composed c. 90 - 110 CE).</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.18">“The time of the nations308 were filled. Therefore, the time of Your wrath and judgment of the dead comes: to give recompense to your servants, the holy prophets, and the righteous who revere You - for the small and the great; and to destroy those who corrupted the earth.”  The Scripture: “And the nations were enraged, and Your wrath has come, and the time of the dead to be judged, and to give the reward to Your servants the prophets and to the set-apart ones, and to those who fear Your Name, small and great, and to destroy those who destroy the earth.”  Aramaic: And the nations were angry; and thy anger is come, and the time of the dead, that they should be judged: and that thou shouldst give a reward to thy servants, the prophets, and the saints, and to them that fear thy name, the small and the great; and that thou shouldst destroy them who destroyed the earth. Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic v’ha’amim “and/ v’hema, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (pron u’ba, “and/ but/ so/ v’ha’eyt, “and/ though, so much the more,” (part) but/ so/ or a time,” peoples, nations,” he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, nit’maleu, “they were filled,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, lishpot, “to judge,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf ha’ metim, “we/ you/ they those v’liten, “to give, la’avde’cha, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to your (mp) servants,” ha’nevi’im, “the prophets,” (n mp) v' l' k’doshim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) holy ones,” “payment, salary, (v. Pa’al/Qal, act v’eilu, “and/ but/ ha' ye’erim, “we/ you/ they fear,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, mipanecha, “from/ of your face, from you,” (prep, 2ms lak'taniym, "for/ to ve’ le’ gedolim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging v' lehashchit, “and/ l'ilu, “whereas, if, but considering, destroy,” (v. Hif’il these, those,” (prep, pron mp) ones,” (adj mp) she’hishchitu,” that/ which/ who/ corrupted, ruined” (v. HIf’il, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="308">See Genesis 15:16, Revelation 11:17 and Luke 21:24. 309 “Nit’pael is a Mishnaic verb binyan with a mix of the Nifal and Hit’pael stems used regularly in Mishnaic Hebrew to express reflexive action. Retrieved from: Accordance software help files. This word is first found in the Mishnah Parah 6:5.  310 See Revelation 2:17 for more details. 311 This spelling is found in Duties of the Heart 3:205. 312 This spelling is found in Midrash of Philo 2:9:26 from the Second Temple Period. 313 This spelling is found in Book of Jubilees 10:8. 314 From the late Second Temple to the Talmudic period, this exact spelling is found in Jerusalem Talmud Peah 3:2:1.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.11.19">In the heavens, Yehovah's house of prayer315 opened and revealed the Ark of the tablets of the Covenant in His house. Then there are voices and thunders and lightnings316 and tremors of the earth and great hail.  The Scriptures: And the Dwelling Place of Elohim was opened in the heaven, and the ark of His covenant was seen in His Dwelling Place. And there came to be lightnings, and voices, and thunders, and an earthquake, and great hail.  Aramaic: And the temple of God in heaven was opened; and the ark of his covenant was seen in his temple: and there were lightnings, and thunders, and voices, and an earthquake, and great hail. u'veit, “and/ but/ tfilat, “prayer,” (n nif’tach, “I/ you b’shamayim, “in/ Note: Mishnaic verb binyan structure. v’nitraea, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it was seen.”  (v. Nit’pael, qatal, past, 3fs) so/ or (the) house,” open(s)” (v Nif’al, heavens,” (prep, n aron, “ark,” (n ms) b’bayit, “in/ with/ v’hayah, “and/ but/ kolot,” sounds, voices,” (n mp) v’re’amim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) thunders,” (n mp) prayer,” (n fs, 3ms luchot, “tablets,” (n mp) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’brit, “the covenant,” (n fs) u’brakim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’radot, “and/ but/ u’varad, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) hail,” tremors, trembling, flashes,” (n mp) shaking,” (n fp) <note type="footnote" n="315">See Isaiah 56:7, Ezekiel 43:10. The Temple is referred to as a "house of prayer." 316 See Exodus 20:18. 317 This spelling with the added yod is found first in Targum of Jonathan Exodus 13:9 318 This is the spelling written 16 times in the Torah including Exodus 25:22; 26:34; 27:21, etc. This is an idiomatic phrase that refers to the Ark of the Covenant that contains the tablets of the covenant.  319 This spelling is found in Sefer HaKana 16:2 320 This spelling is found in The Wisdom of Solomon 19:12</note> <note type="footnote" n="321">This spelling is found in Mishnah Parah 11:2 written possibly before c. 200 CE.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.12">
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.1">A great thing is seen again in the heavens: a woman clothed with the sun, the moon beneath her feet, and on her head a crown of twelve stars.  The Scriptures: And a great sign was seen in the heaven: a woman clad with the sun, with the moon under her feet, and on her head a crown of twelve stars.  Aramaic: And a great wonder was seen in heaven; a woman clothed with the sun, and the moon under her feet, and on her head a coronet of twelve stars. Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic gam, “again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” gadol, “great thing, greatness” (n ms) b’shamayim, “in/ echad, “one, first,” “wife,woman,” heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, pssv part, v’nitraea, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it was seen.”  (v. Nit’pael, qatal, ba’shemesh, “in/ v’ ha’ yareach, “and/ but/ so/ or the moon,” (n ms) tachat, “under, instead, below, beneath, at the foot,” (prep) ragleha, “her/its legs, her/its feet,” (n fp, 3fs pronom) v’al, “and/ but/ so/ coronet, diadem,” sun,” (prep, n ms) leader,” (n ms, 3fs echad, “one, first,” min, “from, of, than,” (prep) shnayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card kochavim, “stars</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.2">She was with child and crying out, sat upon the birthing seat, and was in great pain because of her labor.  The Scriptures: And being pregnant, she cried out in labour and in pain to give birth. v’hi, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, past, me’uberet, “I am/ you (fs)/ she/it is impregnated,” (v. Pi’el, pssv part, fs) v’ tzoeket, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (fs)/ she/it cry(s) out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, v’hi, “and/ but/ so/ yoshevet, “she/it inhabitant,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’mashber, “the birth, birth stool, travailing chair,” v’haya, “and/ but/ ha’lidah,” labor, so/ or was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, much, a lot,” (adv) sorrow, sadness, regret, remorse,” because of,” (conj) her/it,” (prep, 3fs</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.3">Then there was another wonder in the heavens: I saw a dragon,325 and he had seven heads and ten horns, and on his heads were seven crowns.  The Scriptures: And another sign was seen in the heaven: and see, a great, fiery red dragon having seven heads and ten horns, and seven crowns on his heads.  Aramaic: And there appeared another wonder in heaven; and lo, a great fiery dragon, which had seven heads and ten horns, and upon his head seven diadems. v’nes, “and/ but/ haya, “he/it was,” b’shamayim, “in/ v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, echad, “one,” (card tanin, “and/ but/ so/ or dragon, serpent, sea another, different,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) heavens,” (prep, n providential event” monster, dinosaur, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/qal, qatal, shiv’a, “seven,” roshim, “heads,” v’asara, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ten,” karnayim, “horns,” v’al,” and/ but/ so/ shiv’a, “seven,” k’tarim, “crowns,” heads,” (n mp, 3ms <note type="footnote" n="322">This spelling is confirmed in The Midrash of Philo 4:25:2. 323 This spelling is confirmed in Sefer HaKana 9:41. 324 This spelling in confirmed in Book of Tobit 7:7 325 The first use of this word is in Genesis 1:21 where Jewish Publication Society (JPS) translates it as “sea monster.” Revelation 12:15 speaks of a "waters like a great sea from its mouth" so it appears to be associated with the sea.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.4">His tail took a third of the stars and threw them to the earth. Then the dragon stepped in front of the woman giving birth, in order to consume the male child being born of the mother.  The Scriptures: And his tail draws a third of the stars of the heaven and throws them to the earth. And the dragon stood before the woman who was about to give birth, to devour her child as soon as it was born.  Aramaic: And his tail drew along the third part of the stars of heaven, and cast them on the earth. And the dragon was standing before the woman, who was about to bring forth, so that, when she should bring forth, he might devour her child. v’zenavo, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its tail,” (n ms, 3ms m’ha’kokavim, “from/ of the v’ zarak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it threw,” otam, “them,” (DO Pa’al/Qal, qatal, stars,” (prep, n mp) qatal, past, 3ms) v’h’tanin, “and/ but/ so/ or the dragon, serpent, ha’ isha, “the woman,” (n fs) she’ teyaled “that she/it will deliver,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut k’dei, “be able, before the face of, before me, in front according to, as, in Pa’al/Qal, qatal, order to,” (conj) dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” le’echol, “to eat, b’em, “in/ with/ by the mother,” (prep, she’nolad, “that/ male child,” (n ms) which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it is born,” (rel part, v. Nif’al, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.5">She gave birth to a son who leads the nations with a rod of iron.326 And he is taken before Yehovah and His throne.  The Scriptures: And she bore a male child who was to shepherd all nations with a rod of iron. And her child was caught away to Elohim and to His throne.  Aramaic: And she brought forth a male child, who was to rule all nations with a rod of iron. And her child was caught up to God and to his throne. v’ yalda, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it gave ben, “son,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card ha’ minhag, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it barzel,” iron,” (n people, nations,” with/ by (the) rod,” lead(s),” (v. Hif’il, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’yeled, “and/ but/ Yehovah v’kiso, “and/ but/ before the face of, before me, in front throne,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) Hi’fil, pssv, part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.6">Because it was prepared for her by Yehovah, the woman walked the wilderness, in the place there supporting her, one thousand two hundred sixty days.   The Scriptures: And the woman fled into the wilderness, where she has a place prepared by Elohim, to be nourished there one thousand two hundred and sixty days.  Aramaic: And the woman fled into the wilderness, where she had a place which was prepared for her by God; so that they might nourish her there a thousand and two hundred and sixty days. v’ha’isha, “and/ but/ so/ or the halacha, “she/it ba’ ’midbar, “in/ kivan, “because, as she’ haya, “that/ muchan, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it was prepared,” (v. with/ by (the) wilderness,” (n soon as, since,” which/ who/ whom belonging to her/it, (prep, 3fs pronom) woman, wife,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) Hif’il, pssv part, kivan, “directly, exactly,” (adv) makom, “place,” echad, “one, first,” otah, “her/it,” (DO marker, 3fs pron) Yehovah” (prep, provide, support,” (v. Pi’el inf constr) eleph, “thousand,” v’shanei, “and/ but/ so/ or two,” me’ot, “hundred,” v’shishim, “and/ but/ so/ or sixty,” yom, “day,” (n ms) <note type="footnote" n="326">See Psalm 2:9. This phrase is also used in Revelation 2:27A, and 19:15.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.7">Then war was made in the heavens. The messenger Michael and his messengers fought the dragon and his messengers; they fought with them.  The Scriptures: And there came to be fighting in the heaven: Miḵa’ĕl and his messengers fought against the dragon. And the dragon and his messengers fought,  Aramaic: And there was war in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon, and the dragon and his angels fought, v’na’ase, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you milchama, “war,” b’shamayim, “in/ ha’ mal’ach, “the angel, messenger,” Michael (name) im, “with,” (prep) mal’achav, “his/its heavens,” (prep, n messengers,” (n mp, 3ms pronom) become(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, nilchamu, “he/it im, “with,” (prep) ha’tanin, “the dragon, serpent, v’al’achav, “his/its lachamu, “they fought,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, 3mp) them,” (prep, 3mp messengers,” (n mp, 3ms pronom) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.8">They did not prevail, so their place was not found in heaven any longer.  The Scriptures: but they were not strong enough, nor was a place found for them in the heaven any longer.  Aramaic:  and prevailed not; nor was their place found any more in heaven. v’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ nitzchu, “and/ but/ v’ gam, “and/ but/ so/ or again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” lo, “no, not,” (neg nimtza, “he/it is found,” (Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms) et, (DO marker) or no, not,” (neg Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mekomam,” their place,” (n ms, 3mp b’shamayim, “in/ heavens,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.9">And the great dragon - called Satan the Destroyer, the inciter of the entire world - was cast out. Him with his messengers were thrown to the earth, to dwell there.   The Scriptures: And the great dragon was thrown out, that serpent of old, called the Devil and Satan, who leads all the world astray. He was thrown to the earth, and his messengers were thrown out with him.  Aramaic: And the great dragon was cast out, the old serpent, who is called the Deceiver, and Satan, who seduceth all the inhabited world: he was cast upon the earth, and his angels were cast out with him. v’nashlich, “and/ but/ so/ or was lachutz, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) outside,” (prep, n ha’tanin, “and/ but/ so/ or the dragon, ha nokre, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it call(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, ha’ mashchit, “the destroyer,” (n ms) great, big, large,” satan, adversary,” thrown, was cast,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, monster, dinosaur, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” v’ ha’ maschit, “I/ et, (DO marker) kol, “all, every, whole,” (n ms) v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms im, “with,” (prep) mal’achav, “his/its angels, his/its messengers,” (n mp, 3ms pronom) Hif’il, act part, ms) nishlachim, “we/ you (mp)/ they are sent, cast, thrown” (v. Nif’al, act part, l’dur, “to live, to inhabit, to dwell” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.10">Translation #1:  I heard a great voice in the heavens that said, “Now we will see again the mighty works of our Elohim and His Messiah, because he (Satan) was their adversary the entire time.”  Translation #2:  I heard a great voice in heaven that said, "Now the mighty works were seen of our Elohim and His Messiah, because having been the adversary from all time, they are cast out."333  The Scriptures: And I heard a loud voice saying in the heaven, “Now have come the deliverance and the power and the reign of our Elohim and the authority of His Messiah, for the accuser of our brothers, who accused them before our Elohim day and night, has been thrown down.  Aramaic: And I heard a great voice in heaven, which said: Now is there deliverance, and the power and the kingdom of our God, and the dominion of his Messiah: because the Accuser of our brethren is cast out, who accused them day and night before our God. v’shamati, “and/ gadol, “great, big, large, loud,” (adj, b’shamayim, “in/ she’ amar, “that/ achshav, “now,” Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic which/ who/ whom heavens,” (prep, n he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, nit’rea, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it was givurot, “power, mighty works, Eloheinu, “our Elohim,” (n mp, v’ meshicho, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its Messiah,” (n ms, kivan, “because, as l’ chutz, “to/ for/ belonging to out, outside, abroad,” ze, “this,” (pron, soon as, since,” “that/ which who/ whom was thrown, was cast (rel part, deeds, mighty,” (n kivan, “directly, exactly,” (adv) she’ haya, “that/ kol, “all, every,” (n et, “time, period,” l’ satan, “to/ for which/ who/ whom belonging to satan, adversary,” (prep n upon, over, about, regarding them,” he/it was,” (rel part, v. Pa’alQa/, qatal, past, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="332">This was labeled as 15A as the manuscript combines both verses 10 and 11 into one verse.  333 It is uncertain if this is the Hit’pael or the Nit’pael verb form. Therefore, both translations were provided.  334 See Revelation 1:18 for first use of this word.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.11">They prevailed over him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimonies, and they count their lives as nothing.   The Scriptures: “And they overcame him because of the Blood of the Lamb, and because of the Word of their witness, and they did not love their lives to the death.  Aramaic: And they overcame him, because of the blood of the Lamb, and because of the word of their testimony: and they loved not their life, even to death. v’y’natzchu, “and/ oto, “him/it,” (DO dam, “blood,” (n ha’se, “the lamb,” but/ so/ or they Idiom: al’yadei, “by the hand of,” Idiom: al’yadei, “by the hand of,” matter,” (n ms) prevail,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, 3mp) v’hashavu, “and/ but/ so/ or they counted,” (v. et, (DO marker) chay’hem, “their lives,” (n mp, 3mp l‘klum,”to/ for/ nothing,” (prep, (prep, n fp, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="335">This spelling is found in The War of the Jews 3:6 of the Second Temple Period. 336 This spelling is found in Letter of Aristeas 160 of the Second Temple Period. 337 The noun form of “their testimonies” is correct, but it is unique due to the added םהי suffix, which the author did 63 times. 338 This spelling is found in The Midrash of Philo 3:21:2 of the Second Temple Period.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.12">So, rejoice, heavens and everything in it, but woe to those dwelling on land and sea!  Satan is coming down to you with the fierceness of great anger, for he knows his time is shortened!  The Scriptures: “Because of this rejoice, O heavens, and you who dwell in them! Woe to the earth and the sea, because the devil has come down to you, having great wrath, knowing that he has little time.”  Aramaic: Therefore, be joyful, O heaven, and ye that dwell there. Woe to the earth, and to the sea; for the Deceiver hath come down to you, being in great wrath since he knoweth that his time is short. u’ bishvil, “and/ ze, “this,” (pron, tism’chu, “you will Idiom: “and everything in it,” but/ so/ or in/ with/ by the sake of,” Pa’al/Qal yiqtol, v’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all, “(n ms) asher, “that/ which/ who/ whom,” (conj) ba, “in/ with/ by her/it,” (prep, 3fs pronom) v’ oi! “and/ but/ so/ or, woe! alas!” ha’ darim, “we/ you (mp)/ they those dwelling, v’ al, “and/ but/ so/ ha’ yom, “the sea,” these,” (prep, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’ satan, “the satan, adversary, accuser,” (n ms) lachkem, “to/ for/ belonging to you (mp),” (prep, 2mp ba’ charon, “in/ af, “anger, nose,” gadol, “great, big, large,” (adj, ms) descended, is gone (v.Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’yodea, “and/ but/ she’yesh, “that/ mu’at, “he/it was shortened,” (v. Pi’el, pssv qatal, which/ who/ whom season, a set time, appointed time,” (n there is, there exists,” rel part, him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.13">Because the dragon saw that he was thrown to the earth, pursued the woman who gave birth.  The Scriptures: And when the dragon saw that he had been thrown to the earth, he persecuted the woman who gave birth to the male child.  Aramaic: And when the dragon saw that he was cast out upon the earth, he persecuted the woman who brought forth the male child. she’ ra’a, “that/ which he/it saw,” ha’tanin, “the dragon, serpent, she’nashlich, “who/ that was r’def, “he/it pursue(d,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” thrown,” (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dinosaur, sea or river monster, v. Nif’al, qatal, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” she’yaldah, “that/ which/ who/ whom she/it gave birth,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="345">This spelling is found in The Midrash of Philo 2:15:10.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.14">Then the woman is given two wings like a great eagle.346 She walks to the wilderness in a place belonging to Yehovah supporting her there, away from the dragon, for a season and two and one-half seasons.  The Scriptures: And the woman was given two wings of a great eagle, to fly into the wilderness to her place, where she is nourished for a time and times and half a time, from the presence of the serpent.  Aramaic:  And to the woman were given the two wings of the great eagle, that she might fly into the wilderness, to her place; where she is nourished a time and times and half a time, from the face of the serpent. v’noten, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it give(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, l’ ha isha, “to/ for/ belonging to the woman wife,” shtei, “two,” (card k’nesher, “as/ like (the) eagle,” (prep, gadol, “great, big, k’dei, “be able, “wings,” (n mp) according to, as, in order to,” (conj) b’midbar, “in/ with/ by (the) wilderness,” (n ba’makom, “in/ with/ by (the) place,” (prep, n she’natan, “that/ Yehovah l’ far’nes, “to which/ who/ whom belong, provide, support,” (v. Pi’el, her/it,” (prep, 3fs Pa’al/Qal, qatal, otah, “her/it,” (DO marker, 3fs pron) et, “time, period, echad, “one, first,” v’shanei, “and/ but/ so/ or two,” period, season” (n vacheytzi, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) mip’nei, “from/ of tanin, “and/ but/ so/ or the dragon, monster, dinosaur, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” <note type="footnote" n="346">Compare to Exodus 19:4, Isaiah 43:19 and chapter 41. 347 This spelling is found in The Midrash of Philo 2:24:3. 348 This spelling is found in Targum Jonathan on Ezekiel 34:23. 349 The spelling is found in The Midrash of Philo 2:4:15.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.15">From his mouth the dragon cast waters behind her like a great sea, so to silence her.  The Scriptures: And out of his mouth the serpent spewed water like a river after the woman, to cause her to be swept away by the river.  Aramaic: And the serpent ejected from his mouth waters like a river, after the woman, that he might cause her to be carried away by the flood. v’ hislick, “he/it cast, thew,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, ha’tanin, “the dragon, serpent, mayim, “waters,” mipiya, “from/ of k’ yam, “as/ like, (the) sea,” (prep n her/its mouth,” (prep, n ms, 3fs dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” gadol, “great, big, large,” (adj ms) k’dei, “be able, otah, “her/it,” (DO according to, as, in quiet, silence,” (v. Hif’il, inf constr) order to,” (conj)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.16">But because he opened his mouth and swallowed the waters the dragon cast behind her, the earth delivered the woman.   The Scriptures: And the earth helped the woman, and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed up the river which the dragon had spewed out of his mouth.  Aramaic: And the earth helped the woman: and the earth opened its mouth, and drank up the flood which the serpent ejected from his mouth. haya, “he/it was,” li’isha, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) yeshuah, “she/it is delivered, saved,” (v. Pa’al/Qal pssv kivan, “because, as soon as, since,” “that/ which/ who/ she/it opened,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, 3ms) earth,” (prep, n fs) however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay kivan, “directly, exactly,” (adv) et, (DO marker) piha, “her/its ubala,”and/ but/ she’hishlich,” that/ which/ who/ whom ha’tanin, “the dragon, serpent, achareha, “after her/it,” (prep, 3fs mouth,” (n ms, 2fs, water(s),” (n mp) he/it cast, threw hurled,” (rel part, destroyed,”’ (v, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.12.17">The dragon, filled with anger for the woman, went to war with the remnant of her seed - those doing the commands of Yehovah and believing in the testimony of His Messiah.351  The Scriptures: And the dragon was enraged with the woman, and he went to fight with the remnant of her seed, those guarding the commands of Elohim and possessing the witness of עשוהי Messiah.  Aramaic: And the dragon was enraged against the woman; and he went to make war upon the residue of her seed, who keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of Jesus. Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic v’ha’tanin, “and/ b’af, “in/ with/ by (the) anger, nose,” odot, “about, with ha’ isha, “woman, wife, spouse,” (n v’halach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it went,” (v. Pa’alQal, qatal, but/ so/ or the dragon, serpent, fight, battle, war, nit’male, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was full,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” im, “with,” (prep) ha’notarim, “the we/ you (mp)/ they, those who m’ zarah, “from/ of her/its seed,” (prep, n ms, 3fs ha’ osim, we/ you (mp)/ they, those et, (DO marker) mitzvot, “commandments” (n remain,” (v. Nif’al, Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’ ha'aminim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those b’edut, “in/ with/ meshicho, “his/its Messiah,” (n ms, Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="350">This appears to be crossed out by the original scribe and was not included in the translation. 351 See Matthew 5:17-20.</note> <note type="footnote" n="352">This Nit’pael verb binyan in Letter of Aristeas 294. 353 This spelling is found in Onkelos Leviticus 20:2. 354 This spelling is found in Letter of Aristeas 138.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.13">
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.1a">Then I stepped355 onto the sand of the sea.  The Scriptures: And I stood on the sand of the sea.   Aramaic: {12:18} And he stood on the sand of the sea. v’ darchati, “and/ al, “upon, in, on, over, by, for, both, beyond, through,” chol, “sand,” (n ha’yam, “the sea,” stepped, trod bow, cock, marched,” qatal, past, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.1b">And I saw a beast356 come out of the sea,357 and it had seven heads and ten horns, and on its horns ten crowns, and on its head’s, names of slander and mockery.  The Scriptures: 13b And I saw a beast coming up out of the sea, having seven heads and ten horns, and on his horns ten crowns, and on his heads names of blasphemy.  Aramaic:{13:1} And I saw a beast of prey come up from the sea, having ten horns, and seven heads; and upon his horns ten diadems, and upon his heads names of blasphemy. v’ ra’iti, “and/ but/ chaya, “life, living, v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (ms)/ he/it go(es) out, come(s), lead out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “from/ of the sea,” qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms shiv’a, “seven,” rashim, “heads,” va’asara, “and/ but/ so/ or ten,” karnayim, “horns,” v’ al, “and/ but/ so/ krnav, “horns,” (n ktarim, “crowns,” v’ al, “and/ but/ so/ rasheha, “her/its heads,” (n mp, 3fs shamot, “names,” shel, “that/ which/ of/ belonging to,” v’gifufim, “and/ but/ so/ or(the) chorufim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those who say mockeries” (n mp) <note type="footnote" n="355">This can also be “marched” indicating an anticipation of military stance. 356 This word is feminine. So, every verb or adjective that refers to this noun, should be feminine. However, it is masculine all the way through. It is possible that היח was considered a masculine word during the second Temple time, and that would mean that there are no gender mismatches with the verb forms. Could the grammatical gender confusion hint to an end of day event of “gender confusion?” 357 We see the dragon (i.e. the sea monster) and the first beast coming out of the sea, both have 7 heads and 10 horns, which are the leaders (governments) of the nation’s coming together to overcome the earth. For it becomes clear, the dragon and the beast are the same (i.e. Satan) (Revelation 12:3 &amp; 13:2). And isn’t it appropriate that the sea monster comes out of the sea as described in this verse?</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.2">The beast that I saw was like a horse; its legs and feet like the legs and feet of bears, and its mouth like the mouth of a lion.  And the dragon359 gave it (the beast) his power and his throne, military strength360  and great courage. 361  The Scriptures: And the beast I saw was like a leopard, and his feet were like the feet of a bear, and his mouth like the mouth of a lion. And the dragon gave him his power, and his throne, and great authority. be’ha’chaya, “and/ she’raiti, “that/ haya, “he/it was,” kidmut, “like/ as likeness, image,” sus, “horse,” (n v’raglav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its feet, legs,” (n fp, k’raglav’ “as/ like which/ who/ whom I saw,” (rel part, v. qatal, past, 3ms) (prep, n mp constr) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dovim, “bears,” k’pi, “like/ as (the) mouth of,” (prep, n v’ha’tanin, “and/ word, mouth,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) but/ so/ or the dragon, serpent, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms . —Allegorically: dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” et, (DO marker) kochko, “his/its strength, power, v’kiso, “and/ but/ v’gauvrat, “and/ but/ so/ or courage of,” (n fs constr) high, greater, loud, might, force, ability,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) wrong pronoun throne,” (n ms) wrong pronoun</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.3">I saw one of its heads resembling a wound leading to death, but the wound was healed. So, the whole world was astonished by the beast.  The Scriptures: and his deadly wound was healed. And all the earth marvelled after the beast.  Aramaic: And one of his heads was wounded as it were to death; and his deadly wound was healed. And all the earth wondered after the beast of prey. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, echad, “one,” (card m’rashav,”of/ from l’chavura, ‘to/ for/ belonging to (the) shel, “that/ which/ of/ belonging to,” ot, “the death,” (n his/its heads,” (prep n mp, 3ms resemble(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, stripe, wound,” Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic vhavura, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) stripe, wound, bruising” v’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (prep, n mishtomem, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is astonished,” (v. Hit’pael, act part, because of,” (conj) nitrapea, “she/it was healed,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, pssv past, 3fs) <note type="footnote" n="362">See Tractate Kallah 5, c. 100 BCE.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.4">Those praying to the dragon gave power and dominion to the beast.365  And those praying said, “Who is like this beast and who is able to battle366 with it?”  The Scriptures: And they worshipped the dragon who gave authority to the beast. And they worshipped the beast, saying, “Who is like the beast? Who is able to fight with him?”  Aramaic: And they worshipped the dragon, because he had given authority to this beast of prey, and [they said], who can make war upon him? u’mitpallim, “and/ lehatanin, “to the dragon, serpent, ha’ noten, “I/ you ha ‘chaya, “to/ for/ ko’ach, “power,” u-memshala, “and/ but/ so /or (the) belonging to the beast,” (prep, n fs) but/ so/ or (the) “and/ but/ so /or we/ you (mp)/ they monster,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, (mp)/ they pray, those praying,” (v. Hit’pael, act part, Hit’pael, act part, l’hachaya, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) dragon, serpent, omrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those ha’chaya, “beast,” u’mi, “and/ but/ belonging to this,” resemble(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, dinosaur, sea or river monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” youchal, “he/it will him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.5">The beast was permitted to open its mouth to speak words of wonders and cursing until imprisoned for the time of forty-two months.   The Scriptures: And he was given a mouth speaking great matters and blasphemies, and he was given authority to do so forty-two months.  Aramaic: And there was given to him a mouth speaking great things, and blasphemies: and authority was given him to operate forty and two months. v’noten, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ l’ hachaya,”to/ for/ liftoach, to open, to unlock, to turn on (i.e. a light),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf, et, (DO marker) pev, “his/its l’ daber, “to speak, talk,” (v. Pi’el, inf debrei, "words, things, matters, belonging to the mouth,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) wrong pronoun beast,” prep, (prep, Pa’al/Qal, act part, nifala’ot, “we/ you ad, ‘’by, as long, when, as far as, until,” (prep) she’kole, “that/ shel, “of belonging ha’arba’im, “the forty” (card num) (fp)/ they, those are wonderful, “and/ but/ so/ or abuse, reproach, which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it is time, season, a set time, appointed time,” (n ms) added mater lectionis extraordinary,” (n Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’shnayim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) “months,” (n mp) <note type="footnote" n="367">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem.  368 Contrast with Micah 4:8.  369 The first use is Book of Jubilees 31:2.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.6">It opened its mouth to curse against Yehovah, and against those living in the heavens.  The Scriptures: And he opened his mouth in blasphemies against Elohim, to blaspheme His Name, and His Tent, and those dwelling in the heaven.  Aramaic: And he opened his mouth in blasphemy towards God, to blaspheme his name and his tabernacle, and them who dwell in heaven. upatach, “and/ but/ et, (DO marker) pev, “his/its l’charef, “to defy, reproach, taunt, neged, “like/ as against,” (prep) Yehovah v’neged, “and/ but/ mouth,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) wrong pronoun so/ or against,” blaspheme, abuse, curse,” (v. Pi’el inf Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’ ddarim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, b’shamayim, “in/ heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.7">It was permitted to battle with the holy people but prevail over all the peoples and nations.  The Scriptures: And it was given to him to fight with the set-apart ones and to overcome them. And authority was given to him over every tribe and tongue and nation.  Aramaic: And authority was given him over every tribe and people and tongue and nation: and it was given him to wage war with the saints, and to overcome them. v’noten, “and/ but/ am, “people,” (n ha’ kdoshim,” saints, sacred, holy,” (adj, mp) otam, “them,” (DO marker, 3mp prep) battle, fight,” (v. “and/ but/ so/ or to him/it,” (prep, 3ms win, overcome, prevail,” (v. Pi’el, Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) all, every,” (n ms) v’ha’hamim, “and/ v’ umim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) nations,” (n mp) peoples,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.8">All those living on the earth prayed to it - all whose names not written in the Scroll of Life belonging to the slain Lamb, who was from the beginning of the creation of the world. v’kulam, “and/ but or/ so they all,” (n ha’ ddarim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those who live, mitpallim, “we/ you (mp)/ they eylo, “those, those, him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, act part, Hit’pael, act part, et, (DO marker) Shem’am, “their names,” (n ms, 3mp pronom) Idiom: “in the book of life” which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) ‘belonging to,” written,” (v. NIf’al b’ sefer, “in/ with/ by (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, n ms) ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp) ha’se, “the lamb,” ha’ neherag, “the killed, slain,” (adj m’tchilat, “from/ beriot, “creation,” ha’olam, “world,” beginning,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.9">He who has ears, hear!  The Scriptures: If anyone has an ear, let him hear.  Aramaic: If any one hath ears, let him hear. mi, “who?” (inter she’yesh, “that/ oznayim, “ears,” shome’ah, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it hear(s), which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms exists,” (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="370">See the first use of this word in Revelation 4:10. 371 Literally, “scroll of lives,” but is usually translated as “book of life.”  372 The added yod י makes this a Second Temple spelling, Tractate Derekh Eretz Zuta, 8:10 373 This is Second Temple spelling in The Book of Jubilees composed from c. 460CE to 140 BCE.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.10">If one drives another into captivity, he will go into captivity, and if one kills a soul by the sword, he will be killed by the sword.374  But with the holy ones there is hope and faith!  The Scriptures: He who brings into captivity shall go into captivity, he who kills with the sword has to be killed with the sword. Here is the endurance and the belief of the set-apart ones.  Aramaic: If [any one] carrieth into captivity, he shall himself go into captivity; and if any one slayeth with the sword, he must be slain with the sword: here is the patience and the faith of the saints. b’im, “in/ with/ by if, when, whether,” she’ who, “that/ yinhag, “he/it shall yelech, “he/ it will go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) u’vim, “and/ but/ so/ or by if, when, whether,” (prep, which/ who/ whom lead, drives (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, prison, captivity” prison, captivity” she’ echad, “that/ which/ who/ whom nefesh, “soul,” (n echad, one, (card b’ in, “in/ with/ by yehareg, “he/it will be killed (v. Nif’al, b’ harev, “sword, (ms)/ he/it kill(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act destruction,” (prep, yiqtol, pssv, fut u’ b’kan, “and/ tikvah, “hope,” (n v’emunat “and/ so/ but/ or (the) faith,” but/ so/ or with/ in/ there exists, (part) “saints,” (n, mp) <note type="footnote" n="374">Jeremiah 15:2.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.11">Then I saw another beast who came out of the ground. It had two horns like a lamb, and it was speaking like the dragon.  The Scriptures: And I saw another beast coming up out of the earth, and he had two horns like a lamb and spoke like a dragon.  Aramaic: And I saw another beast of prey, which came out of the earth; and he had two horns like those of a lamb, and he spoke like the dragon. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal chaya, “beast, creature,” (n fs) acher, “another,” yotzei, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it went out, went forth, proceeded,” (v. v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” ground,” (prep, n qatal, past, 3ms) him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, act part, shtei, “two,” (card karnayin, “horns,” k’mo, “like, as, l’ha’se,”to/ for/ belonging to the lamb,” (prep, n umidaber, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you katanin, “like/ as speak(s),” (v. Pi’el monster, dinosaur, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.12">It did great wonders before the first beast. And it made those dwelling on the ground pray375 to the first beast, whose wounds were healed.   The Scriptures: And he exercises all the authority of the first beast in his presence, and causes the earth and those who dwell in it to worship the first beast, whose deadly wound was healed. v’ asah, “and/ but/ nifala’ot, “we/ you gedolot, “great,” ha’ rishona, “first,” v’ asa, “and/ but/ so/ or he/ it did, so/ or he/it did, (fp)/ they, those are wonderful, before the face of, before me, in front created, made,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, extraordinary,” (n Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic she’ ha’ adamah, “that/ which/ who/ whom the ground,” ve’ ha’ addarim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ aleha, “on, upon, mitpallim “we/ you (mp)/ they le’ha’chaya, “to/ for/ belonging to the beast,” (prep, n ha’rishona, “first,” regarding her/it,” (prep, 3fs pronom) she’nitrafea, “that/ which/ who/ whom she/it was healed,” Hit’pael, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, chavorot, “her/ its wounds,” (n fp, 3fs <note type="footnote" n="375">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.13">It made fire fall from the heavens before mankind.  The Scriptures: And he does great signs, so that he even makes fire come down from the heaven on the earth before men.  Aramaic: And he wrought great signs, even so as to make fire come down from heaven upon the earth, before men. v’ asah, “and/ but/ she’nafal, “that/ eysh, “fire,” (n fs) so/ or he/ it did, which/ who/ whom he/it fell,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, before the face of, before me, in front created, made,” (v. heavens,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="376">The Nit’pael verb is a Mishnaic verb binyan and is found in Midrash Tanchuma Buber.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.14">It inflamed the children of mankind with signs and wonders.  And it told those dwelling on the earth to make an idol377 of the beast, whose wounds from the sword were healed.   The Scriptures: And he leads astray those dwelling on the earth because of those signs which he was given to do before the beast, saying to those dwelling on the earth to make an image to the beast who was wounded by the sword, yet lived.  Aramaic: And he seduced them that dwell on the earth, to erect an image to the beast of prey who had the wound from a sword and recovered. v’hasit’, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it incited, im, “with,” (prep) otot, “signs,” (n v’moftim, “and/ sons, children,” (n ‘mankind,” (n ms) which/ who/ whom to/ for/ belonging wonders,” (n mp) incited,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, 3ms) part, 3ms pronom) v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal, haddarim “we/ you (mp)/ they, those residing, living,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act she’ya’asu, “that/ which/ who/ whom pesel, “a graven image, idol” (n these,” (prep, 3mp they will make, do,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic le’ha’chaya, “to/ for/ belonging to the beast,” (prep, n she’yesh, “that/ chavurot, “bruises, wounds,” (n mp) chorev, “sword,” which/ who/ whom her/it,” (prep, 3fs) v’she’nitrafea, “and/ but/ so/ or she/it was healed,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, <note type="footnote" n="377">The Hebrew word for “idol” is לספ (pesel) and means that it was designed to be worshipped. And in Revelation 13:15, the pesel (idol) of the beast receives a spirit and soul and is able to speak. Therefore, if this is created by man, then this appears to hint of something similar to a hologram, or tangible hologram that could  potentially manifest in every home. 378 Second Temple use in The Midrash of Philo from c. 10 CE to 50 CE.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.15">And it was permitted to give to the idol379 of the beast a spirit and a soul, so that it would be able to speak. And whoever did not want to pray380 to the idol of the beast would be killed.  The Scriptures: And there was given to him to give spirit to the image of the beast, that the image of the beast should both speak and cause to be killed as many as would not worship the image of the beast.  Aramaic: And it was given him to put life into the image of the beast of prey; and to cause that all they who would not worship the image of the beast of prey, should be slain: v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ noten, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ l’pesel, “to/ for/ belonging to a graven image, ha’cha’ya, “the beast,” (n fs) ruach, “breath, Spirit, wind,” (n v’nefesh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) him/it,” (prep, 3ms idol,” (prep, n ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part, k’dei, “be able, she’yuval, “that/ l’ debir, “to speak, talk,” (v. Pi’el, inf v’ la’asot, “and/ mi, “who?” (inter yirtze, “he/it shall want,” (v, Nif’al, yiqtol, fut 3ms) according to, as, in which/ who/ whom which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) order to,” (conj) brought, result in,” (v. Hif’il, pssv fut, l’pesel, “to/ for/ belonging to a graven image,” she’yahareg, “that/ which/ who/ whom beast,” (prep, n fs) killed,” (rel part, v. Nif’al, yiqtol, fut,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.16">It made them all - the great and the small, the wealthy and the poor, the slaves and the free – take a sign382, 383  in his right hand or in their foreheads,   The Scriptures: And he causes all, both small and great, and rich and poor, and free and slave, to be given a mark upon their right hand or upon their foreheads,  Aramaic: and to cause that all, great and small, rich and poor, bond and free, should receive a mark on their right hands, or upon their foreheads; v’ asah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/ it did, made,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, l’ kulam, “to/ for/ belonging to all of them,” (prep, n ms, v’hak’tanim, “the ha’ashirim, “the rich, wealthy, abundant,” (n ha’avadim, “the slaves, servants,” “and/ but/ so/ or v’hamishochrcharim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) siman, “symbol, b’yad, “in/ with/ by (the) hand,” (prep, n y’mino, “his/its right hand,” (n b' mitzcheihem, “in/ with/ by their omen, mnemonic added mater lectionis</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.17">so that the only one who has the sign in his hands,387 or forehead, or the name belonging to the beast, or the number of its name would be able to buy or sell.  The Scriptures: and that no one should be able to buy or sell except he that has the mark or the name of the beast, or the number of his name.  Aramaic: so that no one might be able to buy or to sell, except those who had the mark of the name of the beast of prey, or the number of his name. k’dei, “be able, sum, “any,” (in a echad, “one,” (card liknot, “to buy, to according to, as, in which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) shall be able,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, order to,” (conj) limkor, “to sell,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf rak, “only, just,” ba’im, "they, those she’yesh, “that/ ze, “this,” (pron which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms exists,” (rel part, mnemonic sign,” b’yadei, ‘in/ with/ by (the) hands,” o, “or,” (conj) ba’mitzcho, “in/ with/ by his/its o, “or,” (conj) hashem, “the name,” (n ms) ‘belonging to,” (prep, n mp constr) forehead,” (prep, n o, “or,” (conj) ha’mispar, “the number,” (n ms) ‘belonging to,” <note type="footnote" n="384">Second Temple use in The War of the Jews by Josephus in Rome in c.73 CE. 385 “Yad” can mean “hand” but can include their arm. 386 Refer to Revelation 9:4. 387 The word “hand” is singular in the previous verse is plural in this verse while the word “foreheads” is plural in the previous verse but is singular in this verse.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.13.18">Here is wisdom and understanding: Appoint one who understands, to calculate the number of the beast, for it is a number belonging to a person, for you will discover the sum is six hundred and sixty-six.  The Scriptures: Here is the wisdom! He who has understanding, let him calculate the number of the beast, for it is the number of a man, and his number is six hundred and sixty six.  Aramaic: Here is wisdom: let him that hath intelligence, compute the number of the beast of prey; for it is the number of a man: and its number is six hundred and sixty and six. b’kan “in/ with/ by here, now,” (prep, shim, “appoint, be’al, “in/ with/ by regarding,” (prep) there exists,” (part) “wisdom,” (n fs) put,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, understanding,” shekel, “prudence, la’cheshov, “to hi’mispar, “the number,” (n ms) hi, “she/it,” (3fs should, must,” (adj devise, think, plan, esteem, calculate, “from/ of/ out of the beast,” (prep, n understanding,” (n judgment, imagine, mispar, “number,” echad, “one,” (card vatimatzey, “and/ but/ so/ or you will find, discover,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, hi, “she/it,” (pron) “belonging to,” mankind” (n, ms) shesh, “six,” (card me’ot, “hundred,” v’ shishim,” and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’ shishah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) six, (card num) sixty,” (card num)</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.14">
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.1">Then I saw a Lamb standing on Mount Zion, and with him one hundred and forty-four thousand,388 on whose foreheads were inscribed the Name of His Father.  The Scriptures: And I looked and saw a Lamb standing on Mount Tsiyon, and with Him one hundred and forty-four thousand, having His Father’s Name written upon their foreheads.  Aramaic: And I looked, and behold, a Lamb stood on mount Zion; and with him the number of a hundred and forty and four thousand, having his name and the name of his Father written upon their foreheads. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, se, “Lamb,” (n cs) echad, “one” (card har, “mountain, qatal, past, 3ms) v’imo, “and/ but/ so/ or with him/it,” mea, “hundred,” v’arba’a, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’arbaim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’aleihem.”and/ but/ so/ or upon inscribed, issued” (v. Nif'al act part, father,” (n ms, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.2">I heard a voice391 from the heavens, like a tumult of many waters, and as the sound of many voices. The voice that I heard was like the voice of a harp.  The Scriptures: And I heard a voice out of the heaven, like the voice of many waters, and like the voice of loud thunder, and I heard the sound of harpists playing their harps.  Aramaic: And I heard a sound from heaven, as the sound of many waters, and as the sound of great thunder; and the sound which I heard, was like that of harpers striking on their harps. veshamati, “and/ echad, “one,” (card k’r’ash, “like/ as mayim, “water(s),” great, large,” (adj heavens,” (prep, n rattling, shaking, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, commotion” (prep, ve’ke’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or like/ as kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) ve’ha’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or the she’shamati, “that/ which/ who/ whom haya, “he/it was,” ke’kol, “like/ as large,” (adj mp) voice, sound,” (n qatal, past, 3ms) sound,” (prep, n sound,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kinor, “stringed violin, harp or lyre, a man skilled</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.3">They were singing392 the renewed song before the throne, the four living creatures, and the elders. No one was able to learn this song but the hundred and forty-four thousand that He redeemed from the ground.393  The Scriptures: And they sang a renewed song before the throne, and before the four living creatures, and the elders. And no one was able to learn that song except the hundred and forty-four thousand who were redeemed from the earth.  Aramaic: And they sang a new song before the throne, and before the four Animals and the Elders: and no one was able to learn that song, except the hundred and forty and four thousand who were redeemed from the earth. u’mezamrim, “we/ b’shir, in/ with/ by (the) song of (prep, chodesh, “renew, or new” (adj ms) harba, “the four,” chayot, “beasts, living creatures,” you (mp)/ they, before the face of, before me, in front throne,” (n ms) those singing,” (v. Pi’el, act part, mp) Note: The song is either new (adj ms) or renewed (act v’ha’zkenim, “and/ v' sum, “and/ but/ so/ any,” (in a neg echad, “one,” (card yuchal, ‘he/it will l’lmod, “to learn, hazot, “this, this one,”’ (fs proun) elders,” (adj mp) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, rak, “only, just,” iIlu, “these, those, v’arba, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) four,” v’arbaim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the0 forty,” (card num) she’kana, “that/ the following,” which/ who/ whom he/it purchased,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ground,” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="391">Literally, "one voice."</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.4">These are those397 who did not sin with women398 and are like virgins399 who go after the Lamb and were redeemed for the firstborn of Yehovah and the Lamb.  The Scriptures: They are those who were not defiled with women, for they are maidens. They are those following the Lamb wherever He leads them on. They were redeemed from among men, being first-fruits to Elohim and to the Lamb.  Aramaic: These are they who have not defiled themselves with women, for they are virgins. These are they who followed the Lamb, whithersoever he went. These have been redeemed by Jesus from among men, the first fruits to God and the Lamb. v' eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, banashim, “with/ in/ by/ with (the) women,” (prep, n v’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (pron k’ be’tulot, “like/ as virgins,” (prep, which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) the following,” (3mp pronom) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’ho’lekim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/you ha’se, “the lamb,” v’he’mah, “and/ but/ so/ or they, niqnim, “we/ you l’ bkorot, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) (mp)/ they (m), these, those,” (3mp those who go,’’ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, purchased,” (v. Nif'al, act part ve’ha’se, “and/ but/ so/ or the lamb,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.5">In their spirit is no deceit, for they are blameless before the throne of Yehovah.  The Scriptures: And in their mouth was found no falsehood, for they are blameless before the throne of Elohim.  Aramaic: And in their mouth was found, no falsehood; for they are without faults. v’ein, “and/ but/ so/ or there is/are not,” (neg part) be’ruchim, “in/ with/ by their remiya, “fraud, deception, deceit, cheating,” (n fs) v’hem, “and/ but/ “blameless, clean, before the face of, before me, in front throne,” (n ms) spirit,” (prep, n cs, Yehovah <note type="footnote" n="397">This word can be both men and women (i.e. common pronoun). Third common plural or masculine plural pronoun. In other words, this can be both men, women, and possibly children chosen to be one of the 144,000.  398 Can mean “idolatry,” as in Isaiah 1:21; Jeremiah 2:2; 3:7-11; Ezekiel 16; Nahum 3:1-4; Hosea 1:3, 4:15; 5:5; Lamentations 1:1 and Matthew 12:39. 399 The kaf (כ) prefix means, “like” or “as.” This means that the 144,000 are not virgins, but they are “like virgins.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.6">Then I saw a messenger hovering in the midst of the heavens, and he had a powerful notice401 to announce to the inhabitants on the earth, the peoples and the nations.   The Scriptures: And I saw another messenger flying in mid-heaven, holding the everlasting Good News to announce to those dwelling on the earth, even to every nation and tribe and tongue and people,  Aramaic: And I saw another angel flying in heaven: and with blood, he had the everlasting gospel, to proclaim to dwellers on the earth, and to every nation and tribe and tongue and people; ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, mal’ach, “angel, echad, “one,” (card ha’shamayim, “the heavens,” (n mp) ve’lo, “and/ but/ so messenger,” (n ms) hovered,” (v. Pi’el, qatal, past, 3ms) him/it,” (prep, 3ms haya, “he/it was,” echad, “one,” (card Le’hodia, “to make known, announce,” (v Hifil, inf constr) ha’dorim, “the inhabitants,” (n strength, vigor," belonging to these, qatal, past, 3ms) gilayon, “writing, tablet, sheet, roll,” ha’amim, “the peoples,” (n mp) v’l’umim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) nations,” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="400">See this word and spelling in The War of the Jews 2:8. 401 This idiom also means, “powerful writing.”  402 This word, ףחר (richef) is a rare word not found in any Sefaria.or source until Machberet Menachem, Letter Resh, Introduction 2 of about c. 950 CE.  However, a form of it is in Genesis 1:2 when Elohim brooded/ swept/ hovered over the face of the water.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.7">He said in a loud voice, “Fear Yehovah!  Pray to Him for the day of judgment comes.  Pray to Him who created the heavens, the earth, the sea, and the wellsprings.  The Scriptures: saying with a loud voice, “Fear Elohim and give esteem to Him, because the hour of His judgment has come. And worship Him who made the heaven and the earth, and sea, and fountains of water.”  Aramaic: saying with a loud voice, Worship God, and give glory to him; because the hour of his judgment is come; and adore ye Him, who made heaven and earth, and the sea, and the fountains of water. v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” b’kol, “with/ in/ by (the) voice,” (prep, gadol, “great, big, yeru, “(to men) Yehovah v’asu, “and/ but/ tfilatchem, “your (mp) prayer,” (n ms, 2mp pronom) so/ or you shall do, (v. Pa’al/Qal, Imp, qatal, past, 3ms) ha’yom, “the day, ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, va’asu, “and/ but/ so/ or you shall do, te’fila, “prayer,” (n him/it,” (prep, 3ms law/the sentence, verdict,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, imp, she’bara, “that/ ha’sah’mayim, “the heavens,” (n ve’ha’eretz, “and/ ve’ha’yam, “and/ but/ so/ or the sea,” be’ha’be’erot, “and/ but/ so/ or belonging to this,” which/ who/ whom he/it created,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) wellsprings” (n fp) <note type="footnote" n="403">The final nun makes it clear these are two words. However, in the early 1900’s the Manchester Gaster 1616 scribe, who copied from the Cochin manuscript, assumed they were to be combined words to produce a Greek transliterated word for “Good news,” (evangelion).  404 For an exact match of this spelling see The Book of Maccabees II 12:3.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.8">After this, the voice of another messenger shouted, “Fallen!  Fallen is the great city Babel!405  Because she406 was appeased with the wine of her fornication for all nations.”  The Scriptures: And another messenger followed, saying, “Baḇel is fallen, is fallen, that great city, because she has made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her whoring.”  Aramaic: And another, a second angel followed him, saying: Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great, which made all nations drink of the wine of the rage of her whoredom. v’achar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) ze, “this,” (pron ha' kol, “the voice, ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, malach, “angel, ve’tza’ak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it messenger,” (n ms) another, different,” shouted, cried,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, naflah, “she/it fell, Babel (name) ha’ir, “the city’ (n ha’gedola, “the hi, “she/it,” (3fs fell, is fallen,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, big, large,” (adj fs) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, hushkit, “he/it was quieted, appeased,’ im, “with,” (prep) ha’yayin, ‘the wine,” (n ms) shel, “to/ for/ of’ znutah, “her/its le’kol, “to/ for/ belonging to all,” peoples, nations,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, fornication,” (n fs) <note type="footnote" n="405">Isaiah 21:9. 406 Although the verb is masculine singular, the word it is associated with is feminine, so this is a gender mismatch and the pronoun "he/it" was used instead of “she/it.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.9">Then the third messenger came and said in a loud voice, “If anyone prays to the idol of the beast and takes the sign on his hand or on his forehead,”  The Scriptures: And a third messenger followed them, saying with a loud voice, “If anyone worships the beast and his image, and receives his mark upon his forehead or upon his hand,  Aramaic: And another, a third angel followed them, saying with a loud voice: If any man shall worship the beast of prey and its image, and shall receive its mark upon his forehead or on his hand, v’achar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) ze, “this,” (pron, ba,”I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, malach, “angel, ha’she’lishi, “the third,” (ord num) ve’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” be’kol, “with/ by/ messenger,” (n ms) in (the) voice,” qatal, past, 3ms) gadol “great, loud,” (adj ms) b’im, “in/ with/ by if, when, whether,” she’echad, “that/ which/ who/ whom one,” (card num) ya’ase, “he/it will t’filato, “his/its prayer,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) l’ha’pesel, “to/ for/ v’ha’chaya, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to the beast,” (prep, n fs) belonging to the graven image, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, idol,” (prep, n ms) ve’yiach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it will take,” (v. o, “or,” (conj) al, “upon, on,” mitzcho, “his/its forehead,” (n ms, hand,” (n ms, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, mnemonic sign,” <note type="footnote" n="407">See Mishnah Chullin 2:4 for a spelling match. 408 See first occurrence of this word in Revelation 13:17.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.10">“then he will drink from the wine of Yehovah’s wrath. There is the cup of wrath.409 And he will be punished with fire and brimstone in the presence of His holy messengers and the Lamb.”  The Scriptures: he also shall drink of the wine of the wrath of Elohim, which is poured out undiluted into the cup of His wrath. And he shall be tortured with fire and sulphur before the set-apart messengers and before the Lamb.  Aramaic: he also shall drink of the wine of the wrath of God, which is poured undiluted into the cup of his indignation, and shall be tormented with fire and sulphur, before the holy angels, and before the throne. ze, “this,” (pron, yishte, “he/it will m’hyyin, “from/ of, (the) wine,” charon, “to for of fierceness, wrath, ha'yesh, “the, that/ Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, b’kos, “in/ with/ by (the) glass, ha’ charon, “the y’anesh, “he/it will be punished,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, b’ esh, “in/ with/ v’sofrit, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) sulfur, brimstone,” (n fs) fierceness, wrath,” before the face of, before me, in front cup,” (prep, n fs) flame,” (prep, n fs) Idiom: His holy messengers v’ha’se, “and/ but/ or/ so the lamb,” (n melachav, “his/its messengers, angels,” (n ms, 3mp pronom) ha’kodashim, “the saints, holy ones,” (adj</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.11">So, the smoke from their punishment will ascend forever. There will be no rest day or night for those who took the sign and prayed to the idol.  The Scriptures: “And the smoke of their torture goes up forever and ever. And they have no rest day or night, those worshipping the beast and his image, also if anyone receives the mark of his name.”  Aramaic: And the smoke of their torment ascendeth up for ever and ever; and there is no rest, by day or by night, to those that worship the beast of prey and its image. m’ onesh, “from/ of (the) penalty, punishment (prep, yelech, “he/it will, go (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) lemala, “upwards, up,” (prep, adv) them,” (prep, 3mp “and/ but/ so/ or the smoke,” (n ms) Idiom for "forever" v lo, “and/ so/ but/ or ‘no/not,” (neg yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) lahem, “to/ for/ of/ them,’ (prep, 3mp menucha, “rest, calm, serenity,” (n m’ olam, “from/ of (the), eternity, forever,” (prep, n ms) v’ ad, “and/ but/so /or until, up to,” (prep) olam, “world, universe, eternity, forever,” (n ms, const) yom, “day,” (n ms) v’layla, “and/ but/ so/ or night,” (n le’ilu, “whereas, if, she’lakchu, “that/ which/ who/ whom l' pesel, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) but considering, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ following,” (prep, mnemonic sign,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Hit’pael, act part, <note type="footnote" n="409">See Jeremiah 25:15-17.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.12">In this there is hope for the holy ones who do the commandments of Yehovah and believe in Yeshua.  The Scriptures: Here is the endurance of the set-apart ones, here are those guarding the commands of Elohim and the belief of  עשוהי.  Aramaic: Here is the patience of the saints, who keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus. b’kan, “in/ with/ by here, now,” tikva, “hope,” (n m’ha’kodashim, “from/ of (the) v’b’kan, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by here,” (prep, adv) ha’osim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those there exists,” (part) there exists,” (part) saints, holy ones,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, Yehovah u’ma’aminim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ commandments, commands” (n fp) with/ by Yeshua” <note type="footnote" n="410">See first occurrence of this word in Revelation 13:16.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.13">Then I heard a small voice from heaven saying to me, “Write!  'From this time forward, the holy ones, they - the dead due to the sanctification of the Name411 - (and truly the Spirit said) they live by their works, because their works follow them.'”  The Scriptures: And I heard a voice out of the heaven saying to me, “Write, ‘Blessed are the dead who die in the Master from now on.’ “Yes,” says the Spirit, “in order that they rest from their labours, and their works follow with them.”  Aramaic: And I heard a voice from heaven, saying: Write, Blessed are the dead that die in the Lord, henceforth: yes, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their toils; for their deeds do accompany them. v’shamati, “and/ Idiom: “voice of God” amar, “he/it said,” katov, “(to men) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) bat kol, “voice of God” or “small voice,” qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kdoshim, “the saints, holy ones,” (n mp) Literally: “they the dead” Idiom: “Sanctification of the Name” m’achshav, “from/ he’mah, “they, these, those,” (3mp kiddush, “holiness,” (n ms) thenceforth,” (prep, ha’shem, “the name,” (n ms) ham’tim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those dying,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, mp) v’emet, “and/ but/ so/ or truth, truly,” Literally: “she who the Spirit” amar, “he/it said,” Literally: “they living” m’ma’asehem, “from/ of their deeds, works,” (prep, n ms, 3ms hi, “she/it,” (3fs pron) qatal, past, 3ms) she’heimah, “that/ which/ who/ they, she’ruach, “that/ which/ who/ whom (the) (rel part, pron 3mp) spirit, breath,” (prep, n cs) shochnim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those residing, living,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, mp) m’ma’asehem, “from/ of their deeds, works,” (prep, n ms, 3mp holhim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those achareihem, “after (v. Pa’al/Qal, act</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.14">I saw one sitting on a white cloud who had the appearance of a man,416 and on his head was a crown of gold, and in his hand was a sickle.  The Scriptures: And I looked and saw a white cloud, and sitting on the cloud was One like the Son of Aḏam, having on His head a golden crown, and in His hand a sharp sickle.  Aramaic: And I looked, and lo, a white cloud; and upon the cloud sat one who was like the Son of man; and on his head was a crown of gold, and in his hand a sharp sickle. v’rai’ti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, anan, “cloud,” (n echad, “one,” (card lavan, “white,” v’alav, “and/ but/ so/ or on, upon, over he/it,” (prep yashav, “he/it sat, echad, “one,” (card Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kidmut, “like/ as likeness,” (prep, n v’al, “and/ but/ so/ keter, “crown,” (n zahav, “gold,” (n mankind” (n ms) head,” (n ms, 3ms “and/ but/ so/ or in/ by/ with his/its hand,” (prep, n ms, chermesh, “the sickle,” (n ms) echad, “one,” (card</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.15">And another messenger came from the house of prayer417 and cried in a loud voice to the one who sat on the cloud, “Harvest with your sickle!  For the time of harvest has come!”  The Scriptures: And another messenger came out of the Dwelling Place, crying with a loud voice to the One sitting on the cloud, “Send Your sickle and reap, because the hour has come for You to reap, because the harvest of the earth is ripe.”  Aramaic: And another angel came out of the temple, crying with a loud voice, to him that sat on the cloud. u’malach, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) m’ bayit, “of/ from v’ tza’ak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it shouted, cried, complained,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, b’kol, “in/ with/ by another, different,’ added mater lectionis angel, messenger,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, sound,” (prep, n gadol, “great, big, large,” (adj ms) she’yashav, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it sat, dwelled,” ha’ the “cloud,” (n r’mais, “sickle, sythe,” (n ms) belonging to this,” belonging to you,” qatal, past, 3ms) ktzor,” (to a man) Harvest! Reap!” (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, ha’ et, “the time,” ha’ ktzirah, “the her/its harvest,” (n ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.16">So, he who sat on the cloud struck with his sickle and he harvested. v’ze, “and/ but/ so/ she’ yashav, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it sat, dwelled,” hika, “he/it beat, hit, struck, smote,” b’charmaish, “in/ shilo, “that/ which/ with/ by (the) sickle,” (prep, n (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, 3ms 3ms) belongs to him/it,” qatal, past, 3ms) v’katzar, “and/ but/ harvested, reaped,” qatal, past, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="417">See Revelation 11:19. 418 See Maccabees I 7:37, dating c.145CE to 125CE, for the first occurrence of this phrase.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.17">Another messenger went to the heavens, and in his hand was a snare.419  The Scriptures: And another messenger came out of the Dwelling Place which is in the heaven, and he too held a sharp sickle.  Aramaic: And another angel came out of the temple that is in heaven, having also a sharp sickle. u’malach, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) l’shamayim, “to/ for/ belonging to haya, “he/it was,” (v. P’al/Qal, qatal, ma’agal, “circle, another, different,” “and/ but/ or/ so in/ with/ by his/its hand,” (prep, n fs) angel, messenger,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, entrenchment, track, snare,” (n heavens,” ‘(n mp) echad, “one,” (card na bo ravim: “Please come Rome” Idiom: The golden calf representing the sin of the Northern Kingdom The inserted marginal note says, "Please come Romans." It appears to be in a different hand from other marginal notes and from the original scribe. This could be simply a note by someone who owned the manuscript and made a comment. It is not included in the translation.</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.14.18">Another messenger came out from the altar having authority over fire and cried out with a loud voice to the one who had the sickle, saying, "Strike with your sickle and reap the grapes of the land, for its fruit are ripe."421  And the messenger harvested with his sickle the grapes of the land and threw them into the great winepress of the wrath of Yehovah.  The Scriptures: And another messenger came out from the slaughter-place, having authority over the fire, and he cried with a loud cry to him having the sharp sickle, saying, “Send your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of the vine of the earth, because her grapes are ripe.”  Aramaic: And another angel came out from the altar, having authority over fire. And he cried with a loud voice, to him who had the sharp sickle, saying: Thrust in thy sickle which is sharp, and gather the clusters of the vineyard of the earth, because the grapes of the earth are ripe. u’malach, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) yotzei, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it goes m’hamizbeach, “from/ of the v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, another, different,” angel, messenger,” out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, altar,” (prep, n ms) authority,” (n fs) ha’esh, “the fire,” v’’tza’ak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it shouted,” (v. be’kol, “In/ with/ by (the) voice,” gadol, “great’ ‘loud,” (adj ms) she’hayah, “that/ which/ who/ whom belonging to this,” he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” ba’magal, “with/ by/ in (the) sickle,” she’lach, “to you,” v’ketzor, “and/ but/ so/ or (to a scourge, thrust,” (v. Hif’il, imp, him/it,” (prep, 3ms qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, imp, perot’ha, “her/its va’yach, “and/ but/ so/ or to he/it will Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic anvi, “grapes of” (n mp constr) (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, nit’vshel, “he/it was ripened,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, pssv past, 3ms) ha’malach, “the ba’magal, “with/ by/  (the) sickle,” v’katzar, “and/ but/ et, (DO marker) a’nvey, “the grapes angel, messenger,” which/ who/ whom to/ for/ belonging harvested,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’zarak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it threw,” b’yekev, “in/ with/ by (the) winepress, wine vat” (prep, n gadol, “great, loud,” (adj ms) ha’charon, “fierce, fierceness, wrath, fury, anger,” (n Yehovah qatal, past, 3ms) Translation #1: And the winepress was outside the city, and the blood of the winepress rose to the bridles of the horses through one thousand six hundred field graves.   Translation #2: And the winepress was outside the city, and the blood of the winepress rose to the bridles of the horses trampling one thousand six hundred field graves.  The Scriptures: (19) And the messenger thrust his sickle into the earth and gathered the vine of the earth, and threw it into the great winepress of the wrath of Elohim. 20 And the winepress was trodden outside the city, and blood came out of the winepress, up to the bridles of the horses, for about one thousand six hundred stadia  Aramaic: (19) And the angel thrust in his sickle on the earth, and gathered the vintage of the earth, and cast [it] into the wine-press of the wrath of the great God. 20 And the wine-press was trodden, up to the horses' bridles, for a thousand and six hundred furlongs. v’ha’yekev, “and/ hayah, “he/it was,” m’chutz, “from/ of v’ha’dahm, “and/ but/ or/ so (the) blood,” (n ms) me’yekev, “from/ belonging (the) city,” (prep, n fs) qatal, past, 3ms) outward,” (n ms) winepress,” (prep, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ad, “until, as far shel, “to for of, belonging to,” elef, “a thousand,” v’ shesh, “and/ but/ so/ or six,” bridle, reign,” (n away, because of, toward,” (adv) or trample(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, me’ot, “hundred,” kivrat, “graves of,” <note type="footnote" n="422">The word לשב (b’shal) means, “mature” or “ripe.”  If the scribe transposed (or reversed the order of) the first two letters, this would be a Second Temple word meaning, “it was ripened.” 423 For this exact spelling see Book of Jubilees 24:41.</note> <note type="footnote" n="424">The last two words are crossed out in the manuscript.  However, the writing indicates that the strikethrough was probably done by a different scribe, so the original words was kept in the translation.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.15">
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.1">Then I saw miracles and great wonders in the heavens: seven messengers came, and they had the seven last plagues. In them is the total wrath of the anger of Yehovah!   The Scriptures: And I saw another sign in the heaven, great and marvellous: seven messengers having the seven last plagues, for the wrath of Elohim was ended in them.  Aramaic: And I saw another prodigy in heaven, great and wonderful; seven angels, having seven plagues, the last in order, because with them the wrath of God is consummated. v’ ra’iti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, nisim, “wonders, miracles,” (n mp) added mater lectionis gdolim, “great, big, large,” (adj. b’shamayim, “in/ shiv’a, “seven,” marvelous,” (adj, heavens,” (prep, n ba’im, “we/ you (mp)/ they come, go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, v’ lahem, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ hayah, “he/it was,” nega’im, “strokes, plagues, diseases, ha’acharonim, “last,” (adj, mp) messengers,” (n qatal, past, 3ms) marks, plague spots, marks of leprosy,” (n mp) them,” (prep, 3mp b’ hem, “in/ with/ by them,” (prep, ku’la, “all, the whole, totality, ha’ charon, “wrath, af, “anger, nose,” everything,” (prep, n ms, 3fs pronom) Yehovah,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.2">I saw something like a sea of glass428 mixed with fire. And which those who overcame the beast, and its idol were standing by the sea of glass, and they had lyres of Yehovah.  The Scriptures: And I saw like a sea of glass mixed with fire, and those overcoming the beast and his image and his mark and the number of his name, standing on the sea of glass, holding harps of Elohim.  Aramaic: And I saw as it were, a sea of glass mixed with fire: and they, who had been victorious over the beast of prey, and over its image, and over the number of its name, were standing on the sea of glass; and they had the harps of God. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, k’mo, “like, as, yam, “a sea,” (n tzlochit, “bowl, flask, vial, jar, cruze” (n ms) im, “with,” (prep) esh, “fire, flame” (v.Pa’al/Qal, qatal, eilu, “and/ but/ so / she’nitzchu, “that/ which/ who/ whom im, “with,” (prep) ha’ chaya, “the beast,” (n fs) u’pesel, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) idol, image,” (n ms) omdim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those or which, some, certain,” (pron, which/ who/ whom to/ for/ belonging to him/it,” (prep, they overcame,” (rel part, v. Pi’el, qatal, past, 3mp) Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’ yam, “sea,” (n ha’ tzlochit, “bowl, vial, flask, saucer,” v’ lahem, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ hayah, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, past, kinorot, “lyres, harps” (n mp) near, by, beside,” them,” (prep, 3mp</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.3">They sang433 the song of Moses and the song of the Lamb, saying, “Great are the works of Yehovah, Elohim of Armies!434  Justice and truth are your ways, King of kings!”  The Scriptures: And they sing the song of Mosheh the servant of Elohim, and the song of the Lamb, saying, “Great and marvellous are Your works, הוהי Ěl Shaddai! Righteous and true are Your ways, O Sovereign of the set-apart ones!  Aramaic: And they sing the song of Moses the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb, saying: Great and marvellous are thy deeds, Lord God Almighty; just and true are thy ways, O King of worlds. mosheh, Moses,” v’ ha’shir, “and/ ha’se, “the lamb,” v’ omrim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those saying,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ singing,” (v. Pi’el, g’dolah, “great,” ma’asei, “deeds, works,” (n mp) Yehovah Elohei, “God(s) of…,” (n mp, plural const) ha’ tzva’ot, “hosts, armies, legions” (n tzedek, “justice, fairness,” (n ms) v’emet, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) truth,” drachecha, “your melech, “king,” (n ha’melachim, “the paths,” (n fp, 2ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.4">“Who does not fear You and give praise to Your Name?  For You alone439 are holy!  People shall come and bow down before You, for Your judgments are revealed!”  The Scriptures: “Who shall not fear You, O הוהי, and esteem Your Name? Because You alone are kind. Because all nations shall come and worship before You, for Your righteousnesses have been made manifest.”  Aramaic: Who shall not fear thee, O Lord, and glorify thy name? Because thou only art holy and just: Because all nations shall come and worship before thee, since thy righteousnesses have been revealed. u’mi, “and/ but/ lo, “no, ‘not,” (neg yir’e, “he/it will lefanecha, “before you, before your face,” (prep, 2ms shevach, “praise,” l’ shemecha, “to/ for/ belonging to your name,” (prep, v’liten, “and/ but/ see,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) atah, “you,” (2ms kadosh, “holy,” kol, “all of, all, every,” (n ms) people, nation,” (n (adv, 3ms pronom) yavo’u, “they shall vavishtachu, “and/ lefanecha, “before you, before your face,” (prep, 2ms nitgala, “he/it was but/ so/ or they shall bow,” (v. Hit’pael, yiqtol, “your judgments,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (v, Hi’tpael qatal, <note type="footnote" n="433">The (root: רמז) means song, might and plucking: Hebrew and Aramaic Lexicon of the Old Testament (HALOT). According to some kohanim (priests) in Israel, this word means the “Power of God in the music.” See Revelation 5:9. 434 The first occurrence is seen in Hosea 12:6.  435 See The War of the Jews 2:16:4. 436 Literally, “The song of Moses” and is found in Tzafnat Pa'neach on Torah c. 1905 - 1935.  437 Literally, “Yehovah, Elohim of Armies (or Hosts).”  This phrase is found in First Temple Minor Prophets Hosea 12:6 and Amos 3:13, 6:14. 438 Literally, “King of Kings.” This phrase is found in Ezra 7:12 and Daniel 2:37.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.5">And after this, I saw that the Ark of the Covenant in the heavens opened.  The Scriptures: And after this I looked and saw the Dwelling Place of the Tent of Witness in the heaven was opened.  Aramaic: And after this I beheld, and the temple of the tabernacle of the testimony in heaven, was opened. Idiom: "after this way" raiti, “I saw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, she’niftach, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it was opened,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, aron, “ark,” (n ms) ha’brit, “the b’shamayim, “in/ covenant,” (n fs) heavens,” (prep, n vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.6">Then the seven messengers having the seven plagues went out, clothed in white garments, belts of gold on their waist.  The Scriptures: And out of the Dwelling Place came the seven messengers having the seven plagues, dressed in clean bright linen, and having their chests girded with golden bands.  Aramaic: And the seven angels who had the seven plagues, went forth from the temple, clothed in clean splendid linen, and girded about their breast with girdles of gold. v’yatzei, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ lachutz, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) outside, out, (prep, mal’achim, “angel, she’haya, “that/ la’hem, “to/ for/ messenger,” (n which/ who/ whom he/it goes out,” (Pa’al/Qal, act he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, them,” (prep, 3mp nega’im, “strokes, plagues, diseases, levush, “and/ but/ b’m’l’vushim, “in/ with/ by of/ from (the) garments,” l’vinim, ‘“in/ with/ by (the) whites,” (prep, adj mp) vagagor, “and/ but/ zahav, “gold,” (n marks, plague spots, marks of leprosy,” (n mp) dressed,” (adj, ms) girdles,” (n mp) matni’im, “their hips, waist,” (prep, n mp 3mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="442">See Revelation 1:19 for more information on this Second Temple idiom. 443 See Revelation 11:19 for more details.  444 It appears the scribe erroneously eliminated the final mem. 445 For this spelling see The Midrash of Philo 8:21:4</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.7">And one of the four living creatures gave the seven messengers seven bowls of gold filled with the wrath of Yehovah, who lives everlasting to everlasting.  The Scriptures: And one of the four living creatures gave to the seven messengers seven golden bowls filled with the wrath of Elohim who lives forever and ever.  Aramaic: And one of the four Animals gave to those seven angels seven cups of gold, full of the wrath of God who liveth for ever and ever. v’echad, “and/ but/ so/ or one,” (card m’ha’arba, “from/ of the four,” (prep, natan, “he/it gave,” l’ha’shiv’a, “to/ for/ belonging to the seven,” (prep, mal’achim, “messengers, angels,” (n mp) sheva, “seven,” creatures, beasts,” qatal, past, 3ms) ka’arot, “bowls, plates, saucers” shel, “of,” (prep) zabavm “gold,” (n m’l’eim, “full,” bacharon, “with/ Yehovah ha’chay, “living,” in/ by (the) wrath,” m’olam, “from/ of everlasting,” (prep, v’ ad, “and/ but/ so/ or until,” (prep) “everlasting,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.15.8">Then the house of prayer was filled with smoke, and the glory of Yehovah filled the tabernacle. Thus no one was permitted inside until the seven messengers completed the seven plagues.  The Scriptures: And the Dwelling Place was filled with smoke from the esteem of Elohim and from His power, and no one was able to enter the Dwelling Place until the seven plagues of the seven messengers were ended.  Aramaic: And the temple was filled with smoke, from the glory of God and from his power; and no one was able to enter the temple, until the seven plagues of the seven angels were accomplished. Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic uveit, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) house b’ashan, “with/ in v’kavod, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) glory,” Yehovah male, “he/it was “prayer,” (n fs) smoke,” (prep, n qatal, past, 3ms) nitmalea, “she/it was filled,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, pssv past, 3fs) et, (DO marker) ha’ mishkan, “the dwelling place, v’sum, “and/ but/ so/ or any (in a neg echad, “one,” (card yuchal, “he/it will be able, cannot,” latocha, “to the interior, inside,” tabernacle,” (n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut 3ms) ad, “unto, until,” nega’im, “strokes, plagues, diseases, m’ha’shiv’a, “of/ from the seven,” (prep, card num) mal’achim, “messengers, angels,” (n mp) which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it is marks, plague spots, marks of leprosy,” (n mp) complete,” (rel part, v. Pi’el, act</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.16">
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.1">Then I heard a voice in the house of prayer saying to the seven messengers, “Go and pour out the bowls of the wrath of Yehovah upon the ground!”   The Scriptures: And I heard a loud voice from the Dwelling Place saying to the seven messengers, “Go and pour out the bowls of the wrath of Elohim on the earth.”  Aramaic: And I heard a voice, which said to the seven angels: Go forth, and pour those seven cups of the wrath of God upon the earth. v’shamati, “and/ uveit, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) house v’achar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) l’ha’shiv’a, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) seven,” (prep, “prayer,” (n fs) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mal’achim, “messengers, angels,” (n mp) lechu, “(to a man) yitzku, (to a man) ha’admah, “the ground,” (n fs) ha’charon, “the wrath,” (n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, imp, Pa’al/Qal, imp, saucers” (prep, n added mater lectionis Yehovah</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.2">So, the first one poured out his bowl upon the ground and a skin disease453 broke out on anyone who had the sign of the beast and was praying to its idol.  The Scriptures: And the first went and poured out his bowl upon the earth, and an evil and wicked sore came upon the men, those having the mark of the beast and those worshipping his image.  Aramaic: And the first went, and poured his cup upon the earth; and there was a malignant and painful ulcer upon those men who had the mark of the beast of prey, and who worshipped its image. v’ha’rishon, “and/ ve’yatzak, “and/ but/ so /or he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, (DO marker) ke’aru, “his/its bowl,” (n fs, 3ms first,” (ord numb) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was,” lishchin, “to/ for/ poreach, “he/it broke out,” (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal, al, “upon, in, on, she’haya, “that/ lahem, “to/ for/ which/ who/ whom (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) boil, eruption, skin through,”  (prep) mankind, (n ms) them,” (prep, 3mp disease, blain,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, m’hachaya, “from/ v’ha’mitpallim, “and/ but/ so /or (the) we/ you (mp)/ they pray, those praying,” (v. l’pesel, “to/ for/ symbol, sign,” (n Hit’pael, act part, mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.3">And the second messenger poured his bowl into the sea, and it became blood like from one dying.  And everything in the sea died. vayitzok, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’mahalach, “the angel, messenger,” et, (DO marker) ke’aru, his “bowl, plate, saucer,” (n bayam, “in/ with/ v’haya, “and/ but/ second,” (ord num) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dam, “blood,” (n k’mo, “like, as, memet, “from/ of (the) I/ you (ms)/ he/it die(s),” (prep, vchol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) asher, “that, which, tamot, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those with/ by (the) sea,” v. Pa’al/Qal, act Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="453">This word could refer to several different skin conditions and diseases. The symptoms described in the Torah are unrecognized by physicians today. This is most likely a condition that once existed and will return in the final days. 454 See Exodus 9:9. 455 See Revelation 13:17 for more details on this unique word. 456 See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem. 457 The noun “beast” is feminine, and the pronoun should match the gender of the beast. 458 There are two marks above this word that appear to refer to the marginal note on the right (circled in red). The marginal note is not included in the translation.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.4">Then the third poured his bowl into the wells of water, and it became blood.  The Scriptures: And the third messenger poured out his bowl on the rivers and fountains of water, and they became blood.  Aramaic: And the third angel poured his cup upon the rivers and the fountains of water; and they became blood yatzak, “he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, (DO marker) ke’aru, “his/its b’be’erot, “in/ with/ by (the) wells, cisterns,” mayim, “water(s),” v’haya, “and/ but/ “and/ but/ so / or (the) third (ord bowl,” (n fs, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, qatal, dam, “blood,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.5">And I heard the messenger say, “Yehovah the Righteous, who was and is holy; You, who gave this judgment!”  The Scriptures: And I heard the messenger of the waters saying, “You are righteous, O הוהי, the One who is and who was and who shall be, because You have judged these.  Aramaic: And I heard the angel of the waters say: Righteous art thou, who art and who wast, and art holy; because thou hast done this judgment. v’shamati, “and/ she’ ha’ mal’ach, “that/ which/ who/ whom the angel, omer, “I/ you (ms)/ Yehovah hitzdik, “the ha’haya, “the/that ve’ hoveh, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it is,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, he/it say(s),” (v. righteous,” (adj he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, messenger,” (n ms) v’ kadosh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) atah, “you,” (2ms she’natata, “that/ which/ who/ whom zot, “this,” (pron holy, sacred,” (adj, judgment,” (n ms) allowed,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.6">Translation #1: “Because they spilled the blood of the holy ones and the prophets like water.  And you gave them blood to drink, for they deserve it.” Translation #2: “Because they spilled the blood of the holy ones and the prophets.  And you gave them blood to drink like water, for they deserve it.”  The Scriptures: “Because they have shed the blood of set-apart ones and prophets, and You have given them blood to drink. For they deserve it.”  Aramaic: For they have shed the blood of saints and prophets; and thou hast given them blood to drink, for they deserve it. he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, shafchu, “we/ you (mp)/ they, spill, damei, “blood(s) of,” (n mp, constr) ha’kdoshim, “the holy ones, saints, set-apart ones,” (n ve’nevi’im, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) prophets,” (n mp) k’mayim, “as/ like water(s),” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve'atah, “and/ but/ so/ or you,” (2ms natata, “you (ms) lahem, “to /for/ dam, “blood,” (n lishtot, “to drink,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf Pa’al/Qal, qatal them,” (prep, 3mp l’ze, this (pron, worthy, deserve,” “to/ for/ belonging</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.7">Then I heard another messenger inside the holy place say, “Yes, Elohim of Armies, your judgments are righteous!”   The Scriptures: And I heard another out of the slaughter-place saying, “Yes, הוהי Ěl Shaddai, true and righteous are Your judgments.”  Aramaic: And I heard [one from] the altar say: Yes, Lord God Almighty: true and righteous is thy judgment. v' shama'iti, “and/ mal’ach, “angel, she’diber, “that/ ha’hechal, “the messenger,” (n ms) another, different,” which/ who/ whom “interior, inside, center, midst,” (n holy place,” (n ms) he/it spoke,” (v, Pi’el, qatal, past, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Elohei, “God(s) of ha’ tzva’ot, “hosts, armies, legions” (n mispatecha, “your (ms) judgements,” tzadak, “justice, righteousness,” (n he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.8">Then the fourth poured his bowl into the sun, giving it authority to cause heat on mankind.    The Scriptures: And the fourth messenger poured out his bowl on the sun, and it was given to him to burn men with fire.  Aramaic: And the fourth poured his cup upon the sun: and it was permitted him, to scorch men with fire. v’ ha’ revi’i, “and/ yatzak, “he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, (DO marker) ke’aru, “his/its b’shemesh, “in/ with/ by (the) ve’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or belonging to him/it,” (prep, 3ms bowl,” (n fs, 3ms (ms)/ he/it give(s), authorize, permit,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act fourth,” (adj ms) sun,” (prep, n fs) l’asot, “to do, to make, to create, to cause,” (v. Pi’el, chom, “heat,” (n l‘adam, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) man,” (prep, n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.9">So, it became very hot for mankind, and Yehovah cursed them with plagues, but they did not repent nor give Him honor.   The Scriptures: And men were burned with great heat, and they blasphemed the Name of Elohim who possesses authority over these plagues. And they did not repent, to give Him esteem.  Aramaic: And men were scorched with great heat; and men blasphemed the name of God, who hath authority over these plagues; and they repented not, to give glory to him. v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was, harbeh, “much, many,” (adj ms) chom, “heat,” (n l’adam, ‘“to/ for/ belonging to man,” um’kulelu, “and/ but/ so /or they were cursed,” (v. Pi’el, qatal, pssv l’Yehovah, “to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah (prep, bishvil, “for the sake of, according qatal, past, 3ms) ha’nega’im, “the strokes, plagues, diseases, marks, l’Yehovah, “to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah (prep, Idiom: “they repented” those" (3mp pron) asu, “they did, made,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3mp) marks of leprosy,” tshuvah, “repentance,” (n fs) him/it,” (prep, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.10">Then the fifth poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast and concealed it. So, they gnawed their tongues in the face of despair.  The Scriptures: And the fifth messenger poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast, and his reign became darkened. And they gnawed their tongues from pain.  Aramaic: And the fifth poured his cup on the throne of the beast of prey; and his kingdom became darkness; and they gnawed their tongues, from pain; v’ha’chamishi, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) fifth,” (adj yatzak, “he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, DO pointer ke’aru, “his/its ha' kise, “the throne,” (n ms) bowl,” (n fs, 3ms v’ha’choshech, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it, was made dark, caused to be oto, “him/it” (DO ve' he’ma, “and/ but/ so/ or they, noshchim, “we/ you (mp)/ they bite(s) chew, gnaw,” (v. mipnei, “from/ of away, from before, because of,” (prep) “their tongues,” (n mp, 3mp pronom) these, those,” (3mp Pa’al/Qal, act part, was hidden, was to obscure, confuse (v. Hif’il, qatal, pssv past, 3ms) tza'ar, “like/ as (the) pain, ache, grief, suffering,” <note type="footnote" n="460">This is a unique spelling, see Revelation 2:17 for more details.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.11"/>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.12">Then the sixth poured out his bowl on the Euphrates River. So, the river dried up and became a ruin for the kings462 of the East.  The Scriptures: And the sixth messenger poured out his bowl on the great river Euphrates, and its water was dried up, in order to prepare the way of the sovereigns from the east.  Aramaic: And the sixth poured his cup upon the great river Euphrates; and its waters dried up, so that a way might be prepared for the kings from the rising of the sun. V’hashishi, “and/ et, DO pointer ke’aru, “his/its but/ so/ or the sixth,” (adj ms) bowl,” (n fs, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Note: transliterated v’yavesh, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it et, (DO marker) hanahar,” ‘the river,” (n ms) k’dei, “be able, liheyot, ‘to be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal inf mapala, “a ruin,” l’ha’melachim, according to, as, in “to/ for/ belonging order to,” (conj) to (the) kings,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, she’he’mah, “that/ which/ who/ they, Idiom: “From the east” mimizrach, “from/ of (the) east,” (prep, n ha’ shemesh, “the sun,” (n ms) <note type="footnote" n="461">The scribe numbers this verse as, "10" but the zero was crossed out and replaced with a “1.” See graphic following the interlinear.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.13">Then I saw three unclean creeping things, like frogs, coming out of the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet.  The Scriptures: And I saw coming out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet, three unclean spirits, as frogs, v’ rati, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it saw,” she’halach, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it went, came,” m'pi “from, of, my hata’nin, “the dragon, serpent, umipei, “and/ but/ u’m’piv “and/ but/ so/ or from his/its mouth,” (prep n ms, 1cs pronom) so/ or from/ of/ (the) mouth,” (prep, n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 1cs) mouth,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) dinosaur, sea or river monster, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” ha’ navie, “the prophet,” (n ms) shaker, “false,” v’shlosha, “and/ but/ so/ or three,” kidmut, “like, as similar,” (prep, n tzfard’im, “frogs,” “creeping/ moving “unclean,” (adj things,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.14">For these are the same spirits of Satan doing wonders and signs, who are going to the kings of the earth, and to all the world to gather them for the battle on the day of the Almighty Yehovah.  The Scriptures: for they are spirits of demons, doing signs, which go out to the sovereigns of the entire world, to gather them to the battle of that great day of הוהי the Almighty.  Aramaic: (for they are the spirits of demons, who work prodigies;) and they go forth to all the kings of all the habitable world, to gather them to the battle of the great day of God Almighty. v' eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or whereas, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, ruchot, “spirits,” (n v’osim, “we/ you nisim, “miracles, wonders,” (n mp) added mater lectionis v’otot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) signs,” satan, adversary,” (mp)/ they do, make, create,’’ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act following,” (pron) v’holkim, “and/ l’malchey, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) kings,” (prep, n mp v’le’khol “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to all,” ha’ohlam, “the world,’’ (n ms) but, so/ or we/ you (mp) they, those gather,” (v. Pi’el, marker, 3mp pron) Pa’al/Qal, act part, lamilchama, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) war, battle,” hayom, “the day,” Yehovah ha’adir, “the great, mighty, powerful,” <note type="footnote" n="463">For this spelling see Book of Jubilees 4:22.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.15">See, I will come as a thief.464 So, holy is he465 who does not sleep and keeps himself; so that he does not go naked without clothes so that he does not reveal his nakedness.  The Scriptures: “See, I am coming as a thief. Blessed is he who is staying awake and guarding his garments, lest he walk naked and they see his shame.”  Aramaic: (And lo, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments; lest he walk naked, and they see his shame.) ra’ah, (to a man) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) avo, “I will come, go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, k’ganav, “as/ like (the) thief,” (prep, v’kadosh, “and/ but/ so/ or holy,” eylu, “these, those, the following,” which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) Pa’al/Qal, imp, yeshenim, “we/ you (mp)/ they v’shamor, “and/ et, (DO marker) atz’mo, “himself, yelech, “he/ it will go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) arom, “naked,” which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) those who sleep,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act keep(s), guard(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf substance,” (n ms, added mater lectionis bli, “without, no, not,” (neg part) k’dei, “be able, yigaleh, “he/it will be revealed,” (v. Nif’al, yiqtol, fut, et, (DO marker) arutaiv, “his/its nakedness,” (n fs, according to, as, in which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, clothes” (n mp) order to,” (conj)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.16">And he gathered them in one place called in the Hebrew tongue Har Mageddan.467  The Scriptures: And they gathered them together to the place called in Hebrew, Har Meḡiddo.  Aramaic: And they collected them together in a place called, in Hebrew, Armageddon. v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms kibetz, “he/it gathered,” (v. Pa;al/Qal, qatal, echad, “one,” (card ha’nikra, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it call(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, bie’lashon, “by/ in/ with (the) tongue,” those,” (prep pron ivri, “Hebrew,” (n Megeddan (name)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.17">Then the seventh poured out his bowl on the atmosphere, and a voice came from the throne and said, “This one has passed.”  The Scriptures: And the seventh messenger poured out his bowl into the air, and a loud voice came out of the Dwelling Place of the heaven, from the throne, saying, “It is done!” v’shevi’i, “and/ but/ so/ or the seventh,” (ord yatzak, “he/it poured out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, et, (DO marker) ke’aru, “his/its bowl,” (n fs, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, qatal, weather,” (prep, n echad, “one,” (card m’ha’ kise, “from/ v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, zot, “this, this one,”’ (pron fs) avar, “he/it passed, ceased to exist,” qatal, past, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="466">Second Temple spelling first found in the Book of Jubilees 3:34, from c. 460 BCE to 140 CE. 467 The scribe added nikkudot (vowel markings) to clarify the pronunciation, but was probably originally two words, "Har (mountain) Megeddan."</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.18">And there were voices, thunders, lightnings, and earthquakes like never before.469  The Scriptures: And there came to be noises and thunders and lightnings. And there came to be a great earthquake, such a mighty and great earthquake as had not came to be since men were on the earth.  Aramaic: And there were lightnings, and thunders, and voices; and there was a great earthquake, the like of which there was never, since men were on the earth, such an earthquake, and so great. v’hayah, “and/ but/ kolot, “sounds, voices,” (n mp) v’ re’amim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) thunders,” (n mp) u’brakim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) v’radot, “and/ but/ tremblings,” (n fp) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, flashes,” (n mp) Idiom: "not like ever before." she'lo, “that/ which/ who/ whom no/not,” (neg part) hayah, “he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) m’olam, “from/ of everlasting, world,” (prep, n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.19">Thus, the great city became three parts, and the cities of the nations fell. So, the great city Babel was remembered before Yehovah who gave her the cup with wine, which is the wrath of His anger.  The Scriptures: And the great city became divided into three parts, and the cities of the nations fell. And great Baḇel was remembered before Elohim, to give her the cup of the wine of the fierceness of His wrath.  Aramaic: And the great city became three parts. And the city of the nations fell; and Babylon the great was remembered before God, to give her the cup of the wine of the heat of his wrath. um’ha’ir, “and/ ha’gadolah, “the great,” (adj fs) shloshah, “three,” v’ha’arim,”and/ but/ so/ or the cities,” (n fp) but/ so/ or from/ of the city,” (prep, n “nations, peoples,” become(s),” (v. Nif’al, act part, territories,” (adj, noflim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those v’nizkar, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you ha’Ir, “the city,” (n ha’gadolah, “the great, large,” (adj Bavel, “Babel,” before the face of, before me, in front Pa’al/Qal, act part, remember(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part ha’ kos, “the glass, tumbler, cup,” (n im, “with,” (prep) ha’yayin, “the wine,” (n ms) shel, “to/ for of, that, which is,” charon, “with/ in by (the) wrath,” her/it,” (prep, 3fs apo, “his/its nose, anger,” (n ms, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.20">Then all the mountains and hills fled and were seen no more.  The Scriptures: And every island fled away, and the mountains were not found  Aramaic: And every island fled away; and the mountains were not found. v’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (prep, n v’ gva’ot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) nasu, “they fled,” v’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ nir’u, “they were visible, seen,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, “mountains,” (n (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3cp) or no, not,” (neg</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.16.21">And great hail fell upon man from the heavens, and they cursed Yehovah because of the plague of the hail.  The Scriptures: And great hail from the heaven fell upon men, every hailstone about the weight of a talent. And men blasphemed Elohim for the plague of the hail, because that plague was exceedingly great. v’ barad, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) gadol, “great, big, large,” (adj, ms) nadal, “he/it fell,” m’ shamayim, “from/ of (the) skies, heavens,” ve' he’ma, “and/ but/ so/ or they, qatal, past, 3ms) these, those,” (3mp mecharfim,” we/ you (mp)/ they curse, insult,” (v. Pi’el, act part, mp) “to/ for/ belonging bishvil, “for, for the sake of,” (prep) <note type="footnote" n="470">This is a unique spelling, see Revelation 2:17 for more details.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.17">
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.1">Then one of the seven messengers had one of the seven bowls came and spoke to me.  And he said, “Come, and I will show you the judgment of the great harlot who sits upon many waters.”   The Scriptures: And one of the seven messengers who had the seven bowls came and spoke with me, saying to me, “Come, I shall show you the judgment of the great whore sitting on many waters,  Aramaic: Then came one of the seven angels who have the seven cups, and talked with me, saying: Come, I will show thee the judgment of the great harlot, who sitteth upon many waters; uva, “and/ but/ so/ she’haya, “that/ la’hem, “to/ for/ which/ who/ whom seven,” (card num) seven,” (prep, card messengers,” (n he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, 3ms) v’hira,” and/ but/ bo! “(to a man) v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’diber, “and he/it k'arot, “the bowls, plates, saucers,” (n belonging to me” (prep,1cs pronom) Pa’al/Qal, imp, qatal, past, 3ms) ma’yim, “waters,” ha’yoshevet, “I/ you (fs)/ she/it dwells, sits,” (v. Pa’al/Qal act part, hazonah, “whore,” shel, “of, belonging ha’mishpat, “the “big, large, great,” harbey, “many, much, great”, (adj,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.2">“The kings471 of the earth committed fornication with her and they became intoxicated by her wine.”  The Scriptures: with whom the sovereigns of the earth committed whoring, and the inhabitants of the earth were made drunk with the wine of her whoring.”  Aramaic: with whom the kings of the earth have practised whoredom, and the inhabitants of the earth have been inebriated with the wine of her whoredom. ha’m’shacheret “I/ you (fs)/ she/it intoxicated,” (v. Pi’el, act part, fs) v’eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, aretz, “earth,” (n malchei, “‘and/ but/ so/ or (the) rulers of, kings o’sim, “we, you (mp)/ they, those doing, making,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act v’ama,”and/ but/ so/ or with her/it,” (prep, 3fs pronom) “whoredom,” (n the following,” of,” (n mp constr) m’yenaih, “from/ of her/its wine,” (prep, n ms,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.3">Then he brought me into the wilderness.  And I saw the woman sitting on the beast, whose appearance was like the appearance of lilies and was full of slanderous names, having seven heads and ten horns.  The Scriptures: And he carried me away in the Spirit into the wilderness. And I saw a woman sitting on a scarlet beast covered with names of blasphemy, having seven heads and ten horns.  Aramaic: And he led me in spirit into the wilderness: and I saw a woman sitting on a red beast of prey, which was full of names of blasphemy, and had seven heads and ten horns. ha’isha, “the woman,” (n fs) v' ra'iti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v.  Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ba’midbar, “in/ with/ by (the) v’hevi, “and/ but/ “that/ which/ who/ whom she/it sat, marker, 1cs pron) wilderness,” (prep, Hif’il, qatal, past, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, haya, “he/it was,” u’mula, “he/it was k’mareh, “as/ like (the) appearance,” haya, “he/it was,” she’marehu, “that/ qatal, past, 3ms) (v Pi’el pssv past, qatal, past, 3ms) whom/ from/ for (prep, n ms, 3ms) added mater lectionis rashim, “heads,” (n sheva, “seven,” haya “he/it was,” v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging shel, “to, for, of, (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) belonging to,” (prep) to him/it,” (prep) (mp)/ they, those names,” (prep, n karnayim, “horns,” v’esreh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ten,” <note type="footnote" n="471">See Revelation 16:12. This word can mean “rulers, kings, or sovereigns.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.4">And the woman473 was clothed in red garments with the appearance of lilies. And on her was a great exceeding gold with precious stones and pearls. A golden cup full of impurities was in her hand. mar’eh, “like/ as (the) appearance,” adom, “red,” (adj b’malbushi, “in/ l’vush, “clothed,” haya, “he/it was” v’ha’isha, “and/ but/ so/ or the woman,” (n fs) “lilies, roses,” (n clothing of,” (prep, mar’galilot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) gems, jewels, pearls,” (n fp) v’avanim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) stones,” (n fp) zahav, “gold,” (n harbey, “great, exceedingly,” (v. haya, “he/it was,” v’aleha, “and/ but/ so/ or upon, over her/it,” (prep, 3fs pleasant,” (adj fp) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) t'meot, maleh, “he/it was full,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, be’ya’da, ‘in/ with/ zahav,” gold,” (n shel, “of, belonging v’chos, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) glass, cup,” (prep, n fs) “impurities,” (adj by her/its hand,” qatal, past, 3ms) <note type="footnote" n="472">While this is translated as "lilies" it could refer to a flower that is like the lily. It is used six times in Song of Songs, as well as Psalm 45:1, 69:1 and 80:1.  473 Literally, "And the woman, he was clothed in…" This seems to hint of an end of day “gender confusion” problem.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.5">And written on her forehead was the name of the mystery of the great city, Babel, the mother of harlots and the defiled of the earth.  The Scriptures: and upon her forehead a name written, a secret: BAḆEL THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF THE WHORES AND OF THE ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.  Aramaic: And upon her forehead was the name written: Mystery: Babylon the great; the Mother of Harlots, and of the contaminations of the Earth. m’ha’ir, “from/ of the city,” (prep, n shel, “of, belonging ka’tuv,”he/it was haya,”he/it was,” uv’mitzchah, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ mystery, secret,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, pssv forehead,” (n ms, ha’eretz, “the earth,” (n fs) m’ha’znot, “from/ of the whoring,” ha’gadola, “the big, large, great,” “and/ but/ so/ or (the) unclean, defiled, impure” (n added mater lectionis added mater lectionis <note type="footnote" n="474">This word and spelling are found in The Midrash of Philo 2:18 of the Second Temple period.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.6">And I saw that the woman drank the blood of the holy ones and the blood of the congregations of Yeshua. I had great astonishment when I saw her.  The Scriptures: And I saw the woman, drunk with the blood of the set-apart ones, and with the blood of the witnesses of עשוהי. And having seen her, I marvelled – greatly marvelled!  Aramaic: And I saw that the woman was intoxicated with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the witnesses of Jesus. And when I saw her, I wondered with great amazement. u’m’dam, “and/ ha’kdoshim, “the holy ones, saints, set-apart ones,” (n m’dam, “from/ of (the) blood” (prep, she’ha’isha, “that/ which/ who/ whom ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or from/ of congregations,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, the woman” (rel k’she’ra’a, “when he/it saw,” (prep, haya,”he/it was,” (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, gadoal, “big, large, v’tamiha, “and/ but/ so/ or(the), sign, wonder, amazement,” Yeshua shel, “of, belonging (prep, 1cs pronom) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, otah, “her/it” (DO <note type="footnote" n="475">Second Temple word. See Revelation 2:4 for first occurrence.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.7">And the messenger said to me, “Why are you astonished? I want to tell you the mystery of the woman, and of the beast which she sat upon — he has seven heads and ten horns.”  The Scriptures: And the messenger said to me, “Why did you marvel? Let me explain to you the secret of the woman and of the beast she rides, which has the seven heads and the ten horns.  Aramaic: And the Angel said to me, Why dost thou wonder? I will tell thee the mystery of the woman, and of the beast of prey that beareth her, which hath the seven heads and the ten horns. yesh, there is, there Idiom: “because of what?” amar, “he/it said,” belonging to you,” “and/ but/ so/ or the angel,” (n ms) qatal, past, 3ms) mah, “what? why?” mipnei, “from/ of away, from before,” m’ha’isha, “from/ of (the) woman,” l’mor, “to say,” (v. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) mystery, secret,” belonging to you,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, wonder,” (n fs) she’yesh, “that/ Idiom: “(and) because of what?” aleha, “upon/ on her/it,” (prep, 3fs she’yahiva, “that/ which/ who/ whom she/it sat, dwelled” u’m’ha’chaya, “and/ but/ so/ or which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms u’mipnay, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of me exists,” (rel part, beast,” (prep, n fs) (prep, 1cs pronom) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ma, “what?” (interog part) kranayim, “horns,” v’asarah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ten,” (card num) rashim, “heads,” (n sheva, “seven,” <note type="footnote" n="476">See Revelation 2:4 for more details on this idiom. 477 See Revelation 2:4 for more details on this Second Temple word.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.8">The beast that you saw was and was not, and it will come once more from the deep and will go to Sheol. The people of the earth will be amazed at it when they see the beast that was and is not even though it is.  The Scriptures: “The beast that you saw was, and is not, and is about to come up out of the pit of the deep and goes to destruction. And those dwelling on the earth, whose names are not written in the Book of Life from the foundation of the world, shall marvel when they see the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.  Aramaic: The beast of prey which thou sawest, was, and is not; and he will ascend from the abyss and go into perdition: and the dwellers on the earth, whose names are not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, will wonder when they see the beast of prey, which was, and is not, and approacheth. v’yavo,”and/ but/ so/ or he/it will v’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” she’ raita, “that/ (ms)/ he/it is,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, or no, not,” (neg (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) which/ who/ whom you (ms) saw,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, past, 2ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, aleha, “on, upon, vayishtomem, “and/ but/ so/ or le’sheol, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) va’yelech,”and/ but/ so/ or he/it m’tehom, “from/ regarding her/it,” (prep, 3fs pronom) deep,” (prep, n fs) od, “again, more,” (adv) astonished,” (v. Hit’pael, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, pa’am, “time (occasion), once, time,” (n v’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ she’haya, “that/ she’yiru, “that/ ba’im, “they, those ha’adamah, “the anshei, ‘the men or no, not,” (neg which/ who/ whom which/ who/ whom part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, she’yesh, “that/ there exists,” (part) Idiom: though, though there are, even though which/ who/ whom af, “anger, nose,” (n ms) al, “upon,” (prep) pi, “mouth, (n ms) <note type="footnote" n="478">See Revelation 2:4 for more details on this idiom.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.9">And here is the matter that requires intellect, wisdom and understanding: the seven heads are seven mountains that the woman480 dwells upon; they are the seven kings.481  The Scriptures: “Here is the mind having wisdom: The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman sits.  Aramaic: Here is intelligence, for him who hath wisdom. Those seven heads are the seven mountains, on which the woman sitteth. utuna, “and/ but/ v’chok’ma, “and/ seychel, “intellect, she’tzorech, “that/ which/ who/ whom u’v’kan “and/ but/ so/ or with/ in/ by but/ so/ or(the) wisdom,” (n fs) matter, word,” (n there exists,” (part) understanding,” (n needs, requires, should,” (adj ms) yoshev, ‘I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), she’ha’isha, “that/ harim, “mountains, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, rashim, “heads,” (n which/ who the woman,” (n fs) seven,” (card num) Pa’al/Qal, act part, mel’achim, shiv’a, “seven,” he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, aleha, “upon, on her/it,” (prep, 3fs “kings,” (n mp) “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, the following,” (pron, <note type="footnote" n="479">This word can be translated as, “again.” See Against Apion 2:2. 480 The verb “dwelling” does not match the gender of the noun “woman.” The literal translation reads as follows, “He, the woman, dwells upon…” This again seems to hint to a “gender confusion” problem relating to the woman and the beast in the end of day events. 481 "Kings” and “messengers" are spelled the same in Hebrew without the nikkudot (vowel markings), but "kings" fits the context of the verse. .</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.10">But five of these fell, and one is, the second is not yet; but when482 he comes, it must be for a short time.  The Scriptures: “And there are seven sovereigns: five have fallen, and one is, and the other has not yet come. And when he comes, he has to remain a little while.  Aramaic: And there are seven kings: of whom five have fallen, one exists, and the other hath not yet come; and when he cometh he must continue for a short time. adayin, “still, yet,” v’ha’sheni, “and/ echad, “and/ but/ so /or (the) one” chamisha, “five,” nafal, “he/it fell” u’mehem, “and/ there exists,” (part) but/ so/ or from/ of them,” (prep, 3mp second” (adj ms) qatal, past, 3ms) lihiyot, “to be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf hu,”he/it,” (pron she' yavo, “that/ u’vim, “and/ but/ so/ or by if, when, whether,” (prep, lo, “no; not” (neg should, must,” (adj which/ who/ whom there exists,” (part) he/it will come,” Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, mu’at, “few in numbers,” (adj ms) season, a set time, appointed time,” (n <note type="footnote" n="482">This can be “if he returns” or “when he returns.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.11">And the beast that is not is the eighth for he was one of the seven but went to Sheol.485  The Scriptures: “And the beast that was, and is not, is himself also the eighth, and is of the seven, and goes to destruction.  Aramaic: And the beast of prey, which was and is not, is the eighth, and is from the seven, and is for perdition. v’hu, “and/ but/ so/ ha’shmini, “the ze, ‘this (pron, ms) yesh, “there is, she’haya, “that/ ha’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or the beast,” eighth,” (ord num) there exists,” (part) “that/who/which/th which/ who/ whom at/of not, which not,” (Ar. rel part, gender mismatch part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) gender mismatch le’sheol, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) v’halach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it there exists,” (part) seven,” (prep, card Pa’al/Qal, qatal, gender mismatch</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.12">And the ten horns that you saw are ten kings who have not yet received their kingdoms, but they will rule as kings with the beast for a short time.  The Scriptures: “And the ten horns which you saw are ten sovereigns who have not yet received a reign, but receive authority as sovereigns with the beast for one hour.  Aramaic: And the ten horns which thou sawest, are ten kings. These persons have not yet received royalty; but they receive authority, as if kings, with the beasts of prey, for one hour. she’adayin, “that/ mel’achim, “kings, rulers, sovereigns,” hem, “they, them,” she’ra’ita, “that/ karnayim, “horns,” v’ha’asarah, “and/ but/ so/ or the ten,” which/ who/ whom you saw” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, whom, still, yet,” lo, “no/not,” (neg ha’malchut, “the kingdom, reign, he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, timshelu, “you will rule,” (v. Pa’al/Qal surely, but,” (adv) yiqtol, fut, 2mp) empire, estate,” sovereigns,” (prep, mu'at, “short,” ‘im, “with,” (prep) season, a set time, appointed time,” (n <note type="footnote" n="486">The dalet prefix is an Aramaic prefix relative particle meaning, “of/ who/ which/ that.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.13">And they have one purpose,487 and they will give their power and strength to the beast.  The Scriptures: “They have one mind, and they shall give their power and authority to the beast.  Aramaic: They have one mind; and they will give their power and authority unto the beast of prey. et, (DO marker) yi’te’nu, “they will hem, “they, them, machshava, “a thought, device, plan, purpose,” (n v’lahem, “and/ but/ there exists,” (part) so/ or to them,” (prep, pronom, (pronoun 3mp) yiqtol, fut, 3mp) l’ha’haya, “to/ for/ belonging to the v’gvuratam, “and/ ko’cham, “their power, strength, ability, wealth” (n ms, 3mp pronom) but/ so/ or their</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.14">And they will make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb will prevail over them. For He is Lord of lords, and King of kings;488 and with Him are the chosen and the faithful.  The Scriptures: “They shall fight with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them, for He is Master of masters and Sovereign of sovereigns. And those with Him are called, and chosen, and trustworthy.”  Aramaic: They will make war upon the Lamb; and the Lamb will vanquish them; because he is Lord of lords, and King of kings, and these with him [are] called and chosen and faithful. v’ha’se, “and/ but/ so/ or the lamb,” (n ha’se, “the lamb,” milchama,”war” Ya’asu, “they will v’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (3mp “he/it will prevail, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) ha’melachim, “the kings, sovereigns,” u’meleḵ, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) king,” adon, “master,” (DO marker, 3mp masters, lords,” v'ha ma'aminim, ha’bichirim, “the chosen, elect,” v’imo, “and/ but/ so/ or with him/it,” “and/ but/ so/ or the faithful,” (n mp) added mater lectionis</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.15">And he said to me, “The waters where the harlot lives that I saw are peoples, corporations, and nations.”  The Scriptures: And he said to me, “The waters which you saw, where the whore sits, are peoples, and crowds, and nations, and tongues.  Aramaic: And he said to me: The waters which thou sawest, where the harlot sitteth, are peoples, and multitudes, and nations, and tongues. she’yashav, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it sat, dwelled,” she’rai’ta, “that/ ha’mayim, “the water(s)” (n mp) amar, “he/it said,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms “I/ you (fs)/ she/it whores, harlot,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, which/ who/ whom you saw” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (prep, 1cs pronom) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, “v’umim, “and/ v’cha’vo’ro’tot, “and/ but/ so/ or amim, “peoples,” hem, “they,them, but/ so /or (the) nations,” (n mp) associations, firms,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.16">And the ten horns that you saw on the beast will hate the harlot, and will make a wasteland of her, and eat her flesh and burn her with fire.492  The Scriptures: “And the ten horns which you saw on the beast, these shall hate the whore, and lay her waste and naked, and eat her flesh and burn her with fire.  Aramaic: And the ten horns which thou sawest, and the beast of prey, will hate the harlot; and they will make her desolate and naked, and will eat her flesh, and burn her with fire. yihyu, “they will hem, “they,them, she’raita, “that/ karnayim, “horns,” v’ha’asarah, “and/ but/ so/ or the ten,” which/ who/ whom you saw” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp) et, (DO marker) va’yoch’lu, “and/ but/ so/ or they mi’m’nah, “from/ va’ya’asu, “and/ but/ so/ or they l’ha’zo’nah, “to/ for/ belonging to son’im, “we/ you (mp) they, those who hate,” (v. (prep, 3fs pronom) will do, make,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, the prostitute, whore, harlot,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Pa’al/Qal, act part, o’tah, “her/it,” (DO marker, 3fs tisrofu “you (mp) esh, “fire,” (n ms) v‘im, “and/ but/ b’sbrah, “her/its flesh, meat,” (n ms, 3fs pronom) so/ or with,” (prep) yiqtol, fut, 2mp) <note type="footnote" n="491">The vav and the tav suffix is a spelling error. 492 Literally, “you will burn her,” but that does not fit in the context.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.17">For Yehovah allowed their hearts to do His will, to give her riches to the beast until she is devastated by the words of Yehovah.  The Scriptures: “For Elohim did give it into their hearts to do His mind, to be of one mind, and to give their reign to the beast, until the words of Elohim shall be accomplished.  Aramaic: For God hath put into their hearts, to do his pleasure, and to execute one purpose, and to give their kingdom to the beast of prey, until these words of God shall be fulfilled. r’tso’no, “his/its la’a’sot, “to do,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf be’l’vavi’hem, in/ natan, “he/it gave, ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) with/ by their heart,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mp, 3mp pronom) Yehovah diburot, “words of,” (n mp constr) added mater lectionis she’tikale, “that/ ad, “until, up to” l’ha’haya, “to/ for/ belonging to the beast,” (prep, n fs) eserot’ha, “her/its tens, riches,” (n fp, which/ who/ whom added mater lectionis ruined, decayed,” (v. Nif’al, yiqtol, <note type="footnote" n="493">This is a unique spelling, see Revelation 2:17 for more details.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.17.18">And the woman that you saw is the great city, the kings over all the kings of the earth.  The Scriptures: “And the woman whom you saw is that great city having sovereignty over the sovereigns of the earth.”  Aramaic: And the woman whom thou sawest, is the great city, which hath dominion over the kings of the earth. ha’melekh, “the ha’gadol, “big, large, great” (adj ha’ir, “the city,” (n she’raita, “that/ v’ha’isha, “and/ but/ so/ or the woman,” (n fs) which/ who/ whom you saw” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’aretz, “the land, machey, “kings of,” (n mp constr) kol, “all, every, everything,’’</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.18">
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.1">Afterwards, I saw another messenger descending from the heavens, and he had power and great strength, and his light illuminated the earth.  The Scriptures: And after this I saw another messenger coming down from the heaven, having great authority, and the earth was lightened from his esteem.  Aramaic: After these things, I saw another angel come down from heaven; and he had great authority and the earth was illumined by his glory. Idiom: "and after this way" malakh “angel, yarad, “he/it came down, descended,” mi’shamayim, “of/ (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, another, different,” vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after” (prep) heavens,” (n mp) qatal, past, 3ms) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this way,” v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was,” koach , “strength, power, authority” ve’gvura, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) valor, power, gdolah, “big, large, v’ha’adama, “and/ shone,” (v. Hif’il qatal, past 3ms) him/it,” (prep, 3ms qatal, past, 3ms) courage, bravery, strength,” (n fs) m’oro, “from/ of (prep, n ms, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.2">Then he cried with all his power, and said, “Fallen! Fallen! Is the great city Babel!495  For she was the dwelling place of the adversaries to hide all the unclean birds and creeping things.”  The Scriptures: And he cried with a mighty voice, saying, “Baḇel the great is fallen, is fallen, and has become a dwelling place of demons, a haunt for every unclean spirit, and a haunt for every unclean and hated bird, v’kol, “in/ with/ by (the) all,” (prep, n v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, nof’lah, “I/ you nof’lah, “I/ you (fs)/ she/it fell,’’ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act ha'ir, “the city,” (n “and/ but/ so/ or strength, power,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) (fs)/ she/it fell,’’ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, he/it cried out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’gedola, “the bavel, “Babel,” ve’ha’yi’tah, “and/ lidorat, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) dwellings,” (prep, ha’sataim, “satans, v’l’hastir, “and/ but/ so/ or to hide, conceal,” (prep, v. Hif’il, inf constr) kol, “all,” (n ms) big, large,” (adj fs) but/ so/ or she/it adversaries,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, m’ofot, “‘from/ of the large birds,” v’sheratzim, “and/ “unclean, impure,” but/ so/ or (the) creeping things, reptile,”(n mp) <note type="footnote" n="494">See Revelation 1:19 for first occurrence. 495 See Isaiah 21:9.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.3">“Because all of them drank of her wine, and the rulers of the earth committed fornication with her. And all the merchants became rich, for their lust was great.”  The Scriptures: because all the nations have drunk of the wine of the wrath of her whoring, and the sovereigns of the earth have committed whoring with her, and the merchants of the earth have become rich through the power of her riotous living.”  Aramaic: For all the nations have drunken of the wine of her wrath; and the kings of the earth have practised whoredom with her; and the merchants of the earth have been enriched by the abundance of her luxuries. ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) shatu, “they drank,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, m’yeinah, “from/ ve’malchei, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) kings of,” (n mp asu, “they made, did,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3mp) them,” (n mp, 3mp of her/its wine (prep, n ms, 3fs Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) ha’socharim, “the merchants,” (n mp) m’ta’avot’ihm, “from/ of their h’gadol, “the big, large, great’ (adj her/it,” (prep, 3fs lust,” (prep, n ms, fornication,” (n fs) nit’asher, “he/it was rich,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.4">Then I heard another voice from the heavens say, “Come out of her, my people,497 so that you will not be punished with her because of her perversions.”  The Scriptures: And I heard another voice from the heaven saying, “Come out of her, my people, lest you share in her sins, and lest you receive of her plagues.  Aramaic: And I heard another voice from heaven, saying: Come ye out of her, my people; that ye may not participate in her sins, and may not partake of her plagues. v' shema'ati, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kol, “voice,” (n ms) mi’shamayim, “of/ v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mi’m’nah, “from/ of her/it, her/it,” heavens,” (n mp) (prep, 3fs pronom) Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic ami, “my people” k’dei, “according to, as, in order to,” i’mah, “with her’ (prep, 3fs pronom) bishvil, “for the sake of, for this reason,” (prep) avonoteha, “her/its which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, wrongs,” (n mp, 3fs nitashtu,“they were punished,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.5">“For her perversions are a plague to the heavens and Yehovah will remember her.”498  The Scriptures: “Because her sins have piled up to reach the heaven, and Elohim has remembered her unrighteousnesses.  Aramaic: For her sins have reached up to heaven; and God hath remembered her iniquities. ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) avonoteha, “her/its niaga, “stroke, plague, disease, el, “to, towards,” ha’may’im, “the heavens,” (n mp) v’Yehovah, “and/ tizkor, “you (ms) will remember,” wrongs, sins,” (n mp, 3fs pronom) mark, plague spot,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2fs) ota(h), “her/it, (DO <note type="footnote" n="497">Jeremiah 51:45.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.6">“So, just as she did, they did to her. Then He paid her double, twice as much, according to her works.”  The Scriptures: “Render to her as she indeed did render, and repay her double according to her works. In the cup which she has mixed, mix for her double.  Aramaic: Recompense ye to her, as she also hath recompensed; and render to her double, according to her deeds; in the cup which she hath mixed, mix ye to her two fold. ve’ka'asher, "and/ but/ so/ or like/ as who, which, that, what’just as,’ or ‘when,’” (prep, rel asta, “she/It did,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, shilem, “and/ but/ so / or he/it paid,” kefel, “multiply, doubling,”’ (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, her/it,” (prep, 3fs her/it,” (prep, 3fs kiflayim, “twice as kfi, “according to,” ma’aseha “her/its deeds,” (n mp, 3fs much, double,” <note type="footnote" n="498">Literally, “You will remember her.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.7">“Then when she boasted and went after her lusts, how they made her suffer.  For she devised in her heart, ‘I am queen, and I will not be a widow,499 nor see sorrow.’”  The Scriptures: “As much as she esteemed herself and lived riotously, so much torture and grief give to her, because in her heart she says, ‘I sit as sovereigness, and I am not a widow, and I do not see mourning at all.’  Aramaic: As much as she pleased herself with lasciviousness, so much of anguish and sorrow give ye to her. Because she saith in her heart, I sit a queen, and am no widow, and I shall see no sorrow; ve’ka'asher, "and/ but/ so/ or like/ as when,” (prep, rel ha’tige, “he/it was proud of, boasted,” (v. Hit’pael, qatal, ve’halcha, “and/ but/ so /or she/it ta’avoteha, “her, lusts, passions, (n fp, 3fs pronom) ki’tzad, how, in what manner? In ze, “this, this one,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, machashava, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it b’livah, “in her/its heart,” (prep, n ms, suffering,” (n ms, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, her/it,” (prep, 3fs devises, plans,” (v. Pi’el, act pat, ms) afflicted, humbled, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) malcha, “queen,” ve' lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not,” ehye, “I will be,” almana, “widow,” v' sum, “and/ but/ so/ or any,” (in a tza'ar, “sadness, regret, remorse, suffering,” (n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) lo, “no; not,” (neg er’e, “I will see,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) <note type="footnote" n="499">Isaiah 47:7-8.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.8">“For this reason, it will come, their sorrows on one day of death: grief and hunger.  And the people will burn by fire because the mighty Master Yehovah will judge her.”   The Scriptures: “Because of this her plagues shall come in one day: death and mourning and scarcity of food. And she shall be burned up with fire, because הוהי Elohim who judges her is mighty.  Aramaic: therefore, in one day, shall these her plagues come, death, and mourning, and famine; and she shall be burned with fire: for strong is the Lord God who judgeth her. ve’bishvil, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) sake of, for this reason,” (prep) ze, “this, this one,” yavo,” he/it will tza'areitem, “their b’yom, “in/ with/ echad,”one,” (card Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, sorrows,” (n mp, ve’he’tza’ar, “and/ ve’ha’ra’av, “and/ ve’am, “and/ but/ ve’saraf, “you (ms) but/ so/ or (the) sadness, regret, burning,” (n cs) uzam, “strength,” people,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, remorse of’ (n ms) she’yeshpot, “that/ which/ who/ whom he/it shall judge,” otah, “her/it,” (DO Lord, Master,” (n yiqtol, fut, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.9">“So they will be ruined over her; the kings of the earth who did fornication with her, when they see the smoke of the fire!”  The Scriptures: “And the sovereigns of the earth who committed whoring and lived riotously with her shall weep and mourn over her, when they see the smoke of her burning,  Aramaic: And the kings of the earth who committed whoredom and were lascivious with her, shall weep, and mourn, and bewail her, when they shall see the smoke of her burning, ve’shamemu, “and/ aliah, “upon, over her/it,” (prep pron malchei, “kings of,” (n mp constr) aretz, “earth, land,” but/ so/ or they were ruined,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, which/ who/ whom Pa’al/Qal, qatal, fornication,” (n fs) b’im, “in/ with/ by if, whether, when,” ha’ashan, “the smoke,” (n ms) mah’esh, “from/ of the fire,” (prep, n which/ who/ whom you (mp) will see,” yiqtol, fut, 2mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.10">“And they will stand far away from the terror and say, ‘Woe!’ and ‘Alas!’  The great city Babel!  Suddenly, your brokenness comes!”  The Scriptures: standing at a distance for fear of her torture, saying, ‘Woe! Woe, the great city Baḇel, the mighty city, because your judgment has come in one hour!  Aramaic: standing afar off, from fear of her torment, [and] saying, Alas, alas! that great city Babylon, that powerful city; for in one hour is thy judgment come! ve' he’ma, “and/ but/ so/ or they, ya’am’du, “they will stand,”’ (v Pa’al/Qal yiqtol, me’rachok, “from/ of afar off,” (prep, mipnei, “from/ of himah, “horror, terror, terrible, terror,” (n fs) va’yomeru, “and/ but/ so/ or they will say,” (v. oyi, “woe!” (interj these, those,” (3mp Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, v’ahah, “and/ but/ so/ or alas! aha!” ha’air, “the city,” ha’gedola, “the great,” (adj fs) bavel, “Babel,” pitom, “suddenly,” yavo,” he/it will shavart’ika, “your (ms) brokenness,” Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.11">“The merchants will weep and hiss because no one can buy merchandise any longer:”  The Scriptures: “And the merchants of the earth weep and mourn over her, because no one buys their merchandise any more –  Aramaic: And the merchants of the earth will mourn over her, because no one purchaseth their cargo; ve’ha’socharim, yevaku, “they will lament, wept” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, v’sharku, “and/ but/ so/ or they hissed, aleicha, “on, upon; bishvil, “for the sake of, for this reason,” (prep) yikne, “he/it will “and/ but/ so/ or the merchants,” (n mp) which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, regarding you,” Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (prep 2ms 'pronom) sum, “any,” (in a echad,”one,” (card me’hem, “from/ of them,” (prep, 3mp) “commodity, good, merchandise,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.12">“the merchandise of gold, silver, precious stones, gems, silk, all kinds of wood, and instruments of silver, iron, tin, and lead,”   The Scriptures: merchandise of gold and silver, and precious stone and pearls, and fine linen and purple, and silk and scarlet, and all citron wood, and every object of ivory, and every object of most precious wood and bronze and iron and marble, zahav, “gold,” (n ve’kesef, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) silver,” ve’avanim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) in u’mar’ga’lit, “and/ u’meshi, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) silk,” commodity, good, merchandise,” (n but/ so/ or (the) gems, jewels, pearls,” (n fp) appropriate,” (adj v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) minei, “types of -,” (n mp, construct) etzim, “woods,” (n u’minei, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) types shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” vessels, utensils, dishes, vessels,’’ error. Should be: u’barzel, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) iron,” ve’dil, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) tin,” (n veoferet, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) lead,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.13">“wine, oil, white bread, grain, oxen, ewes, horses, calves and the souls of man.”  The Scriptures: and cinnamon and incense, and fragrant oil and frankincense, and wine and oil, and fine flour and wheat, and cattle and sheep, and horses and carriages, and bodies and lives of men.  Aramaic: and cinnamon, and amomum, and aromatics, and unguents, and frankincense, and wine, and oil, and fine flour, and wheat, and beasts of burden, and sheep, and horses, and chariots, and the bodies and souls of men. va’yayin. “and/ but/ so/ or (the) wine,” v’shemen, “and/ va’lechem, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) lavan, “white,” (adj v’chitim, “and/ but/ u’bakarim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) kvsim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ewes,” but/ so/ or (the) oil, grain(s),” (n fp) su’sim, “and/ but/ v’agalim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) calves,” (n mp) v’nishmot, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) souls of…’ (n fp horses,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.14">“And the fruit that was satisfaction for your spirit will leave you and all the calculations will not be found again.”  The Scriptures: “And the fruit that your being longed for has gone from you. And all your riches and splendour are lost to you, and you shall find them no more, not at all.  Aramaic: And the fruits which thy soul desired, have departed from thee; and all things delicious and splendid have perished from thee; and the traders in them shall obtain them no more. v’ha’perot, “and/ she’haya, “that, lo'nachat, “to (the) mimcha, “from/ of you,” (prep, 2ms breath, spirit,” (n belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) whom, he/it was,” satisfaction,” (prep, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, qatal, past, 3ms) v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) ha’chasuvim, “the ve' lo, “and/ but/ timtza, “you (ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, reasonings,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.15">“And the merchants who sold her these things will stand far off and lament over her.”  The Scriptures: “The merchants of these, those who became rich by her, shall stand at a distance for fear of her torture, weeping and mourning,  Aramaic: And they who were enriched from her, will stand afar off, for fear of her torment; and will weep and mourn, ve’ha’socharim, eilu, “these, some ha’dvarim, “the words, matters, things,” (n mp) ya’am’du, “they will stand,” (v. Pa’al/Qal yiqtol, me’rachok, “from/ of afar off,” (adj, “and/ but/ so/ or the merchants,” (n mp) “that/ which/ who/ whom they sold,” (v. Pa’al/Qal. qatal, her/it,” (prep, 3fs ve’yvaku, “and/ but/ so/ or they will lament,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, her/it,” (prep pron</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.16">“Then they will say, ‘Woe!’ and ‘Alas!’ The great city, Babel was clothed in splendor of silk, gold, and precious stones.”  The Scriptures: and saying, ‘Woe! Woe, the great city that was dressed in fine linen and purple and scarlet, and adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls!  Aramaic: saying: Alas, alas! that great city, which was clothed in fine linen, and purple, and scarlet, and gilded with gold, and precious stones, and pearls; because, in one hour, such riches are laid waste. v’yomru, “and/ but/ oyi, “woe!” (interj v’ahah, “and/ but/ so/ or alas! aha!” ‘ir, “city’ (n fs) ha’gedola, “the big, bavel, “Babel,” she’haya, “that/ so/ or they will which/ who/ whom say,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp) u' b’zahav, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) gold,” (n ms) u’b' avnaim, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ u’margaliot, “and/ you(ms)/ he/it was pleasant, (adj mp) but/ so/ or (the) gems, jewels, pearls (n fp) silk,” (prep, n ms) by (the) stones,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.17">“Because within the hour, all your merchandise will be destroyed: your sailors,503 and seaman, your ship’s carpenter, and barterers of your merchandise.  So, all the men of your war stand from far off.” ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) b' sha’a, “in/ with/ achar, “another,” necherav,” he/it ha’kol, “the all,” (n maravecha, “your merchandise,” (n ms, 2ms pronom) malachika, “your sailors, mariners,” was destroyed,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ve’chovalayika, “and/ but/ so/ or Maka'zikay, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it varvei, “and/ but/ maravecha, “your merchandise,” (n ms, 2ms pronom) v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms anasei, “men of,” strengtheners,” (n ms, 2ms pronom) (mp)/ they, those who barterer,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, seaman, pilots,” (n ms, 2ms pronom) Hif’il, act part, ms) ya'amdu, “they will m’ rachok, “from/ of afar off,” (adj, “your war,” (n ms, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.18">They will shout when they see the smoke and say, “Who is like the great ruined city?”  The Scriptures: and cried out when they saw the smoke of her burning, saying, ‘What is like this great city?  Aramaic: and cried, when they saw the smoke of her burning, saying: What [other] is like this great city! ve’tzo’akim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those ve’she'at “in/ with/ she’ra’u, “that/ ashan, “the smoke,” v'omrim, “and/ but/ nidmeh, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it was which/ who/ whom they saw,” (prep, v. (mp)/ they say,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, time,” (prep, n fs) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, pssv Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’gedola, “the belonging to (the) city,” (prep, n fs) big, large,” (adj fs) <note type="footnote" n="504">See Ezekiel 27:8, 27:28. 505 This word refers to a repairer of ships. In English, this would be the ship’s carpenter. 506 This word is a transliteration of the word “Arab,” meaning an Arabian, and is translated in Ezekiel 27:27 as “occupiers.” It most likely refers to those who are brokers or barters of goods rather than those who sell directly (merchandisers).</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.19">Then they will throw ashes on their heads,510 shouting, weeping, grieving, and saying, "Woe! Woe! The great city, Babel!”  Because from her, all the merchants who had ships were made rich by the merchandise of the sea and now in one hour, everything is destroyed!  The Scriptures: “And they threw dust on their heads and cried out, weeping and mourning, and saying, ‘Woe! Woe, the great city, in which all who had ships on the sea became rich by her wealth! For in one hour she was laid waste.’  Aramaic: And they cast dust on their heads, and cried, weeping, and mourning, and saying: Alas, alas that great city, in which all that have ships in the sea became rich, by her preciousness; for in one hour she hath become desolate. v'yizreku, “and/ afar, “dust, ashes,” roshhem, “their ve’tzo’akim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those u’bochim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those crying, weeping,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act u’mit’ablim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you but/ so/ or they will heads,” (n mp, 3mp Pa’al/Qal. yiqtol. Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’e’omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those oyi, “woe!” (part, oyi, “woe!” (part, ha’gedola, “the bavel, “Babel,” belonging to (the) city’ (prep, n fs) big, large,” (adj fs) Pa’al/Qal, act part, Hebrew marker Note: Mishnaic mimena, “from/ of her/it,” (prep, 3fs kol, “all,” (n ms ha’ sochar'im, “the she’ haya, ‘that/ lahem, “to /for/ s'fiynot, “ships, which/ who/ whom boats, vessels,” (n traders,” (n mp) he/it was,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, them,” (prep, 3mp nitasheru, “they were made rich,” (v. Nit’pael, qatal, pssv past, 3mp) b'yam, “in/ with/ m'schortia, “from/ u’ba’' sha'a, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ echad,”one,” (card necherav,”he/it ha’kol, “the all,” (n “now, currently, was destroyed,” (v. merchandise,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal, nowadays,” (adv) <note type="footnote" n="507">See Perek Shirah, Concluding Prayer 2 (c. 500 BCE - 1100 CE). 508 See Megillat Ta'anit, Elul 6, (c. 40 – 70 CE). 509 See