      <verse osisID="Rev.18.20">“Rejoice, O heavens, His set apart ones and His prophets!  For Yehovah avenges your vengeance for her!”  The Scriptures: “Rejoice over her, O heaven, and you set-apart emissaries and prophets, for Elohim has completely avenged you on her!”  Aramaic: Rejoice over her, O heaven, and ye Angels, and Legates, and Prophets; because God judgeth your cause with her. ti’samachu, “you will rejoice,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, ha’shama’yim, “the v'kidusheav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its saints, holy ones,” nevi'av, “and his/its Yehovah nikan, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it takes heavens,” (n mp) revenge, (v. Nif’al, et, (DO marker) nikmetikem, “I avenged you,” (v Nifal, qatal, past, bah, "in/ with/ by her/it,” (prep, 3fs added mater lectionis</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.21">Then a messenger took a great stone, like a millstone, and threw it into the sea and said, “Thus, Babel will sink and not rise up again,”  The Scriptures: And one mighty messenger picked up a stone like a great millstone and threw it into the sea, saying, “With such a rush the great city Baḇel shall be thrown down, and shall not be found any more at all.  Aramaic: And an angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying: So shall Babylon, the great city, be thrown down with violence, and shall no more be found: echad, “one,” (card lakach, “he/it took,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, echad,”one,” (card even, “stone,” (n gadol, “big, large, great,” (adj ms) k’mo, “like, as, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) angel,” (n ms) even, “stone,” (n v’zarak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it threw,” (v. Pa’al/Qal qatal, oto, “him/it,” (DO va’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kakhah, ‘thus, this “millstones,” (n ‘in/ with/ by the sea,” (prep, n ms) manner,” (adv) tishka, “she/it will sink,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, bavel, “Babel,” ve' lo, “and/ but/ tarum, “she/it will rise up, stand up” (v Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, <note type="footnote" n="515">This is a Second Temple spelling with the added yod.  See The Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs, The Testament of Joseph, Chapter 20.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.22">“and will not be heard again, not the sound of joy nor a sound of rejoicing, nor the voice of a bridegroom and the voice of a bride.  And no longer will there be any tool of workmanship from the masters of handicrafts, nor will the sound of a breath be heard!”  The Scriptures: “And the sound of harpists, and musicians, and flautists, and trumpeters shall not be heard in you any more at all. And no craftsman of any trade shall be found in you any more at all. And the sound of a millstone shall not be heard in you any more at all.  Aramaic: and the voice of harpers and musicians and pipers and trumpeters, shall no more be heard in thee; and no artificer of any trade, shall be found any more in thee. ve' lo, “and/ but/ neshema, “I/ you od, “more, yet, still, continually, duration,” (adv) bah, "in/ with/ by her/it,” (prep, 3fs qol, “voice, sound,” sasson, “happiness, ve’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) voice, heard,” (v, Nif'al, sim'chah, “rejoice, happiness, joy,” (n ve’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) voice, kala, “bride,” (n fs) ve' lo, “and/ but/ sum, “any,” (in a “bridegroom, groom,” (n ms) m’ ba'alei- “from (the) masters of,” (prep, n mp constr) malakhah, “works, ve’ha’kol, “and/ but/ so/ or the me’ha’ruachim, lo, “no/ not” (neg instrument, utensil, vessel, container, “workmanship, handicrafts,” (n fs) sound, voice,” (n handicraft,” (n fs) breaths,” (prep, n neshema, “I/ you od, “more, yet, still, continually, duration,” (adv) bacha, “in/ with/ by you, “(prep, 2fs, pronom) heard,” (v, Nif'al, <note type="footnote" n="516">In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.  517 See 1 Samuel 17:40b.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.23">“Nor will a light shine in any den because the merchants were the rulers on the ground; for by witchcraft,518 they incited all the people.”  The Scriptures: “And the light of a lamp shall not shine in you any more at all. And the voice of bridegroom and bride shall not be heard in you any more at all. For your merchants were the great ones of the earth, for by your drug sorcery all the nations were led astray.  Aramaic: And the light of a candle, shall not be seen in thee; and the voice of a bridegroom and bride, shall no more be heard in thee: for thy merchants were the great men of the earth, because all nations were seduced by thy sorceries. ve' lo, “and/ but/ yizrach, ‘he/it will od, “more, yet, still, continually, duration,” (adv) or, ‘light’ (n ms) ha’me’urat, “the den, lair” (n fs) ha’socharim, “and/ but/ so/ or the merchants,” (n mp) Pa’al/Qal,yiqtol, hayu, “they were,” sarim,” rulers,” (n ha’adama, “the ground,” (n fs) Idiom: al’yadei, “by the hand of.” yours,” (prep, 2ms qatal, past, 3mp) ha’amim, “the kol, “and/ but/ so/ kishufeicha, “your sorceries, magics, witchcrafts,” (n peoples, nations,” incited, inflamed,” (v. Hif’il, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.18.24">“And in her was found the blood of the holy ones, the prophets, and from all those killed on the ground.”  The Scriptures: “And in her was found the blood of prophets and set-apart ones, and of all who were slain on the earth.” u’bah, "and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by her/it,” (prep, 3fs nimtza, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is am, “blood,” (n ms) ha’kdoshim, “the holy ones, saints, set-apart ones,” (n ve’nevi’im, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) prophets,” (n mp) u’mechal, “and/ eilu, “these, the following,” (3mp found,” (v Nif’al, from/ of (the) all,” she’nehru, “that/ ha’adamah, “the ground, land,” (n which/ who/ whom they were killed” (rel part, v. Nif’al, qatal, past 3ms)</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.19">
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.1">Then afterwards, I heard a voice, from its great companies saying, “HalleluYah! Honor, might, and glory be to Yehovah, our Master.”  The Scriptures: And after this I heard a loud voice of a great crowd in the heaven, saying, “Halleluyah! Deliverance and esteem and respect and power to הוהי our Elohim!  Aramaic: And after these things, I heard a loud voice of a great multitude in heaven, saying: Hallelujah: Deliverance, and strength, and glory, and honor, unto our God: v’achar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this shamati, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it heard,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act kol, “voice,” (n ms) echad,” one,” (card g’dola, “great,” “from/ of her/its societies,” (prep, n ha’amorim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, halleluyah,”(to a man) praise Yah!” ve’cavod, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) honor,” (n ms) ve’gvura,”and/ but/ so/ or (the) might, valor,” (n v’tif'eret, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) la’Yehovah,” to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (name) those saying,’’ (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, Master, Lord,” (n ms, 1cp pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.2">“For righteous and true is His judgment who sentenced the great harlot, destroyer of the land with her fornication. For He avenged the blood of His servants from her.”  The Scriptures: “Because true and righteous are His judgments, because He has judged the great whore who corrupted the earth with her whoring. And He has avenged on her the blood of His servants shed by her.”  Aramaic: for, true and righteous are his judgments; for he hath judged that great harlot, who corrupted the earth with her whoredom; and hath avenged the blood of his servants at her hand. ki, “for, since, because,” (conj) emet, "and/ but/ so/ or (the) truth,” mishpato, “his/its court, sentence, judgment,” (n ms, et, (DO marker) ha’zona, “I/ you “righteous,” (adj whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it judge(s),” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, commits adultery, Pa’al/Qal, act pat, ha’gdula, ‘the great things, greatness,” im, “with,” (prep) zenutuah, “her/its ve’nakam, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it avenged,” (v. et, (DO marker) destroyer,” (n ms) whoredom,” (n fs, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, damei-, ‘bloods of…,” (n mp, avadav, “his/its servants, slaves,” from her/it,” (prep, 3fs pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.3">Then they say once more, “HalleluYah!” And the smoke rises from generation to generation.519  The Scriptures: And a second time they said, “Halleluyah! And her smoke rises up forever and ever!”  Aramaic: And again they said: Hallelujah: and her smoke ascendeth up for ever and ever. ve’ omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those shenit; “again, secondly,” (adv) halleluyah,”(to a man) praise Yah!” (v. Pi’el, imp, 2ms) v’ha’ashan, “and/ m'dor; “from/ of (the) generation,” (occasion), time round, once (adv) but/ so/ or the smoke,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, belonging to (the) generation (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="519">See Isaiah 34:10.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.4">So, the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fall and pray to Yehovah sitting upon the throne, saying, “Amen! HalleluYah!”  The Scriptures: And the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fell down and worshipped Elohim who sat on the throne, saying, “Amĕn! Halleluyah!”  Aramaic: And the twenty-four Elders fell down, and the four Animals, and worshipped God who sitteth on the throne, saying: Amen: Hallelujah! ve’ha’arba, “and/ ve’esrim, “and/ but/ zkenim,” elders,” ve’ha’arba, “and/ haiyot, “beasts, noflim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those u’mitpalelim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those living creatures” (n four,” (card num) four,” (card num) Pa’al/Qal, act part, worshiping,” (v. Hit’pael, act part, la’Yehovah,” to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, ha' yoshev, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) ve’ omrim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those halleluyah,” (to a man) praise Yah!” (v. Pi’el, imp, 2ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="520">See Revelation 4:10 for first use of this word, “pray” in Hit’pael verb binyan stem.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.5">Then a voice comes out from the throne, “HalleluYah! Praise, you servants of Yehovah, praise the name of Yehovah!” For both523 all the small and great before Him, fear His wrath!”  The Scriptures: And a voice came from the throne, saying, “Praise our Elohim, all you His servants and those who fear Him, both small and great!”  Aramaic: And a voice came forth from the throne, saying: Praise our God, all ye his servants; and such as fear him, small and great. v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) voice,” echad,”one,” (card yotzeh, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it goes me’ha’kise, “from/ halleluYah,” (to a man) praise Yah!” (v. Pi’el, imp, 2ms) halelu, “(to men) praise!” (v. Piel, avdei, “servants of,” (n mp constr) out,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, Yehovah halelu, “(to men) praise!” (v. Pi’el, et, (DO marker) shem, “name,” (n Yehovah va’chamat, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) wrath,” (n fs) yere’im, “we/ you (mp)/ they fear,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act lefanav, “before ha’kol, “the all,” (n shneihem “both, two,” (card num) katnim, “small,” gedolim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) great,” him/it,” (prep, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.6">And I heard a voice like the voice of His great companies, like the sound of many waters. And it was like great voices saying, “HalleluYah!  For Yehovah is mighty!”  The Scriptures: And I heard as the voice of a great crowd, as the sound of many waters and as the sound of mighty thunders, saying, “Halleluyah, for הוהי Ěl Shaddai reigns!  Aramaic: And I heard, as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of heavy thunders, saying: Hallelujah; for our Lord God, Omnipotent, reigneth. v' shema'ati, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kol, “voice, sound,” echad,”one,” (card ke’kol, “like/ as gadol, “great,” (adj va’c’kol, “and/ (the) voice,” (prep, but/ so/ or like/ as sound,” (prep, n associations, firms, (n mp) (prep, n fp, mayim, “waters,” gedolim, “many,” ve’k’mo, “and/ kolot, “voices, sounds,” (n mp) ha’omrim, “the halleluyah,”(to a man) praise Yah!” but/ so/ or like, as, similarly to,” (adv, large,” (adj mp) we/ you (mp)/ they those saying,” (v Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.7">“They rejoiced524 happily and gave Him honor, for the time of the wedding of the Lamb has come and His bride is prepared!”  The Scriptures: Let us be glad and rejoice and give Him praise, for the marriage of the Lamb has come, and His wife prepared herself.”  Aramaic: Let us rejoice and exult, and give glory to him: for the marriage supper of the Lamb hath come, and his bride hath made herself ready. nehi’eynu, “they enjoyed, rejoiced,” smechim, “happy, joyful,” (adj mp) liten, “and/ but/ so/ or to give, allow,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf) chevod, “honor,” (n season, a set time, appointed time,” (n (v. Nif’al, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms ha’chatuna, “the wedding,” (n fs) me’ha’se, “from/ ba, “he/it came,” ishto, “and/ but/ muchenet, “she/it is prepared,” (adj spouse, bride,” (n fs, 3ms pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.8">And He gave her pure, becoming, and beautiful silk to wear.  The Scriptures: And to her it was given to be dressed in fine linen, clean and bright, for the fine linen is the righteousnesses of the set-apart ones.  Aramaic: And it was granted her to be clothed in fine linen, bright and clean: for fine linen is the righteousnesses of the saints. v'noten, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it give(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, la, “to her/it,” (prep, 3fs pron) lilbosh, “to wear, b'meshi, “in/ with/ naki, “clean, pure, innocent,” (adj ms) v'tov, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) good, V'yafa, “and/ but/ so/ or beautiful, pretty, wonderful,” becoming,” (adj <note type="footnote" n="524">This word was crossed out by an unknown scribe and a marginal note added. The word was included in the translation. 525 See Revelation 2:17 for more details on this uniquely spelled word.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.9">Then he said to me, "Holy are those called to eat the evening meal with the Lamb.” For he said to me these are the words of Yehovah in truth.”   The Scriptures: And he said to me, “Write, ‘Blessed are those who have been called to the marriage supper of the Lamb!’” And he said to me, “These are the true words of Elohim.”  Aramaic: And he said to me, Write; Blessed are they who are called to the supper of the marriage feast of the Lamb. And he said to me, These my [sayings] are the true words of God. v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, kdoshim, “saint, holy, sacred,” (adj haym, “they,” (3mp le'ekol, “to eat (v. belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) which/ who/ whom he/it called,” (v. Pa’al/Qal. qatal, achilat: “eating of… (n fs constr) arev, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is pleasant, delicious,” (v. im, “with,” (prep) ha’se, “the lamb,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) Pa’al/Qal, act part, ele,“these,” (3ms, dvrayi, “words of,” b'emet, “in/ with/ truly,” (prep, n fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.10">Then I fell at his feet to pray to him, and he said to me, “See, don’t do this! I am of your friends and of your brothers who have the testimonies of Yeshua. Make your prayer to Yehovah!”  The Scriptures: And I fell at his feet to worship him, but he said to me, “See, do not do it! I am your fellow servant, and of your brothers who possess the witness of עשוהי. Worship Elohim! For the witness of עשוהי is the spirit of prophecy.”  Aramaic: And I fell at his feet, to worship him. And he said to me, See, [thou do it] not; I am thy fellow-servant, and of those thy brethren who have the testimony of Jesus. Worship ye God: for the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy. v’nafalti, “and/ but/ l’raglav,” to/ for/ belonging to his/its feet,” (prep, n ms) lhitpalel, “to pray,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, so/ or I fell,” (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal, (v. Hit’pael, inf belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) him/it,” (prep, 3ms al, “don’t, not,” ta’aseh, “you shall ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ha’ve’reika, “your u’m’eachika, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of u’me’eilu, “and/ see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, but/ so/ or from/ of Pa’al/Qal, Yiqtol, your brothers,” (prep, n mp, 2ms brothers,” (n mp, she’yesh, “that/ lahem, “to /for/ ha' eydut, “and/ asi, “(to a man) make, do! (v. tfilatcha, “your prayer,” (n 2ms la’Yehovah,”to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, which/ who/ whom them,” (prep, 3mp testimonies,” (n fp) Pa’al/Qal, imp 2fs) exists,” (rel part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.11">Then I saw the heavens open. And I saw a white horse, and sitting on him was named Faithful and True, for He will judge righteously.  The Scriptures: And I saw the heaven opened, and there was a white horse. And He who sat on him was called Trustworthy and True, and in righteousness He judges and fights.  Aramaic: And I saw heaven opened: and lo, a white horse; and he that sat on it, is called Faithful and True: and in righteousness he judgeth, and maketh war. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, she’hashamayim, “that/ which/ who/ niftachim, “we/ you ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, sus, “horse,” (n ms) echad,”one,” (card lavan, “white,” (mp)/ they, those opening’ (v. Nif’al, heavens,” (n mp) ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this, this one,” (pron, ms) she’yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), dwell(s),” aya, “he/it was,” (v ne'eman, “I/ you ve’e’met, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) upon him, by him, concerning him,” name,” (n ms, 3ms Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Nif’al, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ yishpot, “he/it will be’tse’dek, ‘in/ with/ by (the) righteousness,” (prep, adj ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.12">And His eyes were like a flame of fire and on His head were many crowns; and a name was written upon Him that no one knows - only He alone. v’einav, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its eyes,” haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, c' lahevet, “like/ as (the) flame,” (prep, eysh, “fire,” (n fs) v'al, ”and/ but/ so/ or on, upon,” (prep) harbeh, “many, head,” (n ms, 3ms much, a lot,” (adv) ktarim, “crowns,” v’ shem, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) name, name of,” (n ms) echad,”one,” (card ktuv, “written,” v' sum, “and/ but/ so/ any,” (in a neg echad,”one,” (card oto, “him/it,” (DO rak, “only, just,” hu, “he/it,” (3ms, alone,” (adv, 3ms Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.13">And He was dressed in clothing sprinkled with blood and His name was the Word of Yehovah.  The Scriptures: and having been dressed in a robe dipped in blood – and His Name is called: The Word of הוהי.  Aramaic: And he was clothed with a vesture sprinkled with blood; and his name is called, The Word of God. v' lavush, “and/ b’m’Le'vush, “in/ echad,”one,” (card she' haya, “that/ zarak, “he/it sprinkled,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, alav, “on him/it, upon him/it, by him, concerning dam, “blood,” (n which/ who/ whom you(ms)/ he/it was clothing (prep, n he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, him/it,” (prep, 3ms Pa'al/Qal, pssv part, v’semo, “and/ but/ aya, “he/it was,” (v dibur, “utterance, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, talking,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.14">And all the armies of the heavens follow Him on white horses, wearing clothing of white silk.   The Scriptures: And the armies in the heaven, dressed in fine linen, white and clean, followed Him on white horses.  Aramaic: And the soldiery of heaven followed him, on white horses, clad in garments of fine linen, pure [and] white. v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) all,” (n tzvaot, “hosts, armies,” (n mp) hashamayim, “the heavens, skies,” (n holchim, “the we/ you (mp)/ they, those going,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, susei, “horses of,” him/it,” (prep, pron lavan, “white,” v’kulam, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) all,” (n ms, 3mp lovshim, “we/ you/ they, those putting on, wearing,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” meshi, “silk,” (n lavan, “white,” garments,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.15">Coming from his mouth is a double-edged sword to strike the people with it. He drives them with a rod of iron528 and in the fierceness of the anger of Yehovah, rebuking honestly for the suffering of the land. u’m’piv “and/ but/ so/ or from his/its mouth,” (prep, n ms, 3ms pronom) cherev, “a sword,” pipiyot, “double edged,” (n fp) k’dei, “be able, lehakot, “to beat, bo, “in/ with/ by according to, as, in Pa’al/Qal, qatal, order to,” (conj) Hif’il, inf constr) v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms yinhag, “he/it will ve’hochiach, “he/it proved, rebuked,” peoples, nations,” drive, lead,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, those,” (prep pron with/ by/ (the) rod of, staff, branch, scepter,” (prep, n (v Hif’il, qatal, l’inuy, “to/ for/ be’charon, “in/ with/ by (the) af, “anger, nose,” Yehovah belonging to (the) fierceness,” (prep, uprightness, level place,” (prep, n tortured,” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="528">See Psalms 2:9. This phrase is also used in Revelation 2:27a, and 12:5.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.16">And the name written on His clothes is, “King of the kings, and Lord of the lords.”  The Scriptures: And on His robe and on His thigh He has a name written: SOVEREIGN OF SOVEREIGNS AND MASTER OF MASTERS.  Aramaic: And he hath upon his vesture and upon his thigh the words written: King of kings, and Lord of lords. v’shem, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) name,” echad, ”one,” (card ktuv! “written,” kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this melech, “king,” (n clothing,” (n ms) ha’melachim, “the adon, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) master, master(s), lord(s),”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.17">Then I saw a messenger standing in the sun and he shouted with a loud voice and said to all the birds under the heavens, “Come! Reap from the evening meal of the great Elohim!”  The Scriptures: And I saw one messenger standing in the sun, and he cried with a loud voice, saying to all the birds that fly in mid-heaven, “Come and gather together for the supper of the great Elohim,  Aramaic: And I saw an angel standing in the sun; and he cried with a loud voice, saying to all the fowls that fly in the midst of heaven: Come ye, assemble unto this great supper of God; ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, mal’ach, “angel, echad,”one,” (card amad, “he/it stood,” b’shemesh, “in/ ve’tsaak, “he/it b' kol, “in/ with/ by (the) voice, sound,” (prep, n messenger,” (n ms) (v. Pa’al/Qal, act with/ by (the) sun,” shouted, cried,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it shall le’kol, “to/ for/ she' hem, “that/ mitachat, “under, hashamayim, “the heavens, skies,” (n belonging to (the) all,” (prep, n ms) which/ who/ whom they,” (pron 3mp) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, lechu! “(to men) go! come!” (v. Pi’el, imp, 2mp) kulchem, “all of le’achilat, “to (the) erev, “evening,” (n m’el’o’hay, “of/ from (the) God(s) of,” (n mp constr) collect, reap, pick up,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, you (mp),”’ (n mp, eating of,” (n fs</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.18">“So that you eat the flesh of the kings, the overseers, the strong men, the horses and those riding them, even the flesh of the small and the great, the slaves and the free.”   The Scriptures: to eat the flesh of sovereigns, and the flesh of commanders, and the flesh of strong ones, and the flesh of horses and of those who sit on them, and the flesh of all people, free and slave, both small and great.”  Aramaic: that ye may eat the flesh of kings, and the flesh of captains of thousands, and the flesh of valiant men, and the flesh of horses and of those who sit on them, and the flesh of all the free-born and of slaves, and of the small and the great. k’dei, “be able, she’tochlu, ‘that/ which you (mp) m' ha’melachim, v’sarim, “and/ but/ so/ or the ministers, v’ha’basar, “and/ according to, as, in “from/ of the kings, order to,” (conj) shall eat,” (prep, v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, rulers,” (prep, n princes, leaders, overseers,” (n mp) u’bsar-, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) meat, ha’susim, “the horses,” (n mp) u’me’eilu, “and/ ha’rocvim,” the we/ you (mp)/ v’ha’basar, “and/ ha’kevanim, “the least, small,” (adj but/ so/ or from/ of her/it,” (prep Ar. they, those riding,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act ve’gedolim, “and/ ’meshuchrarim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) large, great,” (adj “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those are freed,” (v. Pi’el, pssv <note type="footnote" n="529">Second Temple spelling found in The War of the Jews by Josephus, Rome c. 73CE.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.19">Then I saw the beast and the rulers of the land assemble their armies to make war with Him sitting upon the throne, and with His army.  The Scriptures: And I saw the beast, and the sovereigns of the earth, and their armies, gathered together to fight Him who sat on the horse and His army.  Aramaic: And I saw the beast of prey, and the kings of the earth, and their warriors, that they assembled to wage battle with him who sat on the [white] horse, and with his warriors. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ve’malchei, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) kings of,” (n mp aretz, “earth, land,” et, (DO marker) ma’chanaihem: “from/ of their, camps of armed assembled,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, hosts, army camp,” (prep, n mp, 3mp la'asot, “to do, to mil’cha’ma, “war, al, “with,” (prep) ze, 'this (pron, ms) she’yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), dwell(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act al, “upon, in, on, over, by, for, both, beyond, through,” throne, chair” (n v'Im, “and/ but/ so/ or with,” (prep) “from/ of his/its army,” (prep, n ms, 3ms pronom)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.20">And the beast was captured with the false prophet, who was performing signs to incite those following who took the sign532 of the beast and prayed to him.  They were sent to533 Sheol burning with sulfur.  The Scriptures: And the beast was seized, and with him the false prophet who worked signs in his presence, by which he led astray those who received the mark of the beast and those who worshipped his image. The two were thrown alive into the lake of fire burning with sulphur.  Aramaic: And the beast of prey was captured, and the false prophet that was with him, who did those prodigies before him, whereby he seduced them who had received the mark of the beast of prey and who worshipped his image. And they were both cast alive into the lake of fire, which burneth with sulphur. v’nishbe, “and/ but/ im, “with,” (prep) navi, “prophet,” (n sheker, “the false, otot, “the signals, so/ or he/it was “the I/ you (ms)/ captured,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part, lefanav, “before k’dei, “be able, according to, as, lehasit, “to incite, to inflame, incite,” l'ilu, “whereas, if, but considering, she’lakhu, “that/ him/it,” (prep, 3ms which/ who/ whom symbol, sign,” (n he/it took,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal qatal, past, 3mp) beast,” (prep, n fs) following,” (prep, mitpallim, “we/ you (mp)/ they pray,” (v. Hit’pael, act part, mp) v’nishl’chu, “and/ she’ole, “’in/ with/ bo’er, “burning,” gofrit, “in/ with/ by (the) sulfur,” but/ so/ or they were sent,’’ (v. by (the) grave,” Nif’al, qatal, past, <note type="footnote" n="532">This word is “sign,” such as a sign from heaven. This is not the same word for the “sign” of the beast. See interlinear table for more details. 533 Literally, “in.” The prefix is ב bet not ל lamed, so it is “in” not “to” and was translated as, “to.” 534 See Revelation 13:17 for more details on this unique word.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.19.21">And the others were killed by the sword (which came out of His mouth) of the one who sat on the horse; and all the beasts of the field were satiated with their flesh.  The Scriptures: And the rest were killed with the sword which came from the mouth of Him who sat on the horse, and all the birds were filled with their flesh.  Aramaic: And the rest were slain by the sword of him that sat on the horse, by that [sword] which issueth from his mouth: and all the fowls were satiated with their flesh. v’ha’acharim, “and/ nehergu, ‘“they were killed,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past m'ze, “of/ from this,” (prep, ms) she’yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom al’yadei, “by the hand of,” (idiom) others,” (adj mp) matter,” (n ms) Note: missing in Pa’al/Qal, qatal, she’yatza, “that/ m’piv, “from/ of his/its mouth,” (prep, n 3ms v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or the) all,” (n haiyot, “beasts, living creatures, animals,” (n fp) which/ who/ whom exited, went out,” Pa’al/Qal,qatal, m’bsaram, “from/ were satisfied,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, flesh,” (prep, n ms,</verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.20">
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.1">Then I saw a messenger descended from the heavens, and he had the key of the deep, and in his hand was a great chain.  The Scriptures: And I saw a messenger coming down from the heaven, having the key to the pit of the deep and a great chain in his hand.  Aramaic: And I saw an angel that descended from heaven, having the key of the abyss, and a great chain in his hand. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, echad,”one,” (card mi’shamayim, “of/ v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ aya, “he/it was,” (v descended,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, Pa'al/Qal, qatal, heavens,” (n mp) him/it,” (prep, 3ms ha’ mafteach, “the m’tehom, “from/ u’v’yado, “and/ gedolah, “great,” but/ so/ or in/ with/ deep,” (prep, n fs) by his/its hand,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.2">And he took the dragon, who is Satan, and bound him for a thousand years.  The Scriptures: And he seized the dragon, the serpent of old, who is the Devil and Satan, and bound him for a thousand years,  Aramaic: And he seized the dragon, the old serpent, who is the Deceiver and Satan, who seduced the whole habitable world: and he bound him a thousand years. v’lakach, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it took,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, “Satan,” ‘accuser, adversary,” (n ms vaye’esor, “and/ but/ so /or he/it oto, “him/it,” (DO elef, “thousand,” dragon, serpent, sea monster, dinosaur, which/ who/ whom she/it,” (rel part, (v Pa’al/Qal, qatal, monster, venomous snake, crocodile, jackal,” (n ms) shanayim, “years,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.3">Then he threw him to the deep, closed538 him in and sealed it from above so that he could not incite the peoples until he had been restrained for a thousand years. Afterwards, he will be free for a short time.  The Scriptures: and he threw him into the pit of the deep, and shut him up, and set a seal on him, so that he should lead the nations no more astray until the thousand years were ended. And after that he has to be released for a little while.  Aramaic: And he cast him into the abyss, and closed and sealed upon him; so that he might deceive the nations no more, until these thousand years shall be completed: but after that, he will be loosed for a little time. v'hishlich, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it threw,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, 3ms) oto, “him/it,” (DO l'tehom: “to/ for/ belonging to the abyss, chasm, v’sagor, “and/ but/ oto, “him/it,” (DO v'chatam, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it mil'ma'la, “from/ of above, on high, so/ or close” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf abs) signed, sealed,” (v. deep,” (prep, n fs) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, directional hey) k’dei, “be able, she’lo, that/ which/ yuchal, “he/it will le'hasit “to incite, inflame,” (V. Hifil. ad, “until,” (prep) she’cal, “that/ according to, as, in peoples, nations,” which/ who/ whom order to,” (conj) no/not, (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, he/it restrained,” Pa’al/Qal, qatal, elef, “a thousand,” shanim, “years,” (n vachar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) bach, “In/ with/ by you,“ (prep, 2fs, yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, chofesh, “I/ you/ he/it is free” (v. season, a set time, appointed time,” (n Pa’al/Qal, act part, mu’at, “few, few in numbers, little,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.4">Then I saw thrones, and those sitting upon them. He authorized them to judge those believing and testifying of Yeshua. These are the ones who did not take the sign of the beast upon their foreheads, nor did they pray to him nor to his idol. These are the ones who live and rule with Yeshua for a thousand years.    The Scriptures: And I saw thrones – and they sat on them, and judgment was given to them – and the lives of those who had been beheaded because of the witness they bore to עשוהי and because of the Word of Elohim, and who did not worship the beast, nor his image, and did not receive his mark upon their foreheads or upon their hands. And they lived and reigned with Messiah for a thousand years  Aramaic: And I saw thrones, and [persons] sat on them, and judgment was given to them, and to the souls that were beheaded for the testimony of Jesus and for the word of God: and these are they who had not worshipped the beast of prey, nor its image, neither had they received the mark upon their forehead or on their hand; and they lived and reigned with their Messiah those thousand years. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kisot, “thrones,” (n va’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (3mp yosevim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those sitting, dwelling,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act, aleihem, “upon v’le’hem, “and/ noten, “I/ you (ms)/ them,” (prep, 3 mp them,” (prep, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, act part, lishpot, “to judge,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf eilu, “these, the ha’ma’aminim, u’me’idim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those testifying,” (v. Hif’il, act part, yeshu, “Yeshua,” veilu, “and/ but/ so/ or these, those, following,” (pron, “the we/ you (mp)/ the following,” mitzeihim, “their ve' lo, “and/ but/ which/ who/ whom no/not,” (rel part, symbol, sign,” (n Pa’al/Qal, qatal beast,” (prep, n fs) tefalelu, “we/ you (mp) /they, those o, “or,” (conj) l’pesel, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) idol,” (prep, n ms) v' eilu, “and/ but/ or/ so whereas, chayim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those him/it,” (prep, 3ms whom, to, for, of, Hit’pael, act part, following,” (pron) Pa’al/Qal, act pat, him/it,” (rel part, prep, 3ms pronom) u’moshlim, “and/ but/ so/ they, those im, “with,” (prep) Yeshu, “Yeshua,” elef, “thousand,” shanayim, “years,” Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="539">This word does not fit in the context so has been left out of the translation. 540 The scribe did not add the gershayim (two slash marks) as was his custom in this manuscript.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.5">Indeed, the other dead are not rising until the thousand years of imprisonment are over. But this is the first resurrection. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay ha'maytim, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it die(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act acherim, “other, lo, “no/ not” (neg kamim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those ad, “until,” (prep) she’kala, “that/ another, different,” which/ who/ whom imprisonment,” (n Pa’al/Qal, act part, shanayim, “years,” ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, hi, “she/ it,” (3fs takumot, “revival, resurrection,” (n fs ha'rishonah, “the first,” (adj fs) thousand,” (n ms) <note type="footnote" n="541">See first occurrence of this word in Revelation 13:17.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.6">Holy is he who has a part in the first resurrection, because there is not a snare of another death for them. Only those will be priests542 to Yehovah and His messiah and rule for a thousand years.  The Scriptures: Blessed and set-apart is the one having part in the first resurrection. The second death possesses no authority over these, but they shall be priests of Elohim and of Messiah, and shall reign with Him a thousand years.  Aramaic: Blessed and holy is he that hath part in this first resurrection: over them the second death hath no dominion; but they shall be, [nay] are, priests of God and of his Messiah; and they will reign with him the thousand years. qadosh, “holy/ set apart/ sanctified/ hu, “he/it,” (3ms, mi,” ‘who?” (inter she’yesh, “that/ chelek, “portion, b'tkuma, “in/ with/ which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms consecrated,” (adj exists,” (rel part, ha'rishona, “the first,” (adj fs) aleihem, “upon lo, “no/ not,” (neg pach, “a snare,” (n m'avet: “from/ of (the) death,” (prep, them,” (prep, 3 mp there exists,” (part) akheret, “other, rak, “only, just,” he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, yi’hyu, “they will kohanim, “priests,” l’Yehovah, “to/ gor/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, u'me'shicho, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its Messiah (n ms, 3ms pronom) another, different,” (v. Pa’al/Qal yiqtol, u'moshlim, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those ruling, reigning,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act imo, “with him/it,” (prep, 3ms pronom) elef, “thousand,” (n she’nayim, “years,” (n fp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.7">But after a thousand years, Satan will be freed from his guards,  The Scriptures: And when the thousand years have ended, Satan shall be released from his prison,  Aramaic: And when these thousand years shall be completed, Satan will be released from his prison; v’achar, “and/ but/ so/ or after,” (prep) elef, “thousand,” yiga’el, “he/it will “Satan,” ‘accuser, adversary,” (n ms) purchased, freed, guards,” (n mp, 3ms pronom) added mater lectionis Nif’al, yiqtol, fut</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.8">Then he will go and entice the peoples throughout the four corners of the land, and Gog and Magog, to gather his army for battle: for their number is as the sand of the sea.  The Scriptures: and he shall go out to lead the nations astray which are in the four corners of the earth, Goḡ and Maḡoḡ, to gather them together for battle, whose number is as the sand of the sea.  Aramaic: and will go forth to seduce the nations that are in the four corners of the earth, Gog and Magog; and to assemble them for battle, whose number is as the sand of the sea. v’yelech, “and/ but/ l’hesit, “to incite, inflame,” (v. Hif’il, arba, “four,” (card pinot, “corners,” (n so/ or he/it will peoples, nations,” go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) v’gog, “and/ but/ v’mgog, “and/ but/ et, (DO marker) chayalo, “his/its army,” (n ms) lavo, “to come,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, inf “to/ for/ belonging u’misparam, “and/ ha’yam, “the sea,” but/ so/ or their number,” (n ms, there exists,” (part)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.9">And they trampled the wide ground surrounding the soldiers of the holy ones and the beloved city. But fire from the heavens fell and burned them.  The Scriptures: And they came up over the breadth of the earth and surrounded the camp of the set-apart ones and the beloved city. And fire came down from Elohim out of the heaven and consumed them. va’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (3m ha’adama, “the ground,” (n fs) savav, “and/ but/ Pa’al/Qal, qatal, surrounded,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ve’ha’ir, “and/ but/ so/ or the city,” (n h’ahuva, “beloved, v’nafal, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it fell,” eysh, “fire,” (n fs) mi’shamayim, “of/ ve’saraf, “and/ but/ loved,” (adj fs) sacred,” (adj mp) heavens,” (prep, n qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, qatal,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.10">And Satan, the inciter, will be thrown into the fire of the Sheol, where the false prophet is. They will be afflicted day and night forever and ever.  The Scriptures: And the devil, who led them astray, was thrown into the lake of fire and sulphur where the beast and the false prophet are. And they shall be tortured day and night forever and ever.  Aramaic: And the Accuser who seduced them, was cast into the lake of fire and sulphur, where also were the beast of prey and the false prophet: and they shall be tormented, day and night, for ever and ever. “and/ but/ so/ or the ha’misit, “the I/ you (ms)/ he/it otam, “them,” (DO hushlach, “he/it was thrown,” (v. Hif’il, pssv past, be’esh, “in/ with/ shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” grave, pit,” (name) adversary,” (n ms) incites,” (v. HIf’il, she' haya, “that/ he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, v' navi, “and/ but/ ha’ sheker, “the false, lie,” (n ms) yit’anu, “and/ but/ so/ or they will be which/ who/ whom those,” (prep, 3mp prophet,” (n ms) part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) Hit’pael, yiqtol, yom, “day,” (n ms) ve’ laylah, “and/ but/ so/ or night,” Idiom: forever and ever me’olam, “from/ of everlasting,” (prep, n ms) v’ad, “and/ but/so/or until, up to,” (prep) olam, “everlasting,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.11">Then I saw a great white throne and He who sat upon it. For the heavens and the ground flee before him, and no place is found for him.545  The Scriptures: And I saw a great white throne and Him who was sitting on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away, and no place was found for them.  Aramaic: And I saw a great white throne, and Him who sitteth thereon; from whose presence the earth and heaven fled away, and this their place was not found. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, echad,”one,” (card kise, “throne,” (n gadol, “great,” (adj v' levan, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) white,” haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, v’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, ms) she’ yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it sit(s), dwell(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act alav, “on him/it, by him/it, concerning him/it,” (prep, 3ms u' mipanav, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of nas, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it flee(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, hashamayim, the heavens, skies,” (n v’ ha’ adama, “and/ but/ so/ or the ground,” (n fs) v' lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no, not, neither,” face,” (prep, 3ms nimtza, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it was makom, “place,” (n found,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms) him/it,” (prep, 3ms Then I saw the dead with them, the least and the great, standing before Yehovah, and the scrolls were opened. Then another scroll was opened.  And this scroll was the Scroll of Life to judge the dead according to what was written in the scrolls, and according to their works.  The Scriptures: And I saw the dead, small and great, standing before the throne, and books were opened. And another book was opened, which is the Book of Life. And the dead were judged from what was written in the books, according to their works.  Aramaic: And I saw the dead, great and small standing before the throne; and the books were opened; and another book was opened, which is [the book] of life. And the dead were judged from the things written in the books, according to their deeds. v’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ha'maytim, “the I/ she' b'hem, “that/ which/ who/ whom with/ in/ with/ by them,” (rel part, ha’ q'tanim, “the small(s),” (adj mp) omdim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those “and/ but/ so/ or the big, large, great,” before the face of, before me, in front Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, prep, 3mp pronom) Yehovah v'nif't'chu, “and/ but/ so/ or they ha's'farim, “the scrolls, books, documents,” (n v'sefer, “and/ but/ so/ or scroll, book, document,” (n ms) acher, “another, other,” (adj ms) nif'tach, “he/it was ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, were opened,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, Nif’al, qatal, past, Idiom: “book of life” lishpot, “to judge, ha'maytim, “the I/ kfi, “according to,” she’katuv, “that/ be’sefarim, “in/ with/ by (the) books,” (prep, n which/ who/ whom written,” (adj ms) sefer, “book, scroll, document,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, act part, ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp) k'fi, “and/ but/ so/ or according to,” <note type="footnote" n="544">See 1 Chronicles 29:10. 545 It is unclear who or what this verse is referring. The word could be translated as either him or it, and the only masculine singular words in the context are the throne and the one sitting on it. It could also be referring to Satan, the Inciter from the previous verse.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.13">Then the sea threw out the dead that were in it.  And the Sheol gave the dead to be judged, everyone according to his works.  The Scriptures: And the sea gave up the dead who were in it, and Death and She’ol gave up the dead who were in them. And they were judged, each one according to his works.  Aramaic: And the sea gave up the dead in it; and death and the grave gave up the dead in them. And they were judged, each one according to his deeds. v'zarak, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it threw, cast,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, ha’yam, “the sea,” et, (DO marker) ha'maytim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those dying,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, she'hayu, “that/ ba, “in/ with/ on/ la’chutz, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) which/ who/ whom they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal. qatal, v’hamet, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ et, (DO marker) v'yishaf'tu, “and/ but/ so/ or they kol, “all,” (n ms) grave, pit,” (name) "the/that we/ you (mp)/ they, those he/it die(s)” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, will be judged,” (v. Nif’al, yiqtol, fut, Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa'al/Qal, act part, echad,”one,” (card kfi, “according to,” ma'a'sav, “his/its deeds, works,” (n mp, 3ms pronom) <note type="footnote" n="546">The original word was smeared, and an unknown scribe placed a mark above it and with the correct word in the margin. This word was included in the final translation.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.14">So, the death and the Gehinnom were thrown548 into the fire: for this (the fire)549 is another death.  The Scriptures: And Death and She’ol were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death.  Aramaic: And death and the grave were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death, [namely,] this lake of fire. v’ha’mavet, “and/ v' ha’gehinnom, nushlach, “they were thrown,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, b’esh, “in/ with/ by (the) fire,” (prep, n v' zot, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, mavet, “death,” (n akheret, “other, and/ but/ so/ or the Gehinnom, hell, or another, different,” Hinnom,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.20.15">And moreover, if one is not found written in the Scroll of Life550 he is thrown into the fire.  The Scriptures: And if anyone was not found written in the Book of Life, he was thrown into the lake of fire.    Aramaic: And if any one was not found enrolled in the book of life, he was cast into this lake of fire. Idiom: “in the book of life” v' gam, “and/ but/ so/ or moreover/ lo, “no/ not” (neg nimtza, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it is echad,”one,” (card ktuv, “written,” b’ sefer, “in/ with/ by (the) book, scroll, found,” (v. Nif’al, document,” (prep, n ms) ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp) hushlach, “he/it was thrown,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, b’esh, “in/ with/ by (the) fire” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="550">Literally, “scroll of lives,” but usually translated as “book of life.” See also Revelation 3:5 and 20:12.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.21">
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.1">Then I saw a new heavens and a new ground,551 for the first heavens and the earth perish, and the sea will be no more.  The Scriptures: And I saw a renewed heaven and a renewed earth, for the former heaven and the former earth had passed away, and the sea is no more.  Aramaic: And I saw new heavens, and a new earth: for the former heaven and the former earth had passed away: and the sea was no more. ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, chodashim, “new,” v’adama, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) ground,” (n fs) chadashah, “new,” shamiyim,” the heavens,” (n mp) heavens,” (n mp) v' ha’eretz, “and/ ha’ rishonim, “the yigva, “he/it will die, perish,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, v’ ha' yom, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ lo, “no/ not,” (neg “yesh, “there is, first,” (adj, mp) there exists,” (part)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.2">For I, John saw the new, holy city Jerusalem, descend from the heavens to the earth. It was adorned as a woman silent before her husband.  The Scriptures: And I, Yoḥanan, saw the set-apart city, renewed Yerushalayim, coming down out of the heaven from Elohim, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.  Aramaic: And I saw the holy city, the New Jerusalem, descending from God out of heaven, prepared like a bride adorned for her husband. v' ani, “and/ but/ so/ or I, I am,” ye’annos, John, ra'iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ha'ir, “the city,” (n kdosha, “holy,” ha’ chadasha, “the Note: transliterated mi’shamayim, “from/ of (the) heavens,” (n mp) ha'ya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, k’isha, “like/ as a woman,” (prep, n ha’m’sheket, “the silent,” (adj ms) descended,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, “adorned,” (adj ba’alah, “master, husband,” (n ms) before the face of, before me, in front <note type="footnote" n="551">Isaiah 65:17.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.3">Then I heard a loud voice from the throne that said, “See, the Tabernacle of Yehovah is near mankind!  So, He was Elohim to them, and they will be His people.”  The Scriptures:  And I heard a loud voice from the heaven saying, “See, the Booth of Elohim is with men, and He shall dwell with them, and they shall be His people, and Elohim Himself shall be with them and be their Elohim.  Aramaic: And I heard a great voice from heaven, which said: Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men; and he dwelleth with them: they will be his people; and God will be with them, a God to them. v' shema'ati, “and/ but/ so/ or I heard,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, kol, “voice,” (n ms) gadol, “great,” (adj me’hakiseh, “from/ she’amar, “that/ re'ei, “see!” (v. which/ who/ whom Pa'al/Qal, imp, ms) “dwelling place, he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, tabernacle,” (n ms) etzel, “by, near,” v’hayah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was,” lahem, “to /for/ va’hem, “and/ but/ so/ or they,” (pron, man, mankind” (n ”God(s),” (n mp) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) them,” (prep, 3mp yih'yu, “they will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp) belonging to (the) people, nation,” him/it,” (prep, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.4">And Yehovah Elohim wipes every tear from every face, and death will not reign again,554 nor will there be any grief, shouting, or sufferings because the first has passed away.   The Scriptures: “And Elohim shall wipe away every tear from their eyes, and there shall be no more death, nor mourning, nor crying. And there shall be no more pain, for the former matters have passed away.”  Aramaic: And every tear will be wiped from their eyes; and there will no more be death, nor mourning, nor wailing; nor shall pain be any more; because the former things are passed away. u’ma’chah, “and/ but/ so/ or I/ you (ms)/ he/it blot(s), Elohim, “God(s)” dim’ah, “tear,” (n m’ al, “from/ of kol, “all, every” (n above, over, on top Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve’ha’mot, “and/ lo, “no/ not” (neg yishmol, “’he/it will rule, reign,” v’ lo, “and/ but/ so/ sum, “any,” (in a tza'ar, “sadness, disappointment, or (the) no/ not” yiqtol, fut, 3ms) affliction,” (n ms) ve’tzoakot, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those shout,” (Pa’al/Qal, act v'inuyim, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, tortures,” (n mp) <note type="footnote" n="553">The lamed is an Aramaism and is acting as a direct object pointer and therefore does not affect the translation. 554 Isaiah 25:8. 555 In Deuteronomy 17:15, this word is used in a negative sense as an infinitive absolute.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.5">And the One sitting on the throne said, “See, I made all things new.” And He said to me “Write, for these are the words of truth.”  The Scriptures: And He who was sitting on the throne said, “See, I make all matters new.” And He said to me, “Write, for these words are true and trustworthy.”  Aramaic: And He who sat on the throne, said: Behold, I make all things new. And he said: Write; because these are the faithful and true words of God. ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ this,” (pron, she’yoshev, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it ha’kise, “the throne,” (n ms) amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, re'ei, “see!” (v. ani, “I,” (1cs pron) Pa'al/Qal, imp, ms) sit(s), dwell(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, isitai, “I did, made, did,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, ha’kol, “the all,” (n chadash, “new,” v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ktov!, “(to a man) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) qatal, past, 1cs) Pa’al/Qal, imp, eleh,“these,” (3ms, emet, “truth,” (n fs) hi, “she/ it,” (3fs “words, matters, things,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.6">Then he said to me, “All has passed. I am the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End, and I will freely give living water to the thirsty.”  The Scriptures: And He said to me, “It is done! I am the ‘Aleph’ and the ‘Taw’, the Beginning and the End. To the one who thirsts I shall give of the fountain of the water of life without payment.  Aramaic: And he said to me: I am Alpha and Omega, the Beginning and the Completion: to him who thirsteth, will I give of the fountain of living water, gratis. v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, avar, “he/it was a’kol, “the all,” (n ani, “I,” (1cs pron) v' ha' acharon, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) last,” (n ms) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, pssv past, 3ms) v' ha' sof, “and/ but/ so/ or the end,” (n ms) ani, “I,” (1cs pron) eten, “I will give,” le’h’tszame, “to/ for/ belonging to the thirsty,” (prep, mayim, “waters,” chayim “living,” “beginning,” (n (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) charge,” (prep, adv with adv suffix)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.7">“He that prevails will inherit everything, and I will be Elohim to him, and he will be My son.”   The Scriptures: “The one who overcomes shall inherit all this, and I shall be his Elohim and he shall be My son.  Aramaic: He that overcometh, shall inherit these things; and I will be his God, and he shall be my son. mi, “who?” (inter she’menateach, yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, me’ha’kol, “from/ of (the) all,” (prep, v' ani, “and/ so, but/ or I,” (1cs yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it prevails,” (rel Pa’al/Qal, act part, part, v. Pi'el, act v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it,” (3ms yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, le’ben, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) son,” (prep, n ms) belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pronom) him/it,” (prep, 3ms</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.8">But, to unbelievers,559 murderers, harlots, sorcerers, and deceivers, I will give their wages from the fire of the Sheol, burning with fire and sulfur. This is the second death.  The Scriptures: “But as for the cowardly, and untrustworthy, and abominable, and murderers, and those who whore, and drug sorcerers, and idolaters, and all the false, their part is in the lake which burns with fire and sulphur, which is the second death.”  Aramaic: But to the timid, and the unbelieving, and to the sinful, and polluted, and to manslayers, and whoremongers, and sorcerers, and idolaters, and to all false persons, their portion shall be in the lake that burneth with fire and sulphur, which is the second death. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay le’he’ainu,”to/ for/ belonging to the no, ma'aminim, “we/ you (mp)/ they believe, those believing,” (v. ve’le’rotzchim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to we/ you (mp)/ they murder,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, ve'le'zonim. "and/ but/ so/ or we/ you (mp)/ they, those ve’le’mechashfim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ ve’le’kizvnim, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) we/ you (mp)/ they, those who deceive,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, for/ belonging to (the) we/ you (mp)/ they, those who do Hif’il, act part, mp) adultery, whores,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act witchcraft,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, eten, “I will give,” et, (DO marker) shcaram, “their payment, wage,” me’esh, “from/ of (the) fire,” (prep, ha’soref, “the I/ you/ he/it burns, incinerate,” (v. b’esh, “in/ with/ by (the) fire,” (prep, n (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 1cs) abyss, grave,” (n Pa’al/Qal, act part, gofrit, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) sulfur,” v' zot, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (fs hi, “she/ it,” (3fs ha’ sheniyah, “the <note type="footnote" n="558">The lamed is an Aramaism and is acting as a direct object pointer and does not affect the translation. 559 Literally, “those without belief.”</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.9">Then one of the seven messengers who had the bowls in their hands filled with the seven last plagues came to me and said, “Come and see the woman, the bride of the Lamb!"  The Scriptures: And one of the seven messengers who held the seven bowls filled with the seven last plagues came to me and spoke with me, saying, “Come, I shall show you the bride, the Lamb’s wife.”  Aramaic: And there came one of those seven angels, who have the seven cups filled with the seven last plagues, and talked with me, saying: Come, I will show thee the bride, the wife of the Lamb. uvah, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it came,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, li, “to/ for/ to me,” echad,”one,” (card she' haya, “that/ (prep, 1cs pron) which/ who/ whom was,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, messengers,” (n hand,” (prep, n fs, seven,” (prep, card ha’ke'arot, “the bowls, plates, mele'im, “we/ you (mp)/ they fill,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, nega’im, “strokes, plagues, diseases, acharonim, “last,” v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) saucers,” (prep, n seven,” (prep, card marks, plague spots, marks of leprosy,” (n mp) qatal, past, 3ms) v’re’eh, “and/ but/ ha' ishah, “the woman,” (n fs) m’ha’se, “from/ of the lamb,” (prep, n Pa’al/Qal, imp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.10">And he led me to a mountain that was large and high, and he showed me the great, holy city, Jerusalem. It came down from the heavens to the earth.  The Scriptures: And he carried me away in the Spirit to a great and high mountain, and showed me the great city, the set-apart Yerushalayim, descending out of the heaven from Elohim,  Aramaic: And he bore me away in the spirit, to a mountain great and high, and he showed me the holy city, Jerusalem, descending out of heaven from God; ve’nahag, and/ but/ har, “mountain,” (n echad,”one,” (card she' haya, “that/ gadol, “great,” (adj so/ or “he/it led, marker, 1cs pron) which/ who/ whom was,” (rel part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ve’gavoah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) tall, high,” (adj ve’her’a, “and/ but/ so /or he/it ha'ir, “the city,” (n gadol, “great,” (adj ha'ir, “the city,” (n ha’kadoshah, “the holy, saintly,” (adj belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) Pa’al/Qal, qatal, yarad, “he/itl descended,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mi’shamayim, “of/ le’aretz, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) earth, land,” (prep, heavens,” (prep, n <note type="footnote" n="562">This is singular (hand); however, it is possible that the scribe left out the yod, which would make it plural (yadim). The English translation makes it plural to make sense in English.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.11">The glory of Yehovah was upon her as the light of the precious stone, called Jasper.   The Scriptures: having the esteem of Elohim, and her light was like a most precious stone, like a jasper stone, clear as crystal,  Aramaic: in which was the glory of God, as a brilliant light, and resembling a very precious gem; like a jasper stone, resembling crystal. v’tif'eret, “and/ but/ so/ or glory,” (n fs) Yehovah aleha, “on, upon her/it,” (prep, pron u’me'orah, “and/ but/ for/ or from/of her/its light,” (prep, n ms, 3fs pronom) haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, k’or, “like/ as (the) shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” even, “the stone,” ha' nikra, “he/it was named,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, yashfe, “Jasper,” pleasant,” (adj fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.12">And it had a wall and twelve large gates. On the twelve gates were twelve messengers563 and the twelve names of the twelve tribes of Israel  The Scriptures: and having a great and high wall, having twelve gates, and at the gates twelve messengers, and names written on them, which are those of the twelve tribes of the children of Yisra’ĕl:  Aramaic: And it had a wall great and lofty, which had twelve gates, and names inscribed on them, which are the names of the twelve tribes of the children of Israel. ve’la, “and/ but/ so/ haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, choma, “wall,” (n gedolim, “great,” ve’shnayim, “and/ eser, “ten,” (card sha’arim, “gates,” but/ so/ or (the) her/it,” (prep, 3fs v'al,”and/ but/ so/ shnayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card ve’shnayim, “and/ eser, “ten,” (card but/ so/ or (the) two,” (card num) messengers,” (n shemot, “names,” m’ shnayim, “from/ eser, “ten,” (card shivtam, “tribes,” shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” yisrael, “Israel,” (prep, card num)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.13">to the east, three gates; to the west, three gates; to the north, three gates; and to the south, three gates. mi’mizrach, “from/ sheloshah, “three,” sha’arim, “gates,” u’me’ma’arav, “and/ but/ so/ or sheloshah, “three,” u’me’tsapon, “and/ sheloshah, “three,” but/ so/ or (the) north,” (prep, n west,” (prep, n ms) u’me’darom, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of (the) south,” (prep, sheloshah, “three,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.14">The wall of the city had twelve foundations and on them were inscribed the names of the twelve sent ones (disciples) of the Lamb.  The Scriptures: And the wall of the city had twelve foundations, and on them were the names of the twelve emissaries of the Lamb.  Aramaic: And the wall of the city had twelve foundations, and upon them the twelve names of the twelve legates of the Lamb. ve’le’chomat, “and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) wall of…” (prep, n ha’ir, “the city,” (n ba, “in/ with/ on/ shnayim,” two,” eser, “ten,” (card u’b’hem, “and/ “foundations,” (n but/ so/ or in/ with by/ them,” (prep, (prep, pronom 3fs) haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ktuv, “written,” ha’shemot, “the me’shnayim, “from/ of (the) two,” (prep, card eser, “ten,” (card sheluchim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those (the) sent ones, dispatched ones, apostles,” (n shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” Pa’al/Qal, n mp) ha’se, “the lamb,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.15">Then the one that spoke with me had in his hand a measuring rod of gold to measure the city, the wall and the gates.   The Scriptures: And he who spoke with me had a golden measuring rod, to measure the city, and its gates, and its wall.  Aramaic: And he that talked with me, had a measure, a golden reed; so that he could measure the city, and its gates, and its wall. ve’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or this,” (pron, she’diber, “that/ imi, “with me,” (prep, 1s pronom) haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, be’yado, “in/ with/ by his/its hand,” (prep, n fs, 3ms kana, “reed, stalk, bone, measuring echad one, “after,” which/ who/ whom he/it spoke,” (v. Pi’el, qatal, past, shel, “to, for, of, belonging to,” zahav, “gold,” (n k’dei, “be able, l’midot, “to/ for/ belonging to/ (the) measures,” (prep, bo, “in/ with/ by ha'ir, “the city,” (n v’ha’choma, “and/ according to, as, in him/it,” (prep, 3ms but/ so/ or (the) order to,” (conj) v’ha’sha’arim, “and/ but/ so/ or the gates,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.16">Then the city was laid out on four sides, its length the same as its width. He measured the city with the measuring-rod as twelve thousand graves567 of the field, with the city’s length, width and height all equal.  The Scriptures: And the city lies four-cornered, and its length is as great as its breadth. And he measured the city with the rod: twelve thousand stadia – the length, and the breadth, and height of it are equal.  Aramaic: And the city stood up four square; and its length was the same as its breadth. And he measured the city with the reed, to twelve furlongs of twelve thousand; and the length and the breadth and the height of it were [all] equal. v'ha'ir, “and/ but/ so/ or the city (n fs) monach, “I/ you be'rovat, in/ of (the) four sides,” (n ms) v'ar'kah, “and/ but/ so/ or long,” (adj k’rabah, “like/ as a wide-open space, u'madad, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it measured,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, a'ir, “the city,” (n placed, laid out” (v. Hif’il, pssv part, im, “with,” (prep) ha'kaneh, “the shenayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card elef, “thousand,” k'varot, “graves, measuring-rod,” (n sepulchers,” (n v'arkah, “and/ but/ v'rachbah, “and/ but/ so/ or her/its width,” (n ms, 3fs v'gavoha, “and/ but/ so/ or high, m'ha'ir, “from/ of the city,” (prep, n he’mah, “these, those,” (3mp, shaviym, “we/ you length, duration (n ms, 3fs pronom) Pa’al/Qal, act part, <note type="footnote" n="567">This appears to be a standard of measurement. Graves and sepulchers probably were made all the same length and became a standard measurement of length.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.17">And its walls were one hundred forty and four cubits like the measurement of a man that was to a messenger.  The Scriptures: And he measured its wall: hundred and forty-four forearms, according to the measure of a man, that is, of a messenger.  Aramaic: And he measured its wall, a hundred and forty and four measures of the cubits of a man, that is, of the angel. ve’chomoteha, “and/ but/ so/ or her/its walls,” (n mp, 3fs pronom) hayu, “they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, me’a, “a hundred,” v’arba, “and/ but/ so/ or four,” (card v’arba’im, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) fourty,” (n mp) amot, “cubits,” (n kemidot, “like/ as (the) measures,” she' haya, “that/ le’ha’mal'ak, “to/ for/ belonging to mankind” (n ms) which/ who/ whom part, v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.18">The wall was jasper, and the city was pure gold.  The Scriptures: And the structure of its wall was jasper. And the city was clean gold, like clear glass. haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, m’yashfe, “jasper,” v’ha’ir, “and/ but/ so/ or the city,” (n m’zahav, “from/ of (the) gold,” (prep, n ms) “and/ but/ so/ or the</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.19">The foundation of the wall and the city was adorned with precious stones. The first foundation was jasper, the second sapphire, the third, chalcedony,568 the fourth emerald,  The Scriptures: And the foundations of the wall of the city were adorned with all kinds of precious stones: the first foundation jasper, the second sapphire, the third agate, the fourth emerald,  Aramaic: And the foundations of the wall of the city were adorned with every precious stone. The first foundation, a jasper; the second, a sapphire; the third, a chalcedony; the fourth, an emerald; v’ ha’yesod, “and/ m'ha’chochmah, “from/ of the wall u’m'ha'ir, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of the city, town (prep, n hayu, “they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, mekushat, “I/ you b’avnim, “in/ with/ by (the) stones,” foundation,” (n ms) adorned,” (v. Pi’el, ha’sod, “and/ but/ haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, yashfe, “Jasper,” echat, “one,” (card sapir, “saphire,” (n first,” (n ms, 2ms second,” (adj ms) foundation,” (n v’ha’shli’shi, “and/ b’lo’ez, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by v’revi’i, “and/ but/ so/ or the fourth,” nofekh, “emerald,” “chalcedony,” (n third,” (ord num) tongue,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.20">the fifth ruby, the sixth onyx, the seventh amethyst, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, tenth agate, the eleventh opal, and the twelfth, called in a foreign tongue, amethyst.  The Scriptures: the fifth sardonyx, the sixth ruby, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and the twelfth amethyst.  Aramaic: the fifth, a sardonyx; the sixth, a sardius; the seventh, a chrysolite; the eighth, a beryl; the ninth, a topaz; the tenth, a chrysoprasus; the eleventh, a jacinth; the twelfth, an amethyst. odem, “ruby,” (n ve’ ha’ shisi, “and/ sho’ham, “onyx,” ve’she’vi’i, “and/ ve’ha’shemini, “and/ but/ so/ or the eighth,” (ord “and/ but/ so/ or the “amethyst,” (n fs) fifth,” (ord num) sixth,” (ord num) tarshish, “beryl, ve’ha’shavi’i, “and/ but/ so/ or the ninth,” (ord pit’dah, “topaz,” (n ve’ha’asiri, “and/ shevo, “agate,” (n ve’ha’echad, “and/ eser, “ten,” (card aquamarine, topaz, chrysolite,” (n ms) tenth,” (ord num) one,” (card num) leshem, “opal, or jacinth,” (n ms) ve’ha’shnayim, “and/ but/ so/ or two,” (card num) eser, “ten,” (card nikra, “he/it was called,” (v. Nif’al, qatal, past, 3ms) b’lo’ez, “in/ with/ by (the) foreign tongue,” (prep, n “amethyst,” (n ms) Note: transliterated</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.21">The twelve gates were pearls, and each gate was of one pearl. The streets of the city were of unalloyed gold, like a clear plate.  The Scriptures:  And the twelve gates were twelve pearls – each one of the gates was a single pearl. And the street of the city was clean gold, like transparent glass.  Aramaic: And the twelve gates [were] twelve pearls; each [pearl] one gate, and each [gate] one pearl: and the broad street of the city was pure gold, like brilliant glass. ve’ha’shnayim, eser, “ten,” (card sha’ar’im, “gates,” hayu, “they were,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, min, “from, of, than,” (prep) margalit, “gems, jewels, or pearls,” v' kol, “and/ but/ so/ or all,” (n ms) “and/ but/ so/ or the two,” (card num) sha’ar, “gate,” (n echad,”one,” (card haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, m’margalit, “from/ echad,”one,” (card ha'ir, “the city,” (n “streets of…” (n jewels, or pearls,” hayu, “they were,” me’zahav, “from/ ke’tsaleach, “like/ zach, “clear, pure,” qatal, past, 3mp) prosperous,” (prep, unadulterated,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.22">But I saw no house of prayer there because Yehovah of Armies was the dwelling place571 for them and the Lamb.572  The Scriptures: And I saw no Dwelling Place in it, for הוהי Ěl Shaddai is its Dwelling Place, and the Lamb.  Aramaic: And the twelve gates [were] twelve pearls; each [pearl] one gate, and each [gate] one pearl: and the broad street of the city was pure gold, like brilliant glass. ve' lo, “and/ but/ ra’iti, “I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, ba, “in/ with/ on/ bayt, “house,” (n (prep, pronom 3fs) tzva’ot, “hosts, armies,” (n mp) haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, Ibayt, “house,” (n ha’mikdash, “the dwelling place,” (n she’lahem, “that/ which/ who/ whom ve’ha’se, “and/ but/ so/ or the lamb,” (n ms) to them,” (pron</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.23">So, the city had no need of light from the sun or the moon because the glory of Yehovah was their light, and there was the light of the Lamb.  The Scriptures: And the city had no need of the sun, nor of the moon, to shine in it, for the esteem of Elohim lightened it, and the Lamb is its lamp.  Aramaic: And the city hath no need of the sun or of the moon, to enlighten it; for the glory of God enlighteneth it, and the Lamb is the lamps of it. v' “and/ but/ so/ or, 'no/not,” (neg part) ha'ir, “the city,” (n or, “light,” (n ms)  me’shemesh, o’, “or,” (conj) m’ha’yareach, “from/ of the should, must,” (adj “from/ of the sun,” moon,” (prep, n tif’eret, “glory, Yehovah m’or,” from/ of l’hem, “to /for/ belonging to v’orah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) light,” splendour, beauty, magnificence,” (n (the) light,” (prep, there exists,” (part) them,” (prep, 3mp ha’se, “the lamb,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.24">And the holy people walk in this light and the kings of the earth bring their wealth to it.  The Scriptures: And the nations, of those who are saved, shall walk in its light, and the sovereigns of the earth bring their esteem into it.  Aramaic: And the nations that were saved, shall walk by means of its light, and the kings of the earth will bring their glory and the wealth of the nations into it. am, “and/ but/ so/ holakim, “the we/ you (mp)/ they, those who walk, go,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, b’or, “in/ with/ by/ (the) light,” (prep, ha’zeh, “the this, that” (pron ms) u’meha’lek, “and/ or the peoples, nations, (n mp) “holiness,” (adj ms) but/ so/ or (the) kings of,” (n ms ya’vo’u, “they will ba, “in/ with/ on/ wealth, goods,” (n mp, 3mp pronom) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (prep, pronom 3fs)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.25">The gates were always open day and night and not closed, for there is no night.  The Scriptures: And its gates shall not be shut at all by day, for night shall not be there.  Aramaic: And its gates shall not be shut by day; for there is no night there. u’patchu, “and/ but/ she'arecha, “gates,” (n fp, 2ms pronom) tamid, “continually, yomam, “by day,” ve’ laylah, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) night,” (n ms) lo, “no/ not” (neg yisgeru, “they will be closed, shut,” so/ or they were opened, unlocked,” (v. Pi’el, qatal, pssv (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol fut, 3mp) lo, “no/ not” (neg yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, laylah, “night,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.26">Translation #1:573  Then they came in with glory and honor of the peoples.  Translation #2: And what glory and honor will come in574 of the peoples!  The Scriptures: And they shall bring the esteem and the appreciation of the nations into it.  Aramaic: And they will bring the glory and honor of the nations into it. ve' he’ma, “and/ but/ so/ or they, ya’vo’u, “they will ba, “in/ with/ on/ tif’eret, “glory, splendor, beauty, magnificence,” (n ve’k’vod, “and/ but/ so/ or like/ as (the) honor,” (prep, these, those,” (3mp Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (prep, pronom 3fs) peoples, nations,”</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.21.27">And no strange thing will come near it; only those whose name is written in the Scroll of Life.  The Scriptures: And there shall by no means enter into it whatever is unclean, neither anyone doing abomination and falsehood, but only those who are written in the Lamb’s Book of Life.  Aramaic: And there shall not enter it, any thing polluted, or that practiseth impurity and falsehood; but they who are registered in the Lamb's book of life. ve’zar, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) alien, foreign, strange,” lo, “no/ not” (neg yikrav, “he/it will come near,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, alayv, “to him/ it,” rak, “only, just,” alayv, “to him/ it,” she'katuv, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it is Pa’al/Qal, pssv Idiom: “in the book of life” shemam, “their name,” (n ms, 3mp b’ sefer, “in/ with/ by (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, n ms) ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp) <note type="footnote" n="575">Literally, “scroll of lives,” but usually translated as “book of life.” See also Revelation 3:5 and 20:12.</note> </verse>
    </div>
    <div type="chapter" osisID="Rev.22">
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.1">Then a river was shown to me full of living waters - pure, like amethyst, coming from the throne of Yehovah and the Lamb.  The Scriptures: And he showed me a river of water of life, clear as crystal, coming from the throne of Elohim and of the Lamb.  Aramaic: And he showed me a river of living water, transparent [as] crystal, which proceeded from the throne of God and the Lamb. v’hurah, “and/ but/ nachal,” river,” echad, “one,” (card she’haya, “that/ me’mayim, “from/ of (the) waters,” so/ or he/it was belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) which/ who/ whom he/it was,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, complete,” (adj shown,” (v. Hif’il, qatal, past, 3ms) chayim, “living,” ve’zakh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) clear, k’achlamah, “like/ as (the), precious stone, amethyst,” yotzeh, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it goes out,” (Pa’al/Qal, m’kiseh, “from/ of ve’ha’se, “and/ but/ so/ or the lamb,” (n ms) chair,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.2">And in the middle of the open places and from the border of the river: and from this side and the other side - every tree is food; and upon the Tree of Life. And its twelve species of fruit on it is to be for food and its leaves will be medicine.  The Scriptures: In the middle of its street, and on either side of the river, was the tree of life, which bore twelve fruits, each tree yielding its fruit every month. And the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.  Aramaic: And in the middle of its broad avenue, and near the river, on this side and on that, [was] the tree of life; which bore twelve [sorts of] fruits yielding one of its fruits each month: and the leaves of the tree [were] for the healing of the nations. ha’echovot, “the v'al,”and/ but/ so/ ha’nachal, “the river,” (n ms) ya'ale, “he/it will rise, grow,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, which/ who/ whom middle,” (prep, n border,” (rel part, n ma' zeh,” of/ from u’m’ze, “and/ but/ so/ or on the other side,” (prep, pron, kol, “all, every” (n etz, “tree, wood,” ma’akal, “food,” ve’eytz, “and/ but/ so/ or the tree,” (n ha'chaim, “lives,” this,” (prep, ms ve’alayv, “and/ but/ so/ or upon haya, “he/it was,” (v Pa'al/Qal, qatal, shnayim, “two,” eser, “ten,” (card mini, “species,” v’haya, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it was,” him/it,” (3ms pron) (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past 3ms) l’ma’achal, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) food,” (prep, v’aleyhu, “his/its leaf, leafage,” (n ms, 3ms pronom) li‘terufah, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) fruit,” (n ms, 3ms medicine,” (prep, n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.3">For there will never again be utter destruction. And the throne of Yehovah and the Lamb will dwell in it,576 and His servants will minister to Him.577  The Scriptures: And no longer shall there be any curse, and the throne of Elohim and of the Lamb shall be in it, and His servants shall serve Him.  Aramaic: And there will be no blight any more: and the throne of God and the Lamb will be in it; and his servants will minister to him. v’cheyrem, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) utter destruction, lo, “no/ not,” (neg yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, v’kisey, “and/ but/ v’ha’seh, “and/ but/ so/ or the lamb,” (n ms) throne,” (n ms) extermination” (n yishkon, “he/it will ba, “in/ with/ on/ v’avdav, “and/ but/ yishretehu, “they will serve, minister Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, (prep, 3fs pronom) servants,” (n mp, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp, 3ms obj) <note type="footnote" n="576">Literally, “In her,” (i.e. the city of Jerusalem). 577 There are two subjects within this verse: Yehovah and the Lamb. Therefore, according to the grammar, both the verb and the pronouns should be plural to reflect the subjects. However, in the Tanakh, the rule of first mention is that the first verb will reflect the first subject. Yet, this grammatical structure the verb following both subjects and appears to be incorrect.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.4">And they will see His face, and His name will be written upon their foreheads.  The Scriptures: And they shall see His face, and His Name shall be upon their foreheads.  Aramaic: And they will see his face, and his name [will be] on their foreheads. v’yiru, “and/ but/ so/ or they will et, (DO marker) panav, “his/its v’shmo, “and/ but/ so/ or his/its name,” yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, katuv, “written,” be’mitzcheihem, “in/ with/ by/ on their foreheads,” face,” (n mp, 3ms see,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 3mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.5">And there never again will be the light of the sun in it580 by day nor the brightness of the moon. It will not shine for you, for Yehovah is the eternal light, and your Elohim is for your glory.  The Scriptures: And night shall be no more, and they shall have no need of a lamp or the light of the sun, because הוהי Elohim shall give them light. And they shall reign forever and eve  Aramaic: And there will be no more night; and they have no need of the light of a candle, or of the light of the sun; because the Lord God giveth them light: and they will reign for ever and ever. v’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or no/ not,” (neg yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, bah, “in/ with/ on/ ha’shemesh, “the yomam, “by day,” (prep, 3fs pronom) v’l’nogah, "and/ but/ so/ or to/ for/ belonging to (the) brightness,” (prep, ve’ ha’yareach, ”and/ but/ so/ or (the) moon,” (n lo, “no/ not,” (neg ya’ir, “he/it will shine,” (v Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) belonging to you,” (prep, 2ms pronom) “he/it was,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, belonging to you,” Yehovah lohr, “to/ for/ olam, “forever, eternal” (n ms) v’elohecha, “and/ but/ so/ or your God(s),” (n mp, 2mp pronom) l’tif’ar’teych, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) light,” (prep, n ms) belonging to your (mp) glory,” (prep, n fs, 3mp pronom) <note type="footnote" n="578">See Zachariah 14:11. 579 This word is used for the priests who minister to Yehovah in the Temple.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.6">Then He said to me, “These words are truth: Yehovah of Armies sent His messengers to show His servants what will soon be.”  The Scriptures: And he said to me, “These words are trustworthy and true. And הוהי Elohim of the set-apart prophets has sent His messenger to show His servants what has to take place with speed.  Aramaic: And he said to me: These words [are] faithful and true. And the Lord God of the spirit of the prophets, hath sent me, his angel, to show unto his servants the things that must soon occur. v’amar, “and/ so/ but/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, eleh, “these,” (3ms, hen, “they,” (3mp emet, “truth,” (n fs) v’Yehovah, “and/ belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) “matters, words, things,” (n mp) Yehovah,” (name) tzva’ot, “hosts, armies,” (n mp) et, (DO marker) melakayv, “his/its messengers,” (n ms, 3mp pronom) la’avadayv, “to/ belonging to/ for his/its servants,” (prep, n mp, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, qatal, demonstrate,” (v. Nif’al, inf constr) she’yihye, “that/ bekarov, “soon, shortly,” (adv) ‘ which/ who/ whom he/it will be,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, <note type="footnote" n="580">Literally, “On her,” (i.e. Jerusalem).</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.7">See, I come in haste! Holy is he who believes in the words of the prophecy, what is written in this scroll.   The Scriptures: “See, I am coming speedily! Blessed is he who guards the words of the prophecy of this book.”  Aramaic: And, lo, I come quickly: Blessed is he that keepeth the words of the prophecy of this book. re'ei, “behold! see!” (v. Pa'al/Qal, imp, ani, “I,” (1cs pron) ba, “I/ you (ms)/ he/it come(s),” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, b’mahara, “quickly, v’kadosh, “and/ but/ so/ or (the) holy,” (adj ms) hu, “he/it,” (3ms, mi, “who?” (inter speedily, hastily” she'meamin, “that/ which/ who/ whom I/ you (ms)/ he/it believe(s),” (rel part, v. Hif’il, act ha' nevi’ut,” the prophecy,” (n fs) she'katuv, “that/ b'sefer, “in/ with/ haze, “this,” (pron which/ who/ whom written,” (rel part, words of,” (prep, n scroll, document,” <note type="footnote" n="581">See Revelation 2:5.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.8">For I, John, heard and saw all these things. And because of what I heard and saw, I fell to the earth and prayed to the messenger who showed me this.   The Scriptures: And I, Yoḥanan, saw and heard these matters. And when I heard and saw, I fell down to worship before the feet of the messenger who showed me these matters.  Aramaic: And more-over I am John, the hearer and the seer of these things. And when I heard and saw, I fell down to worship at the feet of the angel who showed me these things. v' ani, “and/ so, but/ or I,” (1cs ye’annos, John, shamati, “I heard,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ve’ra’iti, “and/ but/ kol, “all,” (n ms) eleh, “these,” (3mp so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, but/ so/ or because, as soon as, when,” Note: transliterated ve’raiti, “and/ but/ so/ or I saw,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, zot, “this,” (pron, nafalti, “I fell,” (v. l'arets, “to/ for/ v’hitpalalti,, “and/ le’ha’mal'akh “to/ for/ belonging to “that/ which/ who/ Pa'al/Qal, qatal, belonging to (the) whom I heard,” earth,” (prep, n Pa'al/Qal, qatal, she'herah, “that/ zot, “this,” (pron, which/ who/ whom he/it showed,” (v. Hif’il qatal, past, belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.9">And he said to me, “See! Don’t do this!” I am also from your friends and of your company of brothers, the prophets and of those fulfilling the words of this scroll. Make your prayer to Yehovah!"  The Scriptures: And he said to me, “See, do not! For I am your fellow servant, and of your brothers the prophets, and of those who are guarding the words of this book. Worship Elohim.”  Aramaic: And he said to me: See, [thou do it] not: I am thy fellow-servant, and of thy brethren the prophets, and of them that observe the words of this book. Worship God. v' hu, “and/ but/ so/ amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa'al/Qal, qatal, re'ei, “see!” (v. al, “don’t,” (part) ta’a’seh, “you will do,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2ms) zot, “this,” (pron, belonging to me,” (prep, 1cs pron) Pa'al/Qal, imp, ms) gam, “again, also, too, in addition, even, as well,” ani, “I,” (1cs pron) m' chaverot, “of/ u’machim, “from/ of (the) brothers,” ha’nevi’im, “the prophets,” (n mp) u’me’eilu, “and/ but/ so/ or from/ of friends,” (prep, n mp, 2ms pronom) following,” (prep, h’mekayemim, “we/ you (mp)/ they, those are had'varim, “the words,” (n mp) m'sefer, “from/ of (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, n haze, “this,” (pron a’sei, “we/ you (mp)/ they do, tfilatcha, “your prayer,” (n ms, 2ms pronom) la’Yehovah,” to/ for/ belonging to Yehovah,” (prep, fulfilled, establish,” (v. Pi’el, pssv part, Pa’al/Qal, act part,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.10">Then he said to me, “Do not seal the vision of this scroll because the time is near.”  The Scriptures: And he said to me, “Do not seal the words of the prophecy of this book, because the time is near.  Aramaic: And he said to me: Seal not the words of the prophecy of this book; for the time is near. v’amar, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, al, “don’t,” (part) tistom, “you will ha’chazon, “the vision, dream, m’sefer, “from/ of (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, haze, “this,” (pron belonging to me,” seal,” (v, Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, fut, 2ms) prophecy,” (n ms) ha’et, “the time,” karov, “near,” (adj <note type="footnote" n="582">See Midrash of Philio 17:17:14 for unique spelling, dating c. 10 CE to 50 CE.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.11">“Those who are evil will be for all time. Yes, those who are impure will also be the same way. However, those who are faithful will continue to be so for all time.  And whoever is holy is also like this. Truly, like this.”  The Scriptures: “He who does wrong, let him do more wrong; he who is filthy, let him be more filthy; he who is righteous, let him be more righteous; he who is set-apart, let him be more set-apart.  Aramaic: He that doth evil, let him do evil still; and he that is filthy, let him be filthy still; and he that is righteous, let him practise righteousness still; and he that is sanctified, let him be sanctified still. mi, “who?” (inter she’yesh, “that/ ti’ha’yeh, “she/it kol, “all,” (n ms) et, “time,” (n fs) ken, “yes, truth,” which/ who/ whom wickedness,” (adj Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, exists,” (rel part, u' mi, “and/ but/ she’yesh, “that/ yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this which/ who/ whom Idiom: “too, also” exists,” (rel part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, gam, “again, also, too, in addition, even, ken, “yes, truth,” (conj) kol, “all,” (n ms) et, “time,” (n fs) aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however,’’ (adv) sheyesh, “who” chasid, “devout, faithful, pious, observant,” (adj yihye, “he/it will be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, “there is, there are” yiqtol, fut, ms) kach, “so, thus, therefore, in this u'mi,”and/ but/ so/ she’yesh, “which/ that/ who/ whom kadosh, “holy/, set apart, sanctified, gam, “also, too, in addition,” (part) ken, “yes, truth,” k’mo, “like, as, consecrated,” (adj ze,” this,” (pron,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.12">“See, I come in haste to pay every man according to his works!”  The Scriptures: “And see, I am coming speedily, and My reward is with Me, to give to each according to his work.  Aramaic: Behold, I come quickly; and my reward is with me, to recompense every one according to his work. v’ r’eh, “and/ but/ ani, “I,” (pron 1cs) yavo,” he/it will b’ma’hara, “in/ with/ by (the) leshilem, “to pay or repay,” ‘(v, Pi’el, ish, “man,” (n ms) belonging to (the) all, every” (prep, n Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, quickly, speedily, ke’ma’asehu, “like/ as his/its deeds, works,” (prep, n ms, 3ms <note type="footnote" n="583">See Revelation 2:5.</note> </verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.13">“I am the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End.”  The Scriptures: “I am the ‘Aleph’ and the ‘Taw’, the Beginning and the End, the First and the Last.  Aramaic: I am Alpha and Omega, the First and the Last, the Commencement and the Completion. ani, ‘I’ (pron 1cs) ha' rishon,”the first,” (n ms) v'ha’acharon, “and/ but/ so/ or the last,” v' ha' sof, “and/ but/ so/ or the end,” (n “beginning,” (n ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.14">“Holy are they who do His commandments so that they will have a part in the tree of life. Pure, he will walk into the city.”  The Scriptures: “Blessed are those doing His commands, so that the authority shall be theirs unto the tree of life, and to enter through the gates into the city.  Aramaic: Blessed are they who do his commandments, that they may have a right to the tree of life, and may enter through the gates into the city. kedoshim, “holy, hem, “they,” (pron she’osim, “that/ mitsvav, “his/its commandments,” k’dei, “so, be able, according to, as, in she’yihye, “that/ l’hem, “to /for/ belonging to saint, sacred, hallowed,” (adj which/ who/ whom they, those who do, which/ who/ whom order to,” (conj) he/it will be” (v. Pa'al/Qal, yiqtol, them,” (prep, 3mp Pa’al/Qal, act part, chelek, “portion, b’etz, “in/ with/ by ha’ chaim, “the lives,” (n mp) v’yezakeh, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it m’ha’ir, “from/ of (the) city,” (prep, n (the) tree, wood (material), (prep, n will win,” (v. Pi’el, yiqtol, fut, 3ms)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.15">“For outside stands the dog, the sorcerers, the harlots, the murderers, and the deceivers.”  The Scriptures: “But outside are the dogs and those who enchant with drugs, and those who whore, and the murderers, and the idolaters, and all who love and do falsehood.  Aramaic: Without [will be] dogs, and sorcerers, and whoremongers, and manslayers, and idolaters, and every one that loveth and doeth falsehood. m’vachutz, “from/ of (the) outside,” omdim, “we/ you v’ha’mechashfim, “and/ but/ so/ or the sorcerers,” (n mp) v’hazonot, “and/ but/ so/ or we/ you v’ha’rotzghchnim, “and/ but/ so or the murderers,” (n mp) (fp)/ they, those who whore,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, act part, Pa’al/Qal, act part, v’ha’kazvanim, “and/ but/ so/ or the deceivers,” (n</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.16">“I, Yeshua, I sent messengers to show the congregation. I am the root of the tribes of David.”  The Scriptures: “I, עשוהי, have sent My messenger to witness to you these matters in the assemblies. I am the Root and the Offspring of Dawiḏ, the Bright and Morning Star.”  Aramaic: I Jesus have sent my angel, to testify to you these things before the churches. I am the root and offspring of David: like the splendid star of the morning. ani,” I,” (pron 1cs) Yeshua, (name) shelachti, “I sent,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, malachai, “angels, messengers of,” (n l’edah, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) show,” (HIf’il, inf assembly,” (prep, shoresh, “root,” (n m’mishpachot, “of/ from (the) families, tribes, clans,” (prep, n David, (name)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.17">“And the Spirit and the bride say, ‘Come!’  For whoever hears, says, ‘Come!’  And whoever thirsts, go to the living water and drink without silver and without price.  The Scriptures: And the Spirit and the bride say, “Come!” And he who hears, let him say, “Come!” And he who thirsts, come! And he who desires it, take the water of life without paying!  Aramaic: And the Spirit and the bride say, Come thou. And let him that heareth, say, Come thou. And let him who thirsteth, come; and he that is inclined, let him take the living water gratis. ve’ha’ruach, “and/ v’kalah, “and/ but/ so /or (the) bride,” amru, “they said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, u'mi, “and/ but/ so/ or who,” (interog she’shema, “that/ which/ who/ whom but/ so/ or (the) spirit, breath,” (n Pa’al/Qal, imp, he/it heard,” (rel part, v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, past, 3ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, 'mi, ”and/ but/ so/ or who,” (interog she’zame, “that/ l’chu, “(to men) go! (v. Pal/Qal, l’mayim, “to/ for/ belonging to (the) water(s),” (prep, n chayim, “we/ you mp)/ they, those who live,” (v. v’shtu, “and/ but/ which/ who/ whom Pa’al/Qal, imp, part, v. Pa’al/Qal, Pa’al/Qal, act part, b’lo, “in/ with/ by/ kesef, “silver, money,” (n ms) u’b’lo, “and/ but/ so/ or in/ with/ by no, not, without,” (prep, neg part) mechir, “price,” (n without,” (prep,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.18">“However, I testify to all the hearers of the prophecy of this scroll: anyone who adds any words584 to it, Yehovah will add to him the plagues written within this scroll.”   The Scriptures: For I witness to everyone hearing the words of the prophecy of this book: If anyone adds to them, Elohim shall add to him the plagues that are written in this book,  Aramaic: I testify to every one that heareth the words of the prophecy of this book, that if any one shall add to them, God will add to him the plagues that are written in this book. aval, “indeed, truly, verily, surely, but however, howbeit, contrariwise, nay ani, “I,” (1cs pron) me’id, “I/ you (ms) ha’shomim, “we/ you (mp)/ they ha' nevi’ut,” the prophecy,” (n fs) m’ha’sefer, “from/ of the book, scroll, document,” (prep, he/it testify,” (v. Hif’il act part, ms) belonging to (the) all,” (prep, n ms) Pa’al/Qal, act part, haze, “the this, that” (pron ms) u’ba, “and/ but/ so/ or he/it came,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, she'echad, “that/ yosif, “he/it will add,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) devarim, “words, things, matters,” (n which/ who/ whom him/it,” (prep, 3ms yosif, “he/it will add,” (v. Hif’il, yiqtol, fut, 3ms) alayv, “on/ upon/ ha’nega’im, “the strokes, plagues, diseases, marks, she’ketuvim, “that/ which/ who/ whom written,” (rel part, b' sefer, “in (the) haze, “the this, that,” (pron ms) him/it,” (prep, 3ms plague spots, mark of leprosy,” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.19">“And if one removes585 any words586 from this scroll, Yehovah will erase his name from the Scroll of Life.”  The Scriptures: and if anyone takes away from the words of the book of this prophecy, Elohim shall take away his part from the Book of Life, and out of the set-apart city, which are written in this Book.  Aramaic: And if any one shall take away from the words of the book of this prophecy, God will take away his portion from the tree of life, and from the holy city, which are described in this book. u’vim, “and/ but/ so/ or by if, when, whether,” (prep, she'echad, “that/ yigra, “he/it will reduce, to remove, eize, ‘‘any,” (pron, devarim, “words, things, matters,” (n ma' zeh,”of/ from this,” (prep, pron, m' sefer, “from/ (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, which/ who/ whom one,” (rel part, card Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, Idiom: “from the book of life” yimche, “he/it will erase, obliterate,” et, (DO marker) shmo, “his/its name,” (n ms, 3ms m’ sefer, “in/ with/ by (the) book, scroll, document,” (prep, n ms) yiqtol, fut, 3ms) ha’ chayim, “of life, lives” (n mp)</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.20">“And thus says this witness to this, ‘Truely, I will come in haste!’ “Amen. Yes, come Master Yeshua!”  The Scriptures: He that bears witness of these matters says, “Yes, I am coming speedily.” Amĕn. Yes, come, Master עשוהי!  Aramaic: He who testifieth these things, saith: Yes, I come quickly. Amen. Come, Lord Jesus! v’ko, “and/ but/ so/ amar, “he/it said,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, qatal, ha’ed, “the witness, zot, “this,” (pron, ken, “yes, truth,” ani,” I,” (pron 1cs) ava, “that I will or thus, to such extent,” (adv) testifier,” (n ms) Pa’al/Qal, yiqtol, b’ma’hara, “in / with/ by (the) amen, “Amen,” ken, “yes, truth,” Yeshua, (name) master,” (n ms) quickly, speedily, Pa’al/Qal, imp,</verse>
      <verse osisID="Rev.22.21">May the grace of our Master Yeshua, the Messiah, be with all of you. Amen!  The Scriptures: The favour of our Master עשוהי Messiah be with the set-apart ones. Amĕn.  Aramaic: The grace of our Lord Jesus the Messiah, [be] with all the saints. Amen. ha’chased, “the m’adoneinu, “from/ Yeshua, (name) ha’mashiach, “the Messiah,” (n ms) im, “with,” (prep) kolkem, “all of grace, kindness,” (n will/let it be,” (v. Pa’al/Qal, jssv, fut, you (mp),” (n ms, master,” (prep n ms, 1cp pronom) amen, “Amen,” <note type="footnote" n="587">Literally, “scroll of lives,” but usually translated as “book of life.” Although this phrase is not found in the Tanakh, it dates from Second Temple. 588 See Revelation 2:5.</note> </verse>
    </div>
